    "chunk_text": "The Ambassador noted that this development will also help to bring both nations closer together, facilitate business exchanges, strengthen tourism cooperation, and deepen the friendship that Vietnam and Sri Lanka have built over more than 55 years of diplomatic relations.\n\nThe momentum from the Vietnamese market is already evident. While the island nation welcomed just over 3,000 Vietnamese visitors in 2025, the first six months of 2026 alone have already recorded more than 4,000 arrivals from Vietnam.\n\n\u201cSri Lanka is a new destination for Vietnamese visitors,\u201d the Ambassador noted, reflecting on her own recent experiences traveling the island. \u201cThis is the first time for me to be in Sri Lanka... But this is like a hidden beauty, I think that, a hidden gem, hidden beauty in the Indian Ocean.\u201d She expressed deep confidence that Vietnamese travelers will quickly fall in love with Sri Lanka\u2019s unique blend of pristine golden beaches, magnificent wildlife, tea plantations, and the profound warmth of its people.\n\nConversely, Vietnam has also become an increasingly attractive destination for Sri Lankan outbound travelers. In 2025, Vietnam welcomed a historic 22 million international global visitors, which included over 14,000 Sri Lankan travelers. The Ambassador pointed out Vietnam\u2019s reciprocal appeal, highlighting the country\u2019s natural landscapes, vibrant cities, rich cultural heritage, renowned cuisine, and most importantly, its hospitality and friendliness."
