    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "07f1401fb9305803e035907c75f3fa86",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1608,
    "chunk_text": "The forum is the latest in the Council\u2019s ongoing program of initiatives to deepen bilateral commercial ties, undertaken in collaboration with the US Embassy in Colombo. The session has been deliberately designed for a wide cross-section of the business community, not only legal practitioners and large corporates, but SMEs, exporters, manufacturers, technology and creative businesses, and entrepreneurs. It will move beyond legal theory to the practical questions businesses actually confront: how to register and defend a brand; what recourse is available when counterfeits surface in the market or at the border; what US buyers and investors expect of IP compliance; and how stronger IP protection translates into greater orders, investment and market access for Sri Lanka.\n\nSLUSABC President Tilak Gunawardana said: \u201cAs Sri Lanka positions itself to attract greater U.S. investment and expand its exports of goods and services, demonstrating a credible, well-enforced IP regime is no longer optional \u2013 it is fundamental. We have brought the regulator, the enforcement agencies, industry and the legal profession to one table, to discuss not theory, but practice: what businesses actually face, and what can be done better.\u201d\n\nThe forum is open to exporters, importers, manufacturers, professionals in the technology and creative industries, legal practitioners, and all businesses engaged in or aspiring to trade with the United States.\n\nRegistrations may be made via https://event.chamber.lk/Details/Event/487 or by contacting the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce on 011 5588801 or [email\u00a0protected]."
