    "md5": "5750d36340a1b72bc036571074668e88",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1628,
    "chunk_text": "Trust, reputation and leadership to take centre stage at Sri Lanka Corporate Director Summit 2026\n\nIn an era where a single social media post can erode decades of brand equity, stakeholder expectations continue to evolve, and talent, culture and corporate purpose increasingly determine long-term business success, the responsibilities of corporate boards have never been greater. Today\u2019s directors must navigate uncertainty, oversee emerging risks, safeguard reputation, inspire stakeholder confidence and create sustainable value in an increasingly complex and interconnected world.\n\nAgainst this backdrop, the Sri Lanka Institute of Directors (SLID) will host the Sri Lanka Corporate Director Summit 2026 on 22 July at Cinnamon Grand Colombo under the theme, \u201cFuture-Ready Sri Lankan Directors: From Compliance to Sustainable Growth.\u201d Bringing together internationally respected business leaders, governance experts and industry practitioners, the Summit will examine the issues reshaping boardrooms and redefining corporate leadership through keynote addresses, panel discussions and executive conversations.\n\nA key highlight of the program will be the keynote address by AP Moller Maersk Head of Public Policy and Regulatory Affairs (India, Bangladesh and Sri Lanka) and Maersk Bharat IFSCA Ltd. Director Vivek Sharma. In his address, \u201cThe New Reputation Risk Landscape \u2013 Social Media, Activism, Cyber Incidents and the Board\u2019s Oversight Responsibility,\u201d he will explore how boards can strengthen governance and oversight as organisations face unprecedented public scrutiny in an increasingly connected world."
  },
