    "chunk_text": "A key highlight of the program will be the keynote address by AP Moller Maersk Head of Public Policy and Regulatory Affairs (India, Bangladesh and Sri Lanka) and Maersk Bharat IFSCA Ltd. Director Vivek Sharma. In his address, \u201cThe New Reputation Risk Landscape \u2013 Social Media, Activism, Cyber Incidents and the Board\u2019s Oversight Responsibility,\u201d he will explore how boards can strengthen governance and oversight as organisations face unprecedented public scrutiny in an increasingly connected world.\n\nLeadership, governance and long-term value creation will also take centre stage during an exclusive Fireside Chat featuring Unilever Sri Lanka Chairman and CEO and Regional Head for Unilever\u2019s businesses in Sri Lanka, Myanmar, Cambodia and Laos Ali Tariq; Galle Face Hotel Group Chairman Sanjeev Gardiner; and Commercial Bank of Ceylon PLC Chairman Sharhan Muhseen.\n\nRepresenting three of Sri Lanka\u2019s top corporate leaders, they will reflect on leading organisations through periods of disruption, driving transformation and making strategic decisions that create enduring value. Muhseen brings more than 25 years of regional and international investment banking experience, having held senior leadership positions at JPMorgan, Merrill Lynch and Credit Suisse, he was the Joint Awardee of the Sri Lanka Institute of Directors \u2018Most Outstanding Independent Director Award in 2025. Together, the three leaders will offer delegates candid perspectives on leadership, resilience, governance and the boardroom decisions that shape successful organisations."
  },
