    "chunk_text": "Meanwhile, former President Maithripala Sirisena described Wickremaratne\u2019s death at the age of 63 as an even greater loss, saying a person at that age is at the peak of intelligence, maturity and ability to serve society.\n\nHe recalled that Wickramaratne had been appointed as Inspector General of Police during his tenure as President.\n\nSirisena described the late former IGP as an honest, virtuous and humble individual who performed his duties with a calm and composed mind.\n\nHe said that despite the pressures and divisions often created by political leaders, Wickramaratne had the ability to navigate difficult situations without creating enemies. He also praised him for maintaining his composure during turbulent periods, including the mass protests known as the Aragalaya.\n\nRecalling their most recent meeting, Sirisena said he had met Wickramaratne around two or three weeks ago along with their mutual friend, Ranga Kalansooriya. They had spent several hours talking and joking together.\n\nSirisena said Wickramaratne had expressed his intention to visit his home for a casual discussion on religion, society and international affairs, while avoiding political matters.\n\nSirisena said the country had lost an exemplary public servant, describing Wickramaratne as an outstanding example not only to the Police Department but to the entire public service."
