    "md5": "6534855f1c5e86d92c77ea8d1d19b9ad",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1336,
    "chunk_text": "Andy Burnham becomes UK prime minister after meeting King Charles\n\nSupport the Guardian - Andy Burnham has formally become the UK prime minister after meeting King Charles at Buckingham Palace, the fourth person to hold the role in less than four years and the sixth within a decade.\n\nBurnham, who took over from Keir Starmer as leader of the Labour party on Friday, accepted the appointment as prime minister shortly after Starmer had gone to the palace to resign to the monarch.\n\nThe former Greater Manchester mayor, who only returned to parliament a month ago, headed to Downing Street, where he spoke to the assembled media before announcing his cabinet.\n\nBurnham returned to parliament in a byelection staged by his allies with the explicit purpose of replacing Starmer, after the incumbent prime minister lost the support of many Labour MPs and a number of his ministers after a seres of political mishaps and U-turns.\n\nWith no one else in the party competing to become leader, Burnham has been made prime minister without any contest and with limited scrutiny.\n\nWhile the same happened for Rishi Sunak in 2022, he had fought a contest against Liz Truss weeks earlier and had very recent cabinet experience.\n\nWhile Burnham has been an MP and cabinet minister before, he left parliament in 2017 to take the Greater Manchester role."
