    "chunk_text": "Excello Developers unveils newest residential landmark \u2018Aathavan\u2019\n\nFrom left: Samira Anthony - CFO - Grafeo One; Aslam Omar - Director - Grafeo One; Subash Thavarajasingam - Founder and CEO \u2013 Excello; Kasun Project - Manager- Excello; Rajkumar Rajeevkanth - Director - Paramount Edu Global\n\nPremier boutique real estate firm Excello Developers has officially launched its newest residential landmark, Aathavan by Excello, situated at the highly accessible Carron Place in Dehiwala. Starting from Rs. 38million, this eco-conscious development introduces a fresh standard of urban luxury featuring premium apartments designed to balance aesthetic excellence with long-term investment value.\n\n\u201cAt Excello, our design philosophy is all about \u2018Elevated Living,\u2019 which means more than just luxury looks,\u201d said Subash Thavarajasingam, Founder and CEO of Excello Developers. \u201cFor Aathavan by Excello, we spent months talking to real people to create spaces that address every day needs. By using a fully solar-powered system, we are not only helping the environment but also protecting our buyers from high maintenance fees and market volatility. Coupled with our special bank partnerships and flexible payment options, this project is about shaping responsible, human-centric environments that guarantee long-term asset value delivered on time and within budget.\u201d\n\nRising eight storeys high, Aathavan by Excello comprises 44 exclusive units engineered in a range of versatile configurations that maximise every square foot of the property. The layouts cater to diverse lifestyle needs, offering optimised two-bedroom apartments at 1,020 square feet and spacious three-bedroom residences at 1,380 square feet."
  },
