    "md5": "22d1b97ba03e91220667ccdbefc3ab51",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1976,
    "chunk_text": "Swedish envoy reaffirms plans to bring trade delegation to Sri Lanka Expo 2027\n\nThe Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB) welcomed Ambassador of Sweden to Sri Lanka Jan Thesleff for an official meeting at the EDB on July 14, 2026.\n\nThe meeting was chaired by EDB Chairman and Chief Executive Officer Mangala Wijesinghe and attended by senior EDB officials. Honorary Consul-General of Sweden in Sri Lanka Sanjay Kulatunga also participated in the discussions.\n\nDuring the meeting, Wijesinghe provided an overview of Sri Lanka\u2019s export performance, highlighting the country\u2019s key export sectors, emerging opportunities and potential areas for expanding trade with the Nordic region. Particular attention was given to Sri Lanka Expo 2027, scheduled to be held from January 14-17, 2027, in Colombo, which is expected to serve as a premier platform for connecting international buyers with Sri Lankan exporters.\n\nThesleff expressed strong interest in supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s export promotion efforts and reaffirmed Sweden\u2019s commitment to bringing a Swedish trade delegation to Sri Lanka Expo 2027. He noted that preparations are already underway to facilitate the participation of Swedish buyers and investors at the exhibition.\n\nThesleff also acknowledged Sri Lanka\u2019s reputation for producing high-quality, sustainable products that are well-positioned to meet the demands of the European and Nordic markets.\n\nThe discussions highlighted the strong export potential of several Sri Lankan sectors, including Ceylon Cinnamon, coconut and coconut-based products, gems and jewellery, apparel and information and communication technology.\n\nThesleff commended the high-quality standards maintained by Sri Lankan exporters and emphasised the growing market opportunities for these products and services in Sweden and the wider Nordic region.\n\nBoth parties reaffirmed their commitment to strengthening trade and investment relations between Sri Lanka and the Nordic countries."
  },
