    "chunk_size_bytes": 1950,
    "chunk_text": "The inaugural FIFA Peace Prize was awarded to Donald Trump in December 2025 on the grounds of his \u201cexceptional and extraordinary actions for peace\u201d and for \u201cpromoting peace and unity around the world\u201d.\n\nMuch worse, the Trump administration in the US has been actively participating in the ongoing genocide committed in Palestine\u2019s Gaza. The US under Trump provides Israel with the arms to continue its attacks on Palestinians in the Gaza. Even worse,\u00a0 through the veto the US exercises at the UN Security Council,\u00a0 it prevents even the condemnation of Israeli actions.\n\nThe controversies do not end there. The US was slammed by Iran over \u201cdiscriminatory treatment\u201d of not granting visas to some members of the Iranian national team\u2019s delegation to attend the 2026 World Cup tournament. The US also imposed strict visa conditions, such as not permitting Iranian players to remain in the US when they played matches in that country. It required them (players) to enter and leave US soil on the exact day of their matches.\n\nThe FIFA made no protest at these discriminatory moves by the US president and his administration. Football fans however, made their feeling clear. When the American leader walked out for the trophy presentation ceremony at the finals alongside FIFA\u2019s Gianni Infantino \u2013the duo were booed by the crowd.\n\nWhen FIFA trophies for individual awards such as \u2018the player of the tournament\u2019 (won by \u2018Rodri\u2019) were awarded,\u00a0 the trophy was presented by Yasir al-Rumayyan, the Governor of Saudi Arabia\u2019s Public Investment Fund. This shows how the football boss permits politics to influence the game.\n\nThe 2026 World cup tournament had a number of other shortcomings as well. Players and teams continue publicly protesting refereeing decisions. A senior member of the coaching staff of a particular country ran on to the playing field to challenge a particular decision and had to be ordered off the field."
