    "chunk_text": "Rajapakse  won the lands, but  AKD can win  people\u2019s hearts by returning them MP Mano Ganesan DPF Leader\n\nSix political parties representing Tamil speaking people have come together and formed this platform\n\nI emphasise we are not going to achieve anything until we achieve the status of Sri Lankanism\n\nThe credit for this communalism we are experiencing should go to peoples\u2019 movement or \u2018aragalaya\u2019\n\n\u201cI want to see a Sri Lanka where each of us are treated as \u2018Sri Lankans\u2019 and that thinking being upheld in this country in the political, social, economic and cultural circles in the country. But it is not so\u201d\n\nDemocratic Peoples\u2019 Front (DPF) Leader MP Mano Ganesan in an interview with the Daily Mirror said that a few political parties who represent minority communities had formed \u2018the platform\u2019 recently with the aim of focusing more on their issues. According to Ganesan, they have three concerns which are issuance of land to the owners in the North, conducting Provincial council elections and making amendments to the Constitution.\u00a0 He further said the situation in the country is better after the peoples\u2019 movement was initiated in the year 2022 where people started treating each other as Sri Lankans sans racial segregation. The Parliamentarian also said that although other countries have made progress where a person from non-numerical communities can become a President, in Sri Lanka, there us an unwritten law that the President has to be a Sinhala Buddhist.\n\n\u201cThanks to the Aragalaya, the concept of \u2018Sri Lankans\u2019 came about\u201d- MP Mano Ganesan Democratic Peoples\u2019 Front Leader\n\nQRecently 21 MPs representing minority communities formed an alliance called \u2018The Platform\u2019."
