    "chunk_text": "\"It was a source of strength for us. As such, we argued against the involvement of foreign courts,\" he said.\n\nReferring to the government's plan for the extension of the retirement age of judges, he said it had been a move widely opposed by civil society, the Sri Lanka Bar Association, academia and others.\n\nThere is uncertainty on the part of the government with regard to the issue. It takes more than one and a half years to implement such a move. They present proposals to people and various groups and gather their ideas on them. There were 1,200 responses for such a move to extend the retirement age of judges within 18 months. We don\u2019t see such a development in Sri Lanka. No one is aware of the government\u2019s move.\n\nExtension of retirement age cannot be confined to judges alone; it should be extended to others, including specialist doctors and academics. There are different ideas expressed on the issue. No idea has been expressed on one matter. It is on that matter which I am going to focus."
