    "md5": "612e210c8822f8b9f102dc2e5965fd19",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1738,
    "chunk_text": "Father seeks probe into daughter\u2019s death at Ratnapura Hospital\n\nColombo, July 21 (Daily Mirror) - The father of a 21-year-old girl who died while receiving treatment at the General Hospital in Ratnapura has called on the Health Ministry to launch an immediate and independent investigation into the circumstances surrounding her death, alleging possible medical negligence.\n\nIn a letter addressed to the Health Minister, the father requested a ministerial inquiry into the death of his daughter, who died after being admitted to Ward 13 of the General Hospital, Ratnapura.\n\nAccording to the letter, she was admitted through the hospital\u2019s Emergency Treatment Unit (ETU) on July 3 after being diagnosed with pneumonia and was later transferred to Ward 13.\n\nThe father alleged that despite repeated requests by family members, his daughter was not adequately reviewed by the treating consultant, medical officers or nursing staff. He further claimed that her complaints of severe chest pain, bleeding from the mouth, persistent diarrhoea and worsening shortness of breath were not acted upon appropriately.\n\nHe also alleged that her oxygen saturation level had dropped to 85 per cent on the day of admission and, although oxygen therapy was administered, the treating consultant was not informed promptly, and no urgent escalation of care was initiated.\n\nAccording to the complaint, the patient\u2019s condition continued to deteriorate until she suffered a cardiac arrest in the ward. She was subsequently transferred to the Intensive Care Unit (ICU), where she later died.\n\nFurthermore, father said the Judicial Medical Officer (JMO) had indicated that the provisional cause of death was pneumonia, pending histopathological examination."
