    "md5": "62daa4db0ed5d00ea7d77a967c0fa168",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1734,
    "chunk_text": "Court issues order against Sumathi Studios over Chandran Rutnam\u2019s film \u2019Rizana: A Caged Bird\u2019\n\nColombo, July 21 (Daily Mirror) - The Colombo Commercial High Court issued an Enjoining Order restraining Jagath Sumathipala and Sumathi Studios from screening, releasing, distributing, broadcasting, selling, licensing or otherwise commercially exploiting the film presently titled 'Rihanna', formerly titled 'Rizana: A Caged Bird', without the consent of its director and co-producer, Chandran Rutnam.\n\nThe order was issued by Colombo Commercial High Court Judge Amali Ranaweera following a plaint filed by Chandran Rutnam, who alleged that the defendants had, without his knowledge or authority, renamed the film, altered its content and attempted to commercially exploit the work while misrepresenting its authorship and creative credits.\n\nThe plaintiff further alleged that the defendants sought to edit, modify, reproduce, re-shoot, transfer or license rights in the film to third parties, while attributing directorial, producer and authorship credits to persons other than the plaintiff.\n\nPresident\u2019s Counsel Upul Jayasuriya, appearing for the plaintiff submitted to court that Chandran Rutnam conceived, developed, directed and co-produced the film, which represents his original creative vision and artistic expression and that the moral rights of the creator of a cinematographic work and the creator\u2019s right to be identified as its author and director is protected under the Intellectual Property Act.\n\nIt was further submitted that the unauthorised alteration and exploitation of the film constituted an infringement of the plaintiff\u2019s moral rights, copyright and related rights under the Intellectual Property Act."
  },
