    "md5": "5d3a92bcc2b69bf8c52fc9dc828bd5e8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1899,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka Brand Conclave 2026 on July 28\n\nUnites global expertise and local insights to shape future brands\n\nSri Lanka Brand Conclave 2026, which is scheduled to be held on July 28, at Cinnamon Grand, will place global brand leadership thinking at the centre of Sri Lanka\u2019s marketing landscape, bringing together internationally recognised experts, senior business leaders and marketing professionals to explore how organisations can build stronger, future-ready brands in a rapidly evolving marketplace.\n\nNational University of Singapore NUS Business School Associate Professor of Marketing and Executive MBA Academic Director Dr. Prem Shamdasani will discuss the increasing significance of purpose-driven brands and how businesses can build deep relationships with consumers.\n\nMarketing Leadership Institute CEO and The Marketing Leadership Masterclass founder Thomas Barta will explore how marketers can evolve from brand managers into leaders who contribute to the growth of their business.\n\nAleph Group Country Director for Sri Lanka and Bangladesh Md. Ehsanul Hoque will highlight new developments and trends in AI-powered marketing within Google\u2019s evolving ecosystem.\n\nThe One Club for Creativity APAC Regional Director and former BBDO Singapore Creative Chairman Tay Guan Hin will address creativity as a strategic advantage in building distinctive brands.\n\nLeaders from Prima and Spa Ceylon will participate in a panel discussion titled \u2018Disrupt to Win \u2013 Creating Brands People Love and Advocate For\u2019.\n\nSenior marketing leaders from Singer Sri Lanka and Dialog Axiata will participate in the CMO Dialogue \u2018How Brands are Leveraging the Modern Digital Ecosystem and the Evolving Skills in Demand\u2019.\n\nA Strategy to Action session will bring together industry leaders from CBL and Fonterra to discuss how organisations can convert brand strategy into measurable business outcomes."
