    "chunk_text": "Teen Academy\u2019s model draws on two established international benchmarks. In the United States, organisations such as Junior Achievement (founded in 1919) and university-run programs at Wharton, Harvard, Babson, Berkeley, Georgetown and NYU have shown that teenagers who build and pitch real ventures arrive at university and the workforce demonstrably better prepared than peers who only study business in theory.\n\nThat contribution is not incidental \u2014 it follows a deliberate policy of embedding entrepreneurship inside the school system itself. Since 2016, the Indian government\u2019s Atal Innovation Mission has established more than 10,000 Atal Tinkering Labs in schools across 722 districts, giving over 10 million students hands-on exposure to innovation, design thinking and problem-solving well before they reach university. India\u2019s founders and policymakers built that pipeline first; the start-up numbers came after."
