    "chunk_size_bytes": 1550,
    "chunk_text": "NIBM launches Best Innovative Business Model Awards 2026 to recognise Sri Lanka\u2019s most innovative organisations\n\nFrom left: NIBM BIBMA 2026 Steering Committee Chair Dr. Baratha Dewanarayana, University of Sri Jayewardenepura Postgraduate Institute of Management Director and NIBM BIBMA 2026 Advisory Committee Member Dr. Asanga Ranasinghe, NIBM Chairman Dr. Chinthake Perera, Director General and BIBMA 2026 Advisory Committee Member Dr. D.M.A. Kulasooriya, NIBM School of Business Director Kolitha Ranawaka, and Central Bank of Sri Lanka Market Operations Director and NIBM BIBMA 2026 Advisory Committee Member Dr. Anil Perera\n\nThe National Institute of Business Management (NIBM) officially launched the Best Innovative Business Model Awards (BIBMA) 2026 on 14 July, reaffirming its commitment to fostering business excellence, innovation, and sustainable economic growth in Sri Lanka.\n\nAs NIBM approaches six decades of excellence in education, research, consultancy, and industry engagement, the Institute continues to introduce initiatives that strengthen the country\u2019s business ecosystem and promote globally competitive organisations.\n\nBIBMA 2026 was introduced as a prestigious national platform dedicated to recognising organisations that have transformed the way they create, deliver, and capture value in today\u2019s rapidly evolving business environment. The awards aim to establish a national benchmark for innovative business models while encouraging organisations to embrace innovation, sustainability, and long-term competitiveness."
  },
