    "md5": "3035ae288cc23f2ee525af3edbd5412f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 895,
    "chunk_text": "Among sectors recording strong growth in June were electrical and electronic components, food and beverages, rubber and rubber-based products, spices and essential oils, seafood, mineral products and ornamental fish. ICT/BPM services also maintained steady growth during the month.\n\nDuring the January\u2013June period, electrical and electronic component exports surged by 123.48%, ICT/BPM exports rose 17.63%, while coconut-based products, food and beverages, seafood and rubber-based products also posted healthy gains. In contrast, apparel exports declined by 6.07%, tea by 5.69% and spices and essential oils by 0.10%.\n\nIndia overtook the United Kingdom to become Sri Lanka's second-largest export destination during the first half of 2026, with exports to India increasing by 36.16% year-on-year. Exports to China also rose by 19.56%, while exports to Turkey nearly doubled during the period."
