    "chunk_text": "Regenerative agriculture lies at the heart of the Roadmap. Hayleys Plantations aims to expand regenerative agricultural practices to 90% of cultivated land and introduce precision technologies across 75% of estates. GIS mapping, drones, digital field records and AI-supported decision-making are expected to improve crop management, water use, nutrient efficiency and climate resilience. At the same time, the Sector has committed to zero conversion of natural forests and the expansion of biodiversity restoration across estate landscapes\n\nWhile the three plantation companies operate under one Roadmap, each contributes a distinct area of ESG leadership.\n\nRegenerate also places strong emphasis on people and governance. strengthen succession planning and further improve occupational health and safety. Community priorities include housing, water and sanitation, education, nutrition, healthcare, digital literacy and youth development. These ambitions are backed by a formal governance structure. Each company maintains Board-level ESG oversight, while a joint Plantation Sector ESG Steering Committee coordinates implementation and reviews progress against key targets. ESG data is monitored through the Hayleys Sustainability Information System, enabling climate, environmental, social and governance performance to be integrated into operational and strategic decision-making. The strength of Regenerate lies in its combined approach. It connects TTE\u2019s science-based climate and nature leadership, KVPL\u2019s regenerative agriculture and community model, and HPL\u2019s responsible sourcing and market-readiness capabilities within one coherent transformation strategy."
