    "md5": "85af6ad88a9d3b6ae9c5aeae3341f06a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1987,
    "chunk_text": "Green finance encompasses a wide range of financial instruments, including:\n\nThese financial tools encourage businesses to adopt environmentally responsible practices while providing investors with opportunities to support sustainable economic growth.\n\nMajor stock exchanges now encourage listed companies to publish sustainability reports. Global development banks continue financing renewable energy, climate adaptation and resilient infrastructure projects. Institutional investors are also shifting billions of dollars into ESG-focused portfolios as they seek long-term value creation and reduced environmental risks.\n\nThis global movement demonstrates that sustainability is no longer viewed as a corporate responsibility initiative alone\u2014it has become a fundamental business strategy and an important consideration in financial decision-making.\n\nSri Lanka possesses enormous potential to become a regional leader in sustainable investment. The country is rich in renewable energy resources, biodiversity, agricultural potential, and human capital. However, climate change, resource depletion, urbanisation, and increasing energy demand present significant challenges.\n\nGreen finance can help address these issues by mobilising private and public capital towards sustainable projects that create long-term economic value.\n\nSri Lanka has significant solar, wind, hydro and biomass resources. Green financing enables businesses and households to invest in clean energy technologies, reducing dependence on fossil fuels while lowering energy costs.\n\nFuture urban development can incorporate energy-efficient buildings, green construction materials, intelligent transportation systems, and climate-resilient infrastructure that minimise environmental impact.\n\nAgriculture remains a vital sector of Sri Lanka\u2019s economy. Green finance supports farmers in adopting sustainable irrigation systems, organic farming practices, precision agriculture, and climate-resilient crop management."
  },
