    "chunk_size_bytes": 1949,
    "chunk_text": "Agriculture remains a vital sector of Sri Lanka\u2019s economy. Green finance supports farmers in adopting sustainable irrigation systems, organic farming practices, precision agriculture, and climate-resilient crop management.\n\nBanks and financial institutions are central to Sri Lanka\u2019s green transition. By integrating ESG principles into lending decisions, banks can encourage businesses to adopt environmentally responsible operations.\n\nFinancial institutions are also improving their own sustainability performance through digital banking, paperless transactions, renewable energy adoption, and responsible lending frameworks.\n\nAs sustainable finance continues to evolve, banks will increasingly act as strategic partners in helping businesses transition towards greener operating models.\n\nGreen bonds have become one of the fastest-growing sustainable investment instruments globally. These bonds raise capital specifically for projects that deliver measurable environmental benefits.\n\nFor Sri Lanka, expanding the green bond market could attract international investors seeking responsible investment opportunities while supporting national infrastructure development.\n\nA transparent regulatory framework and credible sustainability reporting will be essential for strengthening investor confidence.\n\nModern investors increasingly recognise that companies with strong ESG performance often demonstrate greater resilience, stronger governance, improved operational efficiency, and better long-term profitability.\n\nCompanies that successfully integrate ESG principles are often better positioned to attract international capital, improve brand reputation, and respond effectively to changing market expectations.\n\nThis shift is encouraging Sri Lankan businesses to embed sustainability into their corporate strategies rather than treating it as a standalone initiative.\n\nGreen finance creates numerous opportunities for companies of every size."
