    "md5": "bb8aa50ae9caf5e8fda2faf36b944ef2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1980,
    "chunk_text": "Businesses can also adopt reusable packaging systems that minimise single-use plastics while strengthening customer engagement.\n\nConstruction generates large quantities of waste materials that often retain considerable economic value.\n\nGreen building standards increasingly encourage the use of recycled materials and resource-efficient construction techniques.\n\nCrop residues can be converted into compost, bioenergy, animal feed, or biodegradable packaging materials instead of being burned or discarded.\n\nFood waste from hotels, supermarkets, and restaurants can also be processed into organic fertilisers or renewable energy through biogas production.\n\nThese solutions simultaneously reduce landfill waste and improve agricultural productivity.\n\nArtificial Intelligence (AI), the Internet of Things (IoT), blockchain, robotics, and advanced data analytics are helping organisations improve resource efficiency across entire value chains.\n\nProduct passports and digital traceability systems also help manufacturers recover valuable materials at the end of a product\u2019s life.\n\nInnovation is transforming waste management from a disposal challenge into a resource recovery industry.\n\nCompanies around the world are moving beyond traditional product sales towards service-based and circular business models.\n\nCustomers pay for the use of a product rather than owning it outright. Manufacturers retain ownership and responsibility for maintenance, upgrades, refurbishment, and recycling.\n\nExtending the lifespan of products through repair services reduces waste while creating additional employment opportunities.\n\nComponents recovered from used products are restored to like-new condition, reducing manufacturing costs and conserving raw materials.\n\nShared access to vehicles, equipment, office space, and digital platforms reduces unnecessary consumption while improving resource utilisation.\n\nThese business models create recurring revenue while reducing environmental impacts."
