    "md5": "b72b3cd06c976ca56dae66ebaf470eda",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1029,
    "chunk_text": "The transition towards a circular economy represents one of the most significant economic opportunities of the coming decades. Rather than viewing environmental sustainability as a cost, businesses are increasingly recognising it as a catalyst for innovation, efficiency, and long-term growth.\n\nAchieving this transformation will require collaboration between businesses, government agencies, financial institutions, research organisations, and consumers. Investment in technology, supportive regulations, education, and sustainable finance will accelerate progress towards a more resilient economy.\n\nUltimately, the circular economy is about reimagining the relationship between economic growth and environmental stewardship. It demonstrates that prosperity and sustainability can go hand in hand. By turning waste into value through innovation, Sri Lanka has the opportunity to build a cleaner, more resource-efficient, and globally competitive economy\u2014one that benefits businesses, communities, and future generations alike."
