    "chunk_text": "These activities even further the development of soft skills through the inclusion of financial literacy programmes, mathematics camps, arts, sports, leadership development, culinary experiences, and other interactive learning opportunities. Students are introduced to practical financial concepts from an early age while also developing creativity, teamwork, communication, and problem-solving skills. The objective is to expose children to experiences that many schools may have limited access to while encouraging confidence and holistic development.\n\nQ: How does Seylan Bank identify the schools that would benefit most from the programme?\n\nA: Selecting schools is a collaborative and carefully considered process. We work closely with our extensive branch network together with the Ministry and Department of Education to identify schools where our intervention can create the greatest long-term impact.\n\nEvery school has different needs. Some require complete library refurbishment, while others need access to books, digital learning tools, or educational technology. Our assessments help us understand the existing resources and determine how we can best strengthen the school\u2019s learning environment. We also prioritise schools where improved educational infrastructure can help bridge resource gaps and create more equitable learning opportunities for students.\n\nBeyond infrastructure, we provide carefully selected books and digital equipment that broaden educational opportunities while supporting modern teaching methods. Our objective is always to ensure that every investment delivers sustainable value for both students and teachers.\n\nQ: How has \u2018Pahasara\u2019 influenced communities beyond the school itself?"
