    "chunk_text": "This commitment has earned international recognition through an AAA ESG Rating from IdealRatings, reinforcing the Company\u2019s alignment with globally recognised sustainability frameworks and strengthening investor confidence.\n\nThe Company has continued to push the boundaries of sustainable finance. In 2025, LB Finance became the first financial institution in Sri Lanka to publicly commit to the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi), marking another important milestone in its climate journey. Through this commitment, the Company is developing science-based near-term and net-zero greenhouse gas reduction targets that align with the latest climate science and global efforts to limit temperature rise.\n\nLB Finance further strengthened its climate strategy by joining the Partnership for Carbon Accounting Financials (PCAF), adopting internationally recognised methodologies to measure financed emissions. During the 2024/25 financial year, it also became the first financial institution in Sri Lanka to independently verify its greenhouse gas inventory, including financed emissions, through Control Union Sri Lanka, demonstrating compliance with globally accepted standards.\n\nContinuing its leadership, LB Finance became the first financial institution in Sri Lanka to quantify and independently verify avoided greenhouse gas emissions, commonly known as Carbon Handprint. Unlike traditional carbon footprint reporting, Carbon Handprint captures the positive environmental impact created through financing activities that enable customers to reduce their own emissions. During the 2025/26 financial year, the Company\u2019s vehicle and solar financing portfolio generated 4,018 tonnes of independently verified avoided carbon dioxide emissions, highlighting the powerful role responsible finance can play in accelerating Sri Lanka\u2019s transition to a low-carbon economy."
  },
