    "md5": "1026d60bf825841471eb698670cf4997",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1631,
    "chunk_text": "One of the most visible expressions of this commitment is the company\u2019s Green Building Network, a nationwide initiative to develop environmentally responsible branch infrastructure. These purpose-built facilities are designed to operate with minimal environmental impact while enhancing efficiency. Many of these branches are fully powered by solar energy, with the ability to generate surplus electricity that can be fed back into the national grid. The buildings themselves incorporate sustainable construction materials, energy-efficient architectural design, and systems that optimise natural lighting and ventilation.\n\nCollectively, Ceylinco Life\u2019s Green Building Network represents a practical, scalable model of sustainable infrastructure within the financial services sector. At end 2025, Ceylinco Life had 32 green branch buildings on company-owned land. These buildings had generated approximately 1.12 GWh of solar energy, harvested 3.08 million litres of rainwater and recycled 1.386 million litres of water.\n\nBeyond infrastructure, Ceylinco Life has demonstrated a consistent focus on measuring and managing its environmental footprint. The company has undertaken comprehensive assessments of its greenhouse gas emissions, covering both direct and indirect impacts of its operations. These exercises provide a scientific basis for tracking progress and identifying opportunities for improvement. The company has set measurable targets for reducing its carbon footprint and has already achieved reductions through initiatives such as optimising energy use, reducing paper consumption, and improving fuel efficiency."
