    "language": "en",
    "md5": "8a49c7adfdc7e02a6ce06aef1b0ccf05",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1832,
    "chunk_text": "Importantly, this commitment extends beyond corporate reporting. Through initiatives supporting stronger sustainability governance and the development of sustainability reporting in the public sector, the accountancy profession is responding to the sustainability agenda across the wider economy and contributing to the global pursuit of the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).\n\nA significant milestone in this journey was the launch of the Preparers\u2019 Guide to SLFRS S1 & S2, a practical resource designed to support companies and professionals in navigating the requirements of the ISSB standards.\n\nThe initiative positions Sri Lanka among the first jurisdictions globally, and among the first in South Asia, to adopt and implement the ISSB standards. It also sends a clear message to international markets: Sri Lanka is committed to strengthening transparent, comparable and reliable sustainability reporting to support informed decision-making, attract sustainable investment and build long-term economic resilience.\n\nThe Guide provides practical, Sri Lanka-centric guidance for organisations and practitioners implementing the standards. SLFRS S1 establishes the general requirements for disclosing sustainability-related risks and opportunities that could reasonably be expected to affect an organisation\u2019s prospects, while SLFRS S2 focuses specifically on climate-related risks and opportunities.\n\nFor businesses, the transition to sustainability reporting can appear complex. The Guide is intended to help make that transition more practical, structured and accessible.\n\nReporting is only one component of a meaningful sustainability journey. Strong governance is equally essential to ensure that sustainability considerations are embedded in organisational decision-making, oversight and accountability."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-07-23-dailyftlk-aa73091e",
