    "md5": "e2f0737ce27470ad2f9a4f210fe4015c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1715,
    "chunk_text": "Advantis Embeds ESG Principles to Drive Sustainable Growth and Create Long-Term Value\n\nBlue Carbon awareness session for foreign dignitaries at the Anawilundawa Ramsar Wetland\n\nAs sustainability reshapes business models and value creation, the transportation and logistics sector, which faces significant decarbonisation challenges, has an important role to play in supporting a more resilient future. Advantis, the transportation and logistics arm of Hayleys PLC, is advancing this transition by embedding environmental, social and governance (ESG) principles across its operations, sustainability initiatives and stakeholder engagement.\n\nWith over six decades of experience, Advantis is Sri Lanka\u2019s most diversified transportation and logistics services provider. The Group delivers end-to-end solutions across Integrated Logistics, Freight Management, Marine and Energy, Project Logistics, Travel and Aviation, and other specialised services, with operations spanning Bangladesh, India, Indonesia, the Maldives, Myanmar, Singapore, Sri Lanka and Thailand.\n\nThe scale and complexity of these activities require sustainability considerations to be integrated into how the Group plans its operations, delivers services and prepares for future growth. This commitment is guided by HELIOS, Advantis\u2019 ESG strategy, which is aligned with the Hayleys Lifecode and built around seven key pillars: Energy, Emissions, Biodiversity, Employee Engagement, Community Engagement, Safety and Governance. Through HELIOS, Advantis embeds sustainability into decision-making and long-term growth.\n\nFor Advantis, this approach balances environmental stewardship, social responsibility and strong governance across its operations."
  },
