    "md5": "c90b270199267ab19650353a0e7019f4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1479,
    "chunk_text": "Tax burden unfair despite government revenue claims: Namal\n\nColombo, July 23 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka Podujana Peramuna (SLPP) National Organizer Parliamentarian Namal Rajapaksa has accused the government of imposing an unfair tax burden on the public despite claiming to have large amounts of revenue.\n\nAddressing a meeting in Udahamulla yesterday (July 22), he said that although President Anura Kumara Dissanayake had said that the government had \u201ccrores of rupees\u201d, there was no sufficient investment or benefit provided to the people in return for the taxes they pay.\n\n\u201cThe President proudly says, \u2018We have crores of rupees.\u2019 However, there is no investment in the country that is fair considering the amount of tax paid by the people,\u201d he said.\n\nNamal said the country was currently facing severe economic difficulties, with the cost of living increasing daily while taxes were being increased without proper consideration.\n\nHe alleged that the public was being forced to cover financial losses caused by government failures.\n\n\u201cIf there is any loss or theft within the government, the people are taxed to recover those losses,\u201d he claimed.\n\nCommenting on recent increases in electricity tariffs and fuel prices, Rajapaksa linked them to issues including the import of substandard coal and questioned whether ordinary citizens should bear the cost of such problems.\n\nGovt came to power on \u2018endless lies\u2019, failed to deliver promised system change: Namal"
  },
