    "md5": "a549bcfdceb0ba739de83d8893ee99b1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1883,
    "chunk_text": "\u2018Safe Mobility for 4All & 4Life\u2019\n\nThe Federation Internationale de L\u2019 Automobile\u2019s (FIA) \u2018Safe Mobility for 4All &4Life\u2019 global initiative is a collaborative project between the International Automobile Federation (FIA), the United Nations Institute for Training & Research (UNITAR) and the FIA Foundation.\n\nThe main objective of this programme is a joint capacity \u2013 building initiative of FIA & UNITAR, bringing together FIA member clubs and relevant government stakeholders from across the Asia \u2013 Pacific Region to support the design and implementation of National Road Safety initiatives.\n\nSince the Automobile Association of Ceylon(AAC) is a club under the FIA and engages in road safety activities & programmes, under the UN Decade of Action 2010 \u2013 2020 ; extended 2021-2030 along with the collaboration of the Road Development Authority(RDA) and representatives for the government, it was invited to participate in this programme.\n\n\u2018Safe Mobility for 4All &4Life\u2019 originated in Chiangmai, Thailand in October 2025 and thereafter a second Face- to -Face Workshop took place on 5 th & 6 th March 2026 in Manila, Philippines. During this period the participants had the opportunity to present the final outcomes of their national projects developed under this programme, shared experiences and lessons from the mentoring phase, engaged in discussions with international road safety experts and programme partners.\n\nOrganizers of the \u2018Safe Mobility for \u20184All & 4Life\u2019 formally invited AAC to their Fellowship Programme & Graduation event, which took place on the 13 th & 14 th July 2026 in Geneva, Switzerland. For this event Australia (Canberra), Australia (Tasmania), Bangladesh, Cambodia, India, Indonesia, Japan, Kyrgyzstan, Mongolia, Nepal, Philippines, Singapore, Thailand, Uzbekistan, Vietnam Hanoi), Vietnam (Ho Chi Minh City) were also invited."
