    "chunk_text": "The industry also sees potential to raise earnings through value-added products, including cinnamon oil and pharmaceutical products. Such products currently account for only about 5 percent of exports.\n\nCinnamon-based agritourism is another largely untapped opportunity. Lindara said initiatives such as Cinnamon Trails could allow visitors to experience traditional cinnamon-processing methods and sample cinnamon-based food products.\n\nHowever, the industry continues to face rising labour costs, a shortage of skilled cinnamon peelers, higher fertiliser and planting-material prices, outdated cultivation practices and inadequate infrastructure.\n\nDifficulties in consistently meeting international food safety and hygiene standards have also restricted access to some premium markets. Competition from cassia, a cheaper substitute, remains a major threat, particularly as Sri Lanka continues to depend heavily on lower-value markets."
