    "chunk_size_bytes": 1628,
    "chunk_text": "Govt. on alert over rising crimes involving foreign nationals\n\nColombo, July 25 (Daily Mirror) - The government is on high alert over an increasing number of crimes involving foreign nationals across Sri Lanka, following a recent abduction and murder of a Chinese national linked to a suspected rivalry between Chinese groups in Colombo.\n\nDeputy Minister of Public Security Sunil Watagala told the Daily Mirror that authorities are paying special attention to recent incidents involving foreign nationals and that strict actions are being taken under existing laws.\n\nThe Deputy Minister said Sri Lankan authorities remain on high alert following a rise in transnational cybercrime, illegal business operations, and other criminal activities involving foreign nationals.\n\nHe made these remarks following a recent crime involving Chinese nationals that resulted in the death of a Chinese citizen. The incident unfolded on Thursday within the high-security Colombo Port City.\n\nThe latest case has drawn attention to increasing tensions among foreign groups, with police investigating whether the abduction and murder of a foreign national was connected to a dispute involving cryptocurrency-related activities.\n\nAccording to police, three Chinese nationals who had arrived at Colombo Port City in a rented cab were ambushed while fishing near the suspension bridge between 2:00 a.m. and 3:00 a.m. on Thursday by around 20 attackers who arrived in a black van. The assailants allegedly threatened them with pistols, tied and blindfolded them, and assaulted them before taking two victims in the van and the third in another vehicle."
