    "md5": "e98213de9f688f7e95fa13b789a6e53c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1802,
    "chunk_text": "Thotalagala named on World\u2019s 50 Best Discovery list\n\nThotalagala, a luxury planter\u2019s bungalow in Sri Lanka\u2019s Haputale, has been selected for World\u2019s 50 Best Discovery, the global travel and hospitality platform from the team behind The World\u2019s 50 Best Hotels.\n\nThe recognition places Thotalagala among a carefully curated collection of exceptional hospitality destinations worldwide and marks yet another milestone for Island Life - Sri Lanka.\n\nSet on a historic estate stretching towards the iconic Lipton\u2019s Seat, Thotalagala offers an intimate all-inclusive experience with just seven individually themed suites, combining colonial heritage with contemporary luxury.\n\nGuests are invited to discover the culture of Sri Lanka\u2019s tea country through guided plantation walks, award-winning High Tea, heritage-inspired dining, immersive cookery experiences, and exclusive access to one of the island\u2019s most historic estates.\u00a0 \u201cThotalagala is the very first property that we started with at Island Life - Sri Lanka, exactly ten years ago. It has been amazing to see our family home now being transformed into one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most VIP addresses, showcasing the island\u2019s tea culture beautifully. To be recognised by 50 Best Discovery is a wonderful acknowledgement that authentic, destination-led hospitality continues to resonate with travellers around the world,\u201d says Amrit Rajaratnam, Managing Director of Island Life - Sri Lanka.\n\nAs one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most exclusive boutique hotels, Thotalagala has also been featured in leading international publications including Robb Report India, Cond\u00e9 Nast Traveller, Travel + Leisure, National Geographic Traveller, The Telegraph, and Tatler Asia, cementing its reputation as one of the country\u2019s most distinctive heritage stays."
  },
