    "md5": "68a71d0bda5d098488ace78320c34648",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1628,
    "chunk_text": "Eco Spindles-Gunadamin Elephant House lead Ruwanwelisaya cleanup\n\nEco Spindles (Pvt.) Ltd and Gunadamin Elephant House marked the period following Poson Poya Day with meaningful environmental action, bringing together employees, volunteers and community partners to protect the sacred Ruwanwelisaya premises while demonstrating how discarded plastic can be transformed into valuable resources.\n\nConducted in Anuradhapura on June 30, 2026, the day following Poson Poya Day, the corporate social responsibility initiative brought together 60 volunteers, including 20 employees from Eco Spindles and Elephant House, alongside representatives from the Thilaka Eco Centre and local communities.\n\nThe project focused on responsible waste collection, segregation and recycling while raising awareness among pilgrims and visitors about the importance of safeguarding Sri Lanka\u2019s cultural and religious heritage sites.\n\nApproximately 350 kilogrammes of discarded plastic bottles were collected during the cleanup. The recovered bottles will be processed by Eco Spindles and transformed into monofilaments and yarn, reinforcing the company\u2019s commitment to advancing a circular economy by converting plastic waste into useful materials.\n\nEco Spindles CEO Recycling Prashantha Malimbadage said, \u201cProtecting the environment must go hand in hand with preserving the places that hold deep cultural and spiritual value for our nation. This initiative demonstrates that responsible waste management and recycling can create lasting environmental value while encouraging communities to become active participants in the circular economy.\u201d"
  },
