    "md5": "398a299923e53241396de61cc8567b99",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1537,
    "chunk_text": "Week ends in red\n\nThe ASPI closed in red as a result of price losses in counters such as Hatton National Bank, Ceylinco Holdings and Ceylon Grain Elevators with the turnover crossing Rs. 2.4 Bn. Meanwhile, the S&P SL20 edged down. Crossings were witnessed in United Motors Lanka, Hatton National Bank and Commercial Bank accounting for 68.2% of the turnover. Mixed interest was observed in Hayleys, LOLC Finance and Ceylon Grain Elevators whilst retail interest was noted in Merchant Bank of Sri Lanka & Finance Rights, Beruwala Resorts and Browns Investments.\n\nDuring the week, the ASPI and the S&P SL20 lost 1.1% and 1.0% respectively, whilst recording an average daily turnover of Rs. 2.59 Bn.\n\nRetailing sector was the top contributor to the market turnover (due to United Motors Lanka) whilst the sector index gained 0.14%. The share price of United Motors Lanka decreased by Rs 0.10 (0.37%) to close at Rs 26.90.\n\nThe Banking sector was the second highest contributor to the market turnover (due to Hatton National Bank and Commercial Bank) whilst the sector index decreased by 0.23%. The share price of Hatton National Bank lost Rs 3.00 (0.77%) to close at Rs 385.00. The share price of Commercial Bank moved down by Rs 0.50 (0.25%) to close at Rs 201.50.\n\nSoftlogic Life Insurance and Hayleys were also included amongst the top turnover contributors. The share price of Softlogic Life Insurance recorded a loss of Rs 1.20 (1.47%) to close at Rs 80.20. The share price of Hayleys declined by Rs 0.50 (0.22%) to close at Rs 225.00."
  },
