    "chunk_text": "The Uvas \u2013 Initial seasonal offerings, which came up for sale this week, met with excellent demand and the prices for the BOP/BOPFs ranged between Rs.2,100-3,000 per kilogramme and Rs.2,200-2,450 per kilogramme, respectively.\n\nThe CTCs in the High and Medium Grown category \u2013 the availability of the BP1s, were very limited, with hardly any offerings.\n\nIn the Low Grown category, the limited BP1s on offer were irregular, whilst the PF1s, which commenced at marginally lower levels, strengthened by up to Rs.20 per kilogramme for selected invoices towards the close.\n\nThe interest from the shippers to the UK and continent continued to be limited, whilst there was improved activity from South Africa. The shippers to Japan and China also appeared to be fairly active. Less interest was seen from the CIS.\n\nThe seasonal teas from the Uva planting districts, which were readily absorbed, were competed for by a wider array of buyers, which is encouraging.\u00a0 The Low Growns totalled approximately 1.9 M/Kgs. The Semi-Leafy, Tippy and Premium categories witnessed fair demand, whilst the Leafy category met with less demand.\n\nIn the Leafy and Semi-Leafy catalogues, the Select Best and Best BOP1s maintained, whilst the balance together with the bolder varieties appreciated. The Select Best and Best OP1s were firm, whilst the Below Best varieties together with the poorer sorts were irregularly easier. The OPs in general were firm on last levels, whilst the OPAs were easier. The PEK/PEK1s, in general, maintained. In the Tippy catalogue, the high-priced FBOPs were irregular, whilst the balance in general was firm. The well-made FF1s were firm, whilst the cleaner Below Best and cleaner teas at the bottom appreciated.\u00a0 The balance was firm.\n\nIn the Premium catalogue, the Tippy teas in general were firm to selectively dearer."
