    "md5": "123616951f01865b8c20a8ddd5c429e0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1892,
    "chunk_text": "Even while the civil war was raging, in the south an armed uprising to topple the state led by the Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna (JVP) broke out in 1987 against the presence of Indian troops in the Indian Peace Keeping Force (IPKF).\n\nIn the north and east, the ordinary man/woman recognising their politicians were doing little to solve their problems took a revolutionary decision to support a national party \u2013the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) led by the JVP- rather than regional parochial political parties who kept depending on India to solve Lankan problems.\n\nThey realised long before their political leaders, India had neither time nor intention to meddle once more in what was basically Lanka\u2019s internal problems. Basically they were tired of politicians who continually run to India to seek solutions to what were basically Sri Lankan problems.\n\nIn the south too, survivors and victims of previous government\u2019s massacres and ordinary folk tired of waiting for solutions to basic problems and for justice\u00a0 turned to the JVP-led NPP for justice and a better economic deal.\n\nUnfortunately,\u00a0 the new regime has not been able to tackle the basic problems of those in the north and east, the Muslim community or the Sinhalese masses who form the voter-base of the NPP.\n\nThe cost of living is way beyond wage levels in the country. Despite the rural background of the top leadership of the JVP, farmers are protesting high costs of agricultural inputs for their produce. The Muslim community who also voted for the NPP rather than religious themed political parties feel let down.\n\nOn the international scene where even countries of the West are banning Israeli goods produced in occupied territories, the JVP-NPP government boasts of sending more Lankan workers to Israel so-as-to free up Israeli workers to join the Israeli armed forces committing genocide in Palestine and Lebanon."
