    "md5": "6df328d72e5263f89a040adc76fbb871",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2008,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThe global landscape is undergoing profound changes, and hegemonism and power politics continue to prevail. The international community faces the danger of a return to the law of the jungle,\u201d he said.\n\nAmbassador Qi also defended China\u2019s military modernisation, saying the People\u2019s Liberation Army had continued to upgrade its capabilities under the leadership of President Xi Jinping while remaining committed to safeguarding national security and contributing to international peace.\n\n\u201cThe stronger China grows, the more peaceful the world becomes; the more China develops, the more prosperous the world gets,\u201d he said.\n\nChinese Defence Attach\u00e9 Senior Colonel Fu Xiao said the relationship between the two militaries had continued to strengthen through regular engagement with Sri Lanka\u2019s defence establishment and expressed confidence that cooperation would deepen further as the two countries prepare to mark the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations next year.\n\n\u201cChina-Sri Lanka friendship has a long-standing history. Next year we will celebrate the 70th anniversary of our diplomatic ties,\u201d Senior Colonel Fu said.\n\nShe said she had spent the past two months meeting senior Sri Lankan defence officials and military commanders and would work to advance practical cooperation between the armed forces of the two countries.\n\n\u201cI will devote all my time and energy to promote pragmatic and constructive collaboration between the two militaries,\u201d she said.\n\nSenior Colonel Fu said China continued to pursue a defensive national defence policy and described the PLA as a force contributing to international peace and humanitarian assistance.\n\nShe said China had deployed approximately 50,000 personnel to 26 United Nations peacekeeping missions over the past 36 years, while the Chinese Navy had maintained anti-piracy escort operations in the Gulf of Aden since 2008, completing more than 1,600 escort missions and assisting over 80 vessels, more than half of them foreign ships."
  },
