    "chunk_text": "She said China had deployed approximately 50,000 personnel to 26 United Nations peacekeeping missions over the past 36 years, while the Chinese Navy had maintained anti-piracy escort operations in the Gulf of Aden since 2008, completing more than 1,600 escort missions and assisting over 80 vessels, more than half of them foreign ships.\n\n\u201cIn the eyes of our partners, China\u2019s deeds matter more than words,\u201d Senior Colonel Fu said.\n\n\u201cIn the era of global upheaval and uncertainty, let us join hands through our actions to strive for a peaceful and prosperous world.\u201d\n\nThe reception formed part of Beijing\u2019s annual commemoration of the founding of the People\u2019s Liberation Army and comes ahead of the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between China and Sri Lanka in 2027, a milestone both sides indicated would provide an opportunity to further expand bilateral engagement, including defence cooperation."
