    "chunk_text": "No matter how the political landscape changes or how the international situation evolves, China and Sri Lanka have always stood firmly together, carrying forward the spirit of independence, self-reliance, solidarity, and mutual assistance enshrined in the Rubber-Rice Pact. Together, we share weal and woe and set a fine example of friendly coexistence and mutually beneficial cooperation among countries.\n\nAt present, China-Sri Lanka relations are facing a historic opportunity to build on past achievements and forge ahead into the future. Both sides are committed to deepening the China-Sri Lanka strategic cooperative partnership featuring sincere mutual assistance and everlasting friendship, painting a splendid picture of a China-Sri Lanka community with a shared future through concrete actions.\n\nThis journey has witnessed China-Sri Lanka cooperation shine as brilliantly as Ceylon sapphires. China and Sri Lanka are fellow travellers on the path towards development and revitalisation, and good partners in win-win cooperation. China has always supported Sri Lanka in pursuing a development path that suits its national conditions and in focusing on economic development to achieve national prosperity.\n\nOver the past six years, I have been delighted to see fruitful outcomes in high-quality Belt and Road cooperation and exchanges across various fields between our two countries."
