    "chunk_text": "This journey has witnessed China-Sri Lanka cooperation shine as brilliantly as Ceylon sapphires. China and Sri Lanka are fellow travellers on the path towards development and revitalisation, and good partners in win-win cooperation. China has always supported Sri Lanka in pursuing a development path that suits its national conditions and in focusing on economic development to achieve national prosperity.\n\nOver the past six years, I have been delighted to see fruitful outcomes in high-quality Belt and Road cooperation and exchanges across various fields between our two countries.\n\nToday, China is one of Sri Lanka\u2019s largest sources of foreign investment and one of its largest aid providers. The level of China-Sri Lanka economic and trade cooperation has been steadily rising, with robust exchanges and cooperation in the port economy, modern agriculture, digital economy, culture, tourism, and other fields, vigorously promoting Sri Lanka\u2019s economic and social development while bringing tangible benefits to the peoples of both countries. China will continue to share opportunities, pursue development, and promote prosperity with Sri Lanka through high-standard opening-up.\n\nThis journey has witnessed the friendship between our peoples become as rich and mellow as Ceylon tea. As a Sri Lankan poem says, \u201cA true friend shares your joys and sorrows, like a mural that never turns its page.\u201d\n\nOver the past six years, my wife and I have travelled to every province of this beautiful island, visiting numerous temples, villages, communities, and schools, carrying out livelihood assistance initiatives, including school supply donation events, and attending inauguration ceremonies for China-aided water supply projects, water purification facilities, and Chinese language training centres. These events have brought the local people supplies and equipment brimming with the profound friendship and best wishes of the Chinese people."
