    "chunk_text": "Over the past six years, my wife and I have travelled to every province of this beautiful island, visiting numerous temples, villages, communities, and schools, carrying out livelihood assistance initiatives, including school supply donation events, and attending inauguration ceremonies for China-aided water supply projects, water purification facilities, and Chinese language training centres. These events have brought the local people supplies and equipment brimming with the profound friendship and best wishes of the Chinese people.\n\nI vividly remember that my wife and I celebrated the Chinese New Year with Sri Lankan friends at the Nelum Pokuna Theatre, where everyone warmly greeted us in Chinese with wishes of \u201cHappy Chinese New Year!\u201d The Dragon Boat Culture Festival, the \u201cTea for Harmony\u201d Yaji Cultural Salon, the \u201cChinese Bridge\u201d Chinese Proficiency Competition for Foreign Secondary School Students, the Tai Chi Promotion Event, and the Chinese Film Festival have all been warmly embraced by the Sri Lankan people\u2014a \u201cChinese culture craze\u201d has truly taken hold here.\n\nMy wife and I have also spent many Sinhala and Tamil New Years, Vesak Festivals, and Poya days participating in a dazzling array of cultural and people-to-people exchange activities in Sri Lanka. Together, our two countries have composed a new chapter of dialogue, mutual learning, closer interaction, and mutual inspiration among civilisations in the new era."
