    "chunk_text": "We have adhered to the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence, supported and coordinated with each other in multilateral fields, and safeguarded each other\u2019s core interests and international fairness and justice, sending a strong message of Global South solidarity and self-reliance, as well as a shared commitment to regional peace, stability, development, and prosperity. Our two countries are jointly advancing the building of a community with a shared future for humanity and implementing the Global Development Initiative, the Global Security Initiative, the Global Civilisation Initiative, and the Global Governance Initiative so as to address global challenges and create a brighter future for the world.\n\nThe China-Sri Lanka friendship reflects the shared aspirations of our peoples, and China-Sri Lanka cooperation represents the trend of the times.\n\nWe will further strengthen the synergy of development strategies, deepen industrial and investment linkages between our two countries, advance high-quality Belt and Road cooperation, and continue to promote cooperation in infrastructure, new quality productive forces, new energy, modern agriculture, rural revitalisation, poverty reduction, digital transformation, tourism, marine economy, port economy, science and technology, and other fields.\n\nWe will expand Sri Lanka\u2019s exports of specialty products to China, join hands to open up broad prospects for mutual success and shared prosperity, and build a China-Sri Lanka community with a shared future. By doing so, we can better benefit our two peoples. History and facts have proven and will continue to prove that partnering with China means embracing opportunities; believing in China means believing in tomorrow; and investing in China means investing in the future.\n\nThough mountains may separate us, we share the same clouds and rain; though miles lie between us, we look upon the same moon. As a diplomat, I am destined to keep moving forward