    "chunk_size_bytes": 1900,
    "chunk_text": "Tharoor, Mano discuss Indo-Lanka ties, regional cooperation and democratic governance\n\nColombo, July 25 (Daily Mirror) - Acclaimed author, parliamentarian and Chairman of India\u2019s Parliamentary Standing Committee on External Affairs, Dr. Shashi Tharoor MP, held a cordial and substantive meeting with Tamil Progressive Alliance Leader and Member of Parliament Mano Ganesan and TPA Vice President for International Relations Barath Arullsamy during his recent visit to Colombo.\n\nMano Ganesan and Arullsamy paid a courtesy call on Dr. Tharoor, during which they exchanged views on Sri Lanka\u2013India relations, regional political developments, cultural ties and opportunities for deeper cooperation between the two neighbouring nations.\n\nDr. Tharoor, a four-term Member of Parliament representing Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala and one of India\u2019s most celebrated authors and public intellectuals, discussed the strategic importance of regional connectivity, transshipment and closer economic engagement between India and Sri Lanka.\n\nMano Ganesan highlighted the longstanding relationship between India and Sri Lanka and the importance of continued engagement concerning the aspirations of the Indian Origin Tamil community, while strengthening wider people-to-people and cultural relations.\n\nThe discussion also covered the emerging common platform of Tamil-speaking political parties in Sri Lanka and its role in advancing democratic dialogue, constitutional reform and inclusive national development.\n\nDr. Tharoor further shared insights into the functioning of India\u2019s Parliamentary Standing Committee on External Affairs, including the contribution of parliamentary committees and opposition legislators to policy oversight and democratic governance.\n\nIn a gracious gesture, Dr. Tharoor presented Mano Ganesan with an authentic Kerala shawl, adding warmth and cultural significance to the occasion."
