    "chunk_size_bytes": 1120,
    "chunk_text": "Iran rescues 28 Indian seafarers after vessel attacked\n\nAl Jazeera: All 28 Indian crew members on board a Mozambique-flagged ship have been safely rescued after coming under attack near Iran\u2019s territorial waters.\n\nThe tanker DISHA transmitted a distress signal after being targeted by \u201chostile forces\u201d as it entered Iranian waters.\n\n\u201cUpon the occurrence of the incident, the ship immediately transmitted a distress call to the Iranian coastguard,\u201d Mohammad Fathali, Iran\u2019s ambassador to India, told the ANI news agency.\n\n\u201cIn response, the relevant Iranian maritime and rescue authorities were deployed to the scene without delay and promptly initiated rescue operations. All crew members on board the vessel, including the 28 Indian nationals, were rescued safely and remain in good health.\u201d\n\nFathali cautioned against foreign naval involvement in the Strait of Hormuz.\n\n\u201cExperience has repeatedly demonstrated that the presence and intervention of extra-regional military forces have not enhanced security in the region; rather, they have contributed to heightened tensions and greater instability.\u201d"
