    "chunk_text": "In 2025, President Xi Jinping and other Chinese leaders met with President Dissanayake and Prime Minister Amarasuriya during their visits to China, reaching important consensus and fruitful outcomes of cooperation. These interactions have provided new strategic guidance for the development of bilateral relations. Today, political mutual trust between our two countries has continued to consolidate, economic and trade cooperation has further expanded, people-to-people and cultural exchanges have grown increasingly rich, and interactions at all levels\u2014across departments, regions, and sectors\u2014have become ever closer. At present, China-Sri Lanka relations are facing a historic opportunity to build on past achievements and forge ahead into the future. Both sides are committed to deepening the China-Sri Lanka strategic cooperative partnership featuring sincere mutual assistance and everlasting friendship, painting a splendid picture of a China-Sri Lanka community with a shared future through concrete actions.\n\nToday, China is one of Sri Lanka\u2019s largest sources of foreign investment and one of its largest aid providers. The level of China-Sri Lanka economic and trade cooperation has been steadily rising, with robust exchanges and cooperation in port economy, modern agriculture, digital economy, culture, tourism, and other fields\u2014vigorously promoting Sri Lanka\u2019s economic and social development while bringing tangible benefits to the peoples of both countries. China will continue to share opportunities, pursue development, and promote prosperity with Sri Lanka through high-standard opening-up."
