    "chunk_text": "This journey has witnessed mutual trust and support between China and Sri Lanka stand as firm as Sigiriya Lion Rock. China and Sri Lanka have always steadfastly upheld the international system with the U.N. at its core, the international order underpinned by international law, and the basic norms governing international relations based on the purposes and principles of the U.N. Charter. We have adhered to the Five Principles of Peaceful Coexistence, supported and coordinated with each other in multilateral fields, and safeguarded each other\u2019s core interests and international fairness and justice, sending a strong message of Global South solidarity and self-reliance, as well as a shared commitment to regional peace, stability, development and prosperity. Our two countries are jointly advancing the building of a community with a shared future for humanity and implementing the Global Development Initiative, the Global Security Initiative, the Global Civilization Initiative, and the Global Governance Initiative, so as to address global challenges and create a brighter future for the world."
