    "chunk_text": "Trump pauses Iran strikes over missile shortages\n\nThe Telegraph - Donald Trump has paused plans to escalate the war on Iran after being warned that the US is running low on missiles.\n\nFor the first time in nearly two weeks, the US president called off strikes on the Islamic Republic over the weekend and has set aside plans to return to major combat operations.\n\nThe decision also allows time and space for negotiations with Iran.\n\nConcerns were raised during a White House meeting on Friday night, according to reports.\n\nJD Vance, the vice-president, and General Dan Caine, the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, were among those who spoke out, the New York Times (NYT) reported.\n\nOfficials familiar with the deliberations told US media that concerns over dwindling supplies of air-defence munitions, particularly interceptor missiles needed to defend American bases and regional partners against Iranian ballistic missiles and drones, played a central role in the decision.\n\nThree American soldiers were killed in Jordan last Friday when a ballistic missile slipped through American air defences fending off a barrage of Iranian missiles and drones.\n\nAnother soldier was killed in Iraq while trying to make safe a downed Iranian drone.\n\nAfter 13 straight nights of US attacks on Iran, Mr Trump ordered no more strikes on Friday or Saturday night.\n\nA department of defence source told CNN that operations are \u201con a hold\u201d.\n\nThe pause came as Mr Trump also signalled he believes Tehran may now be prepared to negotiate, though Tehran continues to dig its heels in with demands to retain control of the critical Strait of Hormuz.\n\nOn Sunday, the Iranian foreign ministry said that technical and political consultations between the two sides were ongoing via Omani intermediaries. Talks over the strait were, Iran said, productive."
