    "chunk_size_bytes": 1936,
    "chunk_text": "Shan Althaf\u2019s Trinity immortals of 2026\n\nInter-school rugby season 2026 scripted a story of unmatched quality produced by Trinity College Kandy culminating with the second leg of the 80th Bradby Shield encounter on the 25th of July at the Lion\u2019s Den at picturesque Pallekele Rugby Stadium.\u00a0 Bradby Shield only in its 80th year more importantly stands as the world\u2019s second oldest inter-school rugby fixture between Trinity College Kandy and Royal College Colombo dating back to well over a century.\n\nTrinity\u2019s fairy tale Bradby triumph of 2024 and the dominant destruction of 2026, had its set of heroes spearheaded by a calm and composed Shan Althaf who finally held aloft the prestigious Shield in his eighth Bradby appearance, five of which were rewarded with player of the match awards. Althaf\u2019s instinct driven deceptive penetrative runs during moments of stagnation made the Trinity side look untouchable and a treat to watch right throughout the season.\n\nDeputy leaders in Nisith Kumarasinghe and senior prefect Udan Wijekoon made the challenges that much easier. Imposing figures of Achintha Jayasena, Minula Yaddehige, Hamza Abdeen, Kevin Weerakoon, Nahil Jayah, Akash Fernando, Sadeesha Weerawansa, Maduranga De Silva, Prathiv Yainne, Rithika Weragama, Dimath Ambepitiya, Bilal Nazeer, Mukshith Shyam, Misala Perera and Vihanga Indusara now becomes a part of Trinity rugby folklore whilst Aamar Malik, Evin Jayasena, Abdul Malik are thrust with the mantle of guiding the schools rugby cradle to continued success.\n\nFor purposes of record Trinity overcame Thurstan College, Zahira College and, Wesley College before dismantling Royal College to win the President\u2019s Trophy Knockout tournament. What followed was a nine match unbeaten run brushing aside opponents\u2019 with relative ease to add the League title for a second year running before regaining the prize scalp \u2013 the Bradby Shield with an 72 -20 aggregate."
