    "md5": "ee9fd245b1d5d51a93f559d0b4bdcdc6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1376,
    "chunk_text": "Former Envoy Kananathan salutes Liberia on 179th Independence Day, signals renewable energy partnership initiative\n\nColombo, July 26 (Daily Mirror) - Former Envoy Ambassador Kananathan has extended his warmest congratulations today to His Excellency President Joseph Nyuma Boakai,\u00a0 the Government, and the people of the Republic of Liberia on the occasion of the country\u2019s 179th Independence Day.\n\nIn his message, Kananathan commended Liberia\u2019s enduring legacy as Africa\u2019s oldest republic and expressed his admiration for the resilience, unity, and determination of the Liberian people in advancing peace, democracy, and national development.\n\n\u201cAs Liberia celebrates this important national milestone, I extend my sincere best wishes to President Boakai and all Liberians. Kananathan said .\n\nKananathan also reaffirmed his commitment to strengthening ties with Liberia through sustainable development initiatives. He noted that he is currently in the process of initiating a renewable energy project in Liberia, aimed at supporting the country\u2019s clean energy transition, promoting economic growth, and expanding access to sustainable power solutions.\n\nHe expressed confidence that the planned initiative would contribute to Liberia\u2019s long-term development goals while fostering innovation, investment, and international cooperation in the renewable energy sector."
