    "md5": "2e4d568fe55939dc2507a9c6ce882ed7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1994,
    "chunk_text": "India Calling forum on August 6\n\nIn a major push to redefine economic ties between Sri Lanka and India, the Lanka India Business Association (LIBA) has announced the highly anticipated \u2018India Calling\u2019 corporate forum.\n\nScheduled for August 6, at Taj Samudra, Colombo, from 9:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m., the full-day event is designed to bridge commercial gaps, unpack regulatory friction and establish a framework for shared cross-border prosperity.\n\nThe LIBA is hosting the forum to actively catalyse deeper private sector integration, moving bilateral talks from policy theory into actionable investment corridors.\n\nThe event arrives at a critical juncture as Sri Lanka actively recalibrates its macroeconomic framework and eyes stronger integration with the Indian market.\n\nThe forum boasts an extraordinary line-up of keynote speakers flying in from India to address the critical facets of the economic relationship:\n\nIndia\u2019s former Planning Commission Deputy Chairman Montek Singh Ahluwalia, a key architect of India\u2019s 1991 economic reforms, will discuss India\u2019s massive economic transformation and the specific structural lessons Sri Lanka can adopt to drive its own recovery.\n\nProfessor C. Raja Mohan, one of India\u2019s leading foreign policy strategists and academics, will present on the geopolitical necessity of \u2018shared prosperity\u2019 as a sustainable, long-term strategy for regional stability.\n\nRenowned mythologist, author and corporate consultant Devdutt Pattanaik will offer an unconventional perspective, breaking down the \u2018Monsoon Market Myth\u2019 to explain how deep-rooted cultural narratives shape consumer behaviour and market dynamics in South Asia.\n\nThe media landscape will also be represented by leading Indian journalists. These include Asian News International Editor-in-Chief Smita Prakash, known for her extensive political reporting and WION Principal Diplomatic Correspondent Sidhant Sibal, who has covered global geopolitics and foreign affairs extensively."
  },
