    "md5": "d0dc56bc562b9400dbfb65cb08c56fca",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1826,
    "chunk_text": "Committed to protecting natural ecosystems, Pussalla Agri Ventures implements responsible agricultural practices focused on soil conservation, biodiversity protection, efficient resource utilisation and the elimination of prohibited synthetic chemicals. These initiatives support the long-term sustainability of agricultural production while preserving the environment for future generations.\n\nPussalla Agri Ventures Chairman Philip J. Wewita said, \u201cThis recognition is a proud milestone for our organisation and reflects our commitment to sustainable agriculture and responsible business practices. Sustainability is not simply a certification or a project for us; it is embedded throughout our operations, from cultivation to the final product. We remain committed to producing premium-quality organic cinnamon while protecting the environment, empowering our farming communities and enhancing Sri Lanka\u2019s reputation as a trusted supplier of sustainable agricultural products to global markets.\u201d\n\nThe Sri Lankan Sustainability Awards recognise organisations that demonstrate leadership in environmental sustainability, governance, innovation, social responsibility and sustainable business excellence, encouraging businesses to align their operations with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals.\n\nReceiving the Sustainable Agriculture Infrastructure Award further strengthens Pussalla Agri Ventures\u2019 position as one of Sri Lanka\u2019s emerging leaders in sustainable agribusiness. The company continues to invest in environmentally responsible farming, internationally certified production systems and value-added product development, supporting the country\u2019s ambition to expand exports of premium organic agricultural products while creating long-term value for customers, communities and the environment."
