    "md5": "faa2b3287b9ecfa51d23548a4a57d6dc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1856,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka Brand Conclave 2026 tomorrow\n\nKey event to unite global expertise and local insights to shape future brands\n\nSri Lanka Brand Conclave 2026, which is scheduled to be held on 28 July at Cinnamon Grand, will place global brand leadership thinking at the centre of Sri Lanka\u2019s marketing landscape, bringing together internationally recognised experts, senior business leaders and marketing professionals to explore how organisations can build stronger, future-ready brands in a rapidly evolving marketplace.\n\nNational University of Singapore NUS Business School Associate Professor of Marketing and Academic Director of the Executive MBA Dr. Prem Shamdasani, Marketing Leadership Institute CEO and Founder of The Marketing Leadership Masterclass Thomas Barta; The One Club for Creativity APAC Regional Director and BBDO Singapore former Creative Chairman Tay Guan Hin; and Aleph Group Country Director for Sri Lanka and Bangladesh Ehsanul Hoque, are the global voices that will be featured at the conclave shaping the future of branding and marketing.\n\nThe conclave, which is designed to serve as Sri Lanka\u2019s flagship platform for brand leadership and innovation, will explore the factors transforming modern brands, varying from creativity and purpose to artificial intelligence, digital transformation, and evolving consumer expectations.\n\nDr. Prem Shamdasani will discuss the increasing significance of purpose-driven brands and how businesses can build deep relationships with consumers. Thomas Barta will explore how marketers can evolve from brand managers into leaders who contribute to the growth of their business. Md. Ehsanul Hoque will highlight new developments and trends in AI-powered marketing within Google\u2019s evolving ecosystem, while Tay Guan Hin will address creativity as a strategic advantage in building distinctive brands."
  },
