    "chunk_text": "Dr. Prem Shamdasani will discuss the increasing significance of purpose-driven brands and how businesses can build deep relationships with consumers. Thomas Barta will explore how marketers can evolve from brand managers into leaders who contribute to the growth of their business. Md. Ehsanul Hoque will highlight new developments and trends in AI-powered marketing within Google\u2019s evolving ecosystem, while Tay Guan Hin will address creativity as a strategic advantage in building distinctive brands.\n\nSenior marketing leaders from Singer Sri Lanka and Dialog Axiata will participate in the CMO Dialogue, \u201cHow Brands are Leveraging the Modern Digital Ecosystem and the Evolving Skills in Demand,\u201d which will explore how organisations are adapting to digital transformation, evolving consumer behavior, and the changing capabilities needed in modern marketing teams.\n\nA Strategy to Action session will also be included in the programme, which will bring together industry leaders from CBL and Fotera to discuss how organisations can convert brand strategy into measurable business outcomes. The conversation will provide useful insights on carrying out brand initiatives, promoting growth, and generating long-term value in a market that is becoming increasingly competitive.\n\nThe conclave program will also offer delegates access to expert deep dives of today\u2019s brand playbook, local and global case studies, consumer data, including Gen Z behavior, and the current thoughts on AI, creativity, purpose, and community-driven brand growth. To strengthen brand performance and deal with changing market dynamics, participants will be exposed to global perspectives, practical frameworks, and actionable strategies."
