    "description": "Hayleys Plantations advances Payment for Ecosystem Services across Sri Lanka\u2019s estates",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/Hayleys-Plantations-advances-Payment-for-Ecosystem-Services-across-Sri-Lanka-s-estates/34-795195",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1785114613.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-07-27-dailyftlk-0d19704e-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "46c7678546edb040f530b73c3c8165f6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1991,
    "chunk_text": "Hayleys Plantations advances Payment for Ecosystem Services across Sri Lanka\u2019s estates\n\nHayleys Plantations Managing Director Dr. Roshan Rajadurai, UNDP in Sri Lanka Resident Representative Azusa Kubota and Hayleys General Manager - Group ESG Prashani Illangasekera with the top management and other officials\n\nHayleys Plantations Managing Director Dr. Roshan Rajadurai, UNDP in Sri Lanka Resident Representative Azusa Kubota, Hayleys General Manager - Group ESG Prashani Illangasekera and The Pekoe Trail Organisation Executive Director Pramudith Thenabadu with officials\n\nHayleys Plantations has joined hands with with UNDP BIOFIN to advance Payment for Ecosystem Services (PES) initiatives across its plantation landscapes through Talawakelle Tea Estates PLC, Horana Plantations PLC and Kelani Valley Plantations PLC\n\nPayment for Ecosystem Services (PES) is a nature-financing mechanism that rewards individuals, communities and organisations for protecting ecosystem services such as water resources, biodiversity, carbon storage and soil conservation. By recognising the economic value of these environmental benefits, PES encourages long-term investment in ecosystem protection.At Bambarakelly Estate in Nuwara Eliya, Horana Plantations PLC has formalised a watershed conservation initiative focused on protecting critical water catchments, enhancing biodiversity, strengthening renewable energy integration and improving climate resilience for surrounding communities and downstream users.\n\n\u201cHealthy ecosystems are fundamental to the long-term success of our plantations. Through Payment for Ecosystem Services, we are investing in conservation approaches that protect biodiversity, strengthen climate resilience and create shared value for communities and businesses alike. These projects reflect our commitment to integrating sustainability into the way we manage our landscapes for future generations,\u201d stated Hayleys Plantations Group Managing Director Dr. Roshan Rajadurai."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-07-27-dailyftlk-0d19704e",
    "num": "dailyftlk-0d19704e",
    "date_str": "2026-07-27",
    "description": "Hayleys Plantations advances Payment for Ecosystem Services across Sri Lanka\u2019s estates",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/Hayleys-Plantations-advances-Payment-for-Ecosystem-Services-across-Sri-Lanka-s-estates/34-795195",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1785114613.0,
