    "chunk_size_bytes": 1823,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s underworld violence escalates\n\nColombo, July 27 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka has recorded 22 shooting incidents so far this year, leaving 15 people dead and 12 others injured. Nearly half of these incidents, 10 in total, were reported within the two-week period between July 11 and July 25.\n\nThe 10 shootings during this period claimed three lives and left five people injured. The incidents have ranged from targeted killings and attacks linked to organized criminal groups. Several other incidents resulted in property damage or targeted individuals without causing casualties. Police have made a number of arrests in connection with the shootings, while investigations into the remaining cases are continuing.\n\nMeanwhile, Sri Lanka Police have attributed the recent spate of shootings across the country to rival drug trafficking networks, saying the attacks are primarily driven by organized criminal disputes, contract killings, and attempts to intimidate rival groups.\n\nResponding to questions about the ten shootings reported over the past two weeks, including the latest incident on Saturday, Police Spokesman Assistant Superintendent of Police (ASP) F.U. Wootler said every incident investigated so far has shown links to organized crime and the illegal drug trade.\n\nAccording to the Police Spokesman, the shootings are largely the result of rival criminal groups attempting to eliminate competitors, settle financial disputes, and prevent opposing gangs from expanding their influence.\n\nHe said that many of the individuals believed to be orchestrating the attacks are currently operating from overseas, while the intended victims are often relatives or associates of rival gang members. Such attacks, he said, are carried out to intimidate opponents and send a message to competing criminal networks."
