    "md5": "6ff987fca0458ce72229f083b298860c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1423,
    "chunk_text": "Power of criminals\n\nThe police called for suspending the Kavadi dance segment of the historic Devinuwara Vishnu Maha Devalaya main procession amidst security concerns due to a possible eruption of violence between two Kavadi groups alleged to underworld connections. The police asked the Devalaya officials to do without Kavadi this year following threats issued by an underworld figure, known as Mohamed Imran aka Kanjipani Imran that he would not allow  Kavadi dance to be performed in the Perahera without the participation of a group of dancers backed by him.\n\nIt was reported that threat assessments carried out by the state intelligence agencies had indicated the possibility of a violent clash in case of the Kavadi segment being included in the Perahera.\n\nBut Minister of Public Security Ananda Wijepala yesterday granted permission for all Kavadi dance troupes that participated in last year\u2019s procession to take part in this year\u2019s Perahera as well. Thus, an underworld character has succeeded in forcing the custodians of a holy shrine, the government and the police into bending to his will.\n\nThe JVP-NPP government boasts of having launched a series of successful anti-crime operations, but drug dealers and other criminals remain powerful, so much so that their members are carrying out narcotics operations and unleashing violence in heavily guarded prisons and threatening to attack religious festivals."
