    "md5": "011e389aece9ecb154ab7c856327bbbb",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1686,
    "chunk_text": "The JVP-NPP government boasts of having launched a series of successful anti-crime operations, but drug dealers and other criminals remain powerful, so much so that their members are carrying out narcotics operations and unleashing violence in heavily guarded prisons and threatening to attack religious festivals.\n\nTerrorists and other criminals have to be lucky only once. The task of neutralising underworld threats to a religious festival cannot be accomplished overnight by simply deploying the police and the armed forces. If the police and the intelligence agencies are of the view that the best way to handle the underworld threat at issue is to suspend the Kavadi dance segment in the Devinuwara Perahera, they cannot be faulted for that.\n\nThe manner in which a criminal\u2019s threats to the Devinuwara Perahera have unsettled the law enforcement authorities is proof of the growing vulnerability of the state vis-\u00e0-vis the power of crime syndicates involved in drug trafficking, contract killings and gun running. This is no longer just a public security issue; it is a threat to national security. Hence, the need for the government, the police, the intelligence agencies, and, if necessary, the armed forces to go all out to neutralise the underworld.\n\nHelping the government tame the Opposition has apparently become the raison d\u2019etre of the police, especially the CID. There is no gainsaying that the former rulers and their associates responsible for criminal activities, including financial crimes, must be brought to book, but the police must remain focused on protecting the public against organised criminal gangs that are still capable of striking anywhere at will."
  },
