    "md5": "a1d43da4c2a9744b76a1b75632a8d974",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1986,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka officially banned the culling of dogs twenty years ago, in 2006, replacing extermination by the most inhuman methods with a more humane CNVR (Catch-Neuter-Vaccinate-Release), Initially,\u00a0 most street dogs were caught, treated and released, with several foreign organisations, too, helping.\n\nToday, the number of street dogs is put as high as six million, but there is no exact census and the actual figure could be between one million to 1.3 million.\n\nThis puts those who feed and care for street dogs under terrific strain in these cash-strapped, high inflationary times. The main ojective of the\u00a0 government\u2019s anti-rabies seems to the gradual elimination of street dogs by neutralising those who feed them. Not getting food would weaken and gradually starve these dogs to death. When applied to people, this method is called genocide.\n\nThis is patently clear from all the social media posts made so far in favour of this rabies elimination campaign.\n\nBefore delving into the blatant inhumanity of this objective, let\u2019s see just how bad the rabies situation in Sri Lanka is.\n\nIn 2025, 14 rabies related deaths were recorded. This is the lowest figure on record, while 2024 recorded 20 confirmed deaths.\n\nCompared to this, 56 people have died of dengue so far in 2026.\u00a0 Wild elephants killed over 100 people in 2025, while between 100-400 people die of snakebite any given year. What about deaths caused by alcohol-related driving? Overall traffic accidents claim an average of about 2,500 to 3,000 lives each year, with alcohol consumption identified as a contributing factor in roughly 4.5% to over 5% of investigated road traffic accidents. During this year\u2019s Vesak festival, a drunken double\u00a0 cab\u00a0 driver\u00a0 killed\u00a0 eight people waiting at a dan sal queue. Even if we take the lower figure of 2,500, we have 25 deaths per year due to alcohol-related driving accidents. But there is no debate or any no serious protest regarding the cause \u2013 alcohol consumption."
  },
