    "chunk_text": "He alleged that the proposal would undermine judicial independence by prolonging the tenure of incumbent judges while existing vacancies in the Superior Courts remained unfilled, delaying the progression of judicial officers through the judicial hierarchy.\n\nPremadasa also said the SJB had consistently defended the independence of the judiciary and had never attempted to exert pressure on judges through parliamentary committees.\n\nAbeysinghe also questioned whether the BASL applies consistent standards, saying he would welcome a statement from the association regarding former Justice Minister Wijeyadasa Rajapakshe or his son.\n\n\u201cWe will see whether this is genuine or whether these actions are being taken to protect one particular class,\u201d he said.\n\nCommenting on recent remarks made in Parliament by NPP MP Asitha Niroshana, Abeysinghe said he did not believe the MP had made the allegations merely by relying on parliamentary privilege and suggested further clarification should be sought from the MP."
  },
