    "chunk_text": "JVP-NPP propagandists are in overdrive, condemning MP Wijesiri and the entire Opposition, which they say is full of lawbreakers. However, Wijesiri committed the offence at issue when he was in the UNP, which was on honeymoon with the JVP. The UNP-led UNF, which formed the Yahapalana government in 2015 with the SLFP-led UPFA as a partner, was dependent on the JVP for survival in 2019. The JVP threw its weight behind the UNP when the then President Maithripala Sirisena fell out with Prime Minister Ranil Wickremesinghe, sacked the latter, appointed former President Mahinda Rajapaksa as Prime Minister and tried to dissolve Parliament as he could not muster a working majority, in late 2018.\n\nNow that MP Wijesiri has been sentenced to prison for attacking and injuring two police officers, action must be taken against the perpetrators of heinous crimes against the members of the police and the security forces in the late 1980s, such as the killing of police and military personnel and their family members for refusing to carry out the JVP\u2019s illegal orders, attacking police stations and military camps and robbing their weapons.\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake has rightly pointed out that some serious crimes are not subject to statutory limitations for prosecution. He has said he will not allow those crimes to be buried in the sands of time. He ought to ensure that all lawbreakers who got away with their offences during the previous governments, especially those who perpetrated barbaric crimes against the JVP members in the late 1980s, are brought to justice. Most of those who committed crimes during the Mahinda Rajapaksa government have not been brought to justice. Why hasn\u2019t the JVP-led NPP government ordered a thorough probe into the Batalanda torture chamber, where hundreds of JVP members and many others suspects with no links to the JVP suffered painful deaths."
