    "md5": "84d96d6992929cf050938874816831d0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1918,
    "chunk_text": "Tea traders chart new course for Ceylon Tea through quality, value and resilience\n\nSenaka Alawattegama, Raj Obeysekere, Lushantha De Silva, Dr. Martha Tesfaye Woldemichael and Mansoor Akbarally\n\nMansoor Akbarally, Dr. Martha Tesfaye Woldemichael, Lushantha De Silva and Senaka Alawattegama\n\nThe Colombo Tea Traders\u2019 Association (CTTA), the apex private sector body representing Sri Lanka\u2019s tea trade, reaffirmed its commitment to strengthening the global competitiveness of Ceylon Tea, as it concluded its 132nd Annual General Meeting (AGM), unveiling a renewed vision centred on sustainable industry growth.\n\nHeld recently at Cinnamon Life Hotel, Colombo, the AGM brought together leading representatives of Sri Lanka\u2019s tea industry, government institutions, diplomatic missions, development partners, exporters, plantation companies, brokers, buyers and the international business community, to review the industry\u2019s progress and discuss strategies for safeguarding the future of one of the country\u2019s most valuable export sectors.\n\nThe event was graced by International Monetary Fund (IMF) Resident Representative in Sri Lanka Dr. Martha Tesfaye Woldemichael as the chief guest, Sri Lanka Tea Board Chairman Raaj (R.K.) Obeysekere as the guest of honour, while Ceylon Chamber of Commerce Secretary General and Chief Executive Officer Shiran Fernando delivered the guest address.\n\nFormer CTTA chairmen and honorary members, senior officials from the Plantation Industries Ministry, Sri Lanka Tea Board, Tea Research Institute, Tea Small Holdings Development Authority, members of the diplomatic community and representatives of the affiliated industry associations were also in attendance.\n\nDelivering the Chairman\u2019s Address, CTTA Chairman Lushantha de Silva reflected on the association\u2019s distinguished 132-year legacy in promoting governance, transparency and integrity within Sri Lanka\u2019s tea trade."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
