    "chunk_size_bytes": 1443,
    "chunk_text": "The Jaffna crab curry is the kind of centrepiece that demands both attention and a willingness to get one\u2019s hands involved. Close behind are the mutton curry and much sought-after fish head curry, completing a trio that captures the depth and intensity for which northern Sri Lankan cooking is celebrated.\n\nThere is also a quiet visual code running through the dining room. The chefs in red aprons have travelled from Jaffna; those in black belong to Sheraton\u2019s Colombo team.\n\nFor those unwilling to surrender the entire plate to spice, the buffet includes a selection of international dishes. It is a thoughtful concession to mixed dining groups, allowing the curious to explore Jaffna\u2019s cuisine while others remain closer to familiar territory.\n\nBeneath the aromas and live cooking is a smart hospitality strategy.\n\nThemed food festivals have become an effective way for city hotels to draw diners who may not otherwise enter their restaurants. A limited run creates urgency; visiting chefs provide credibility; and the cultural narrative turns dinner into an experience worth sharing. I\n\nThe Jaffna showcase follows the hotel\u2019s Malaysian Food Festival, which concluded earlier in July. More culinary promotions are expected in the coming months as Sheraton continues using food to bring different cultures and destinations to Colombo.\n\nA Journey Through Jaffna continues at Colombo Kitchen, Sheraton Colombo, until Sunday, 2 August."
  },
