    "md5": "9f8f4c2f86057243e48321f0c8d2f686",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1879,
    "chunk_text": "Alumex quarterly profit jumps sevenfold as margins improve\n\nAlumex PLC reported a sevenfold increase in net profit for the three months ended June 2026, as lower cost of sales, stronger operating profit and higher finance income offset a marginal decline in revenue.\n\nThe aluminium manufacturer posted a net profit of Rs.149.9 million for the quarter, compared with Rs.21.4 million in the corresponding period last year. Earnings per share rose to 25 cents from four cents.\n\nRevenue declined 3.8 percent year-on-year to Rs.3.58 billion from Rs.3.72 billion. However, cost of sales fell at a faster rate of 8.4 percent to Rs.2.84 billion, lifting gross profit by 19 percent to Rs.733.9 million.\n\nAs a result, the gross profit margin improved to 20.5 percent from 16.6 percent a year earlier.\n\nThe gains at gross profit level were partly offset by higher operating expenses. Distribution expenses rose 11 percent to Rs.162.2 million, while administrative expenses increased 20 percent to Rs.311.1 million.\n\nDespite the higher expenses, profit from operating activities climbed 23 percent to Rs.270.2 million. The operating profit margin improved to 7.6 percent from 5.9 percent in the year-earlier quarter.\n\nFinance income rose sharply to Rs.185.9 million from Rs.65.5 million. Finance costs also increased by 28 percent to Rs.324.4 million, but net finance costs narrowed to Rs.138.5 million from Rs.188.3 million.\n\nThis helped lift profit before tax to Rs.131.8 million from Rs.30.5 million.\n\nThe bottom line was further supported by a tax reversal of Rs.18.2 million, compared with a tax expense of Rs.9.1 million in the corresponding quarter.\n\nAlumex\u2019s balance sheet expanded during the quarter, with total assets rising to Rs.18.84 billion as at end-June from Rs.17.53 billion at end-March. Inventories increased to Rs.6.14 billion from Rs.4.43 billion over the same period."
  },
