    "chunk_size_bytes": 1198,
    "chunk_text": "The same principle applies to infrastructure. Development is not measured only by new highways or impressive buildings. Reliable public transport, efficient digital services, modern hospitals, dependable energy supplies and strong water management systems are equally important. These investments rarely produce immediate political dividends, but they shape the quality of life and economic competitiveness of a country for generations.\n\nClimate resilience deserves the same long-term thinking. Responding after disasters occur is no longer enough. Planning ahead is not optional; it is essential.\n\nSri Lanka has already shown remarkable resilience. The question now is whether the country will settle for recovery or aim for something more lasting.\n\nHistory rarely remembers governments for short-term political victories. It remembers those that strengthened institutions, invested in people and made choices that continued to benefit the country long after they had left office.\n\nThat is the challenge before Sri Lanka today. The decisions made now will shape the opportunities available not only to today\u2019s citizens but also to the children who will inherit this country in the decades ahead."
