    "chunk_size_bytes": 1212,
    "chunk_text": "None of these improvements will succeed in isolation. This is not one-way traffic. Public awareness of the true scale of the menace, combined with a clear understanding of shared responsibility, is essential. The people must recognise that they are simultaneously victims of this threat and the primary beneficiaries of success. With that recognition comes responsibility, to report credible intelligence, support rehabilitation and reintegration, protect young people from recruitment, and reject the stigma that hinders recovery.\n\nThe thousands of public security committees already formed must be genuinely activated and empowered as the grassroots engine of this partnership.\n\nImmediate goals should focus on visible network disruption, rapid user referral and activation of community structures. Mid-term goals must deliver technical upgrades, judicial coordination and institutional capacity. Long-term success, however, rests overwhelmingly on prevention.\n\nWhatever else is said and done, the most effective, efficient and ultimately most beneficial investment is in robust prevention measures-sustained, consistent and powered by proactive intelligence blended with actionable and strategic intelligence."
