    "md5": "87d0f0d69d00fcb5fa3418a95a8f3aa2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 871,
    "chunk_text": "Formally engage major social media platforms to secure faster removal of damaging content while launching sustained public media literacy campaigns through community and religious platforms.\n\nProvide visible leadership, clear assurance and institutional protection to honest officers, while maintaining firm accountability.\n\nIt is time to move from announcements to outcomes, from reactive responses to structured immediate, mid-term and long-term goals, and from rhetoric to disciplined, intelligence-driven prevention and collective national effort. The stakes are too high for anything less.\n\n(This analysis is offered in the interest of national security, institutional reform, and public safety)\n\n(The writer is a Senior Superintendent of Police (Retd.), Former Deputy Director (Counter Terrorism), State Intelligence Service; Former Director, Police Special Branch)"
