    "chunk_text": "High Commissioner Jha emphasised that Pali is the language of the earliest Buddhist scriptures, including the Tripitaka, which embodies the timeless message of Dhamma. In a world increasingly affected by conflict, he said, the Buddha\u2019s teachings provide a path towards peace, compassion, and the welfare of all humanity.\n\nHe further observed that Sri Lanka continues to play a unique role in preserving Pali through its use in religious rituals, chanting, and Theravada Buddhist traditions.\n\nBuilding on that momentum, he said India has continued to support efforts to preserve and promote Pali, including assisting the Pathfinder Foundation in reprinting important classical Pali grammar texts such\u00a0 as Namamala and Balawatharo.\n\nThe symposium focused on the current state of Pali education in Sri Lanka, future prospects for its development, innovative approaches to teaching and learning, and stronger collaboration among Pirivenas, universities, research institutions, and international partners.\n\nParticipants also discussed ways of strengthening cooperation between Sri Lankan and international Pali scholars and educational institutions while laying the foundation for a sustainable national program to promote the study, teaching, research, preservation, and wider use of the Pali language for future generations."
