    "chunk_size_bytes": 1990,
    "chunk_text": "FLi Super expands islandwide presence with Karandeniya outlet\n\nFLi Super, the supermarket chain of FLi Trading, a strategic business unit of Future Life Holdings, recently opened its newest outlet in Karandeniya.\n\nThe new outlet highlights the unique concept by bringing together FLi Super, a dedicated FLiCo electronics corner inside the supermarket, and the group\u2019s flagship microfinance brand, Future Life Investments Ltd. (FLi), under one roof.\n\nThe ground floor houses the supermarket, offering a comprehensive range of groceries, fresh produce, household essentials, and everyday necessities alongside quality electrical and home appliances through the FLiCo Corner.\n\nThe brand offers an integrated ecosystem, bringing together retail, electronics, and inclusive finance under one roof. Customers can shop for their daily essentials and purchase selected products through exclusive interest-free five-instalment payment schemes, whilst also conveniently accessing FLi\u2019s responsible financial solutions within the same location. This concept reflects the group\u2019s commitment to making everyday living more affordable while creating greater financial inclusion for the communities it serves.\n\nLocated on the upper floor, the FLi branch extends the group\u2019s commitment beyond retail by delivering accessible financial solutions to entrepreneurs, self-employed individuals, daily wage earners, salaried employees, and families seeking to improve their livelihoods. Through responsible lending, a culture of investment, and customer-focused financial guidance, FLi continues its mission of promoting financial inclusion and supporting sustainable economic growth.\n\nFLi Trading Director \u2013 Operations Hansa Jayawardhana said: \u201cOur vision has always been to create convenient, reliable, and customer-focused experiences wherever we operate. The opening of our 19th supermarket in Karandeniya reflects this commitment while bringing greater convenience and value to the community.\u201d"
