    "md5": "4cd20570d13792cd9983d694ab8d98c9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1781,
    "chunk_text": "Ibrahim Zadran\u2019s 95 powers Jaffna Kings to win over Colombo Kaps\n\nJuly.29 (Mirror Sports) - Jaffna Kings boosted their Lanka Premier League 2026 playoff hopes with a convincing 19-run victory over Colombo Kaps at the Pallekele International Cricket Stadium, powered by Ibrahim Zadran\u2019s brilliant half-century and Dilshan Madushanka\u2019s match-winning bowling spell.\n\nZadran produced his best innings of the tournament, anchoring the Jaffna innings with a classy 95 from 65 deliveries. The Afghanistan opener combined timing and power, smashing 12 boundaries and three sixes before narrowly missing out on a well-deserved century.\n\nKamil Mishara provided valuable early momentum with 44, while Towhid Hridoy\u2019s unbeaten 31 helped Jaffna finish strongly as they posted an imposing 202 for 5 from their 20 overs.\n\nColombo needed an aggressive start in their chase but struggled to build momentum throughout the innings. Sadeera Samarawickrama top-scored with 44, while Kamindu Mendis and Milan Rathnayake contributed 28 and 26 respectively. However, regular wickets prevented Colombo from building the partnerships required.\n\nMadushanka turned the game decisively in Jaffna\u2019s favour with an outstanding left-arm pace spell, claiming 3 for 30 \u2014 his best bowling figures of the tournament. He received strong support from the rest of the attack as Colombo\u2019s required run rate continued to rise.\n\nColombo eventually finished on 183 for 9, handing Jaffna Kings another valuable victory as the race for the LPL 2026 playoffs intensifies.\n\nJaffna Kings 202/5 (20 overs): Ibrahim Zadran 95 (65), Kamil Mishara 44, Towhid Hridoy 31*; James Neesham 2/30.\n\nColombo Kaps 183/9 (20 overs): Sadeera Samarawickrama 44 (36), Kamindu Mendis 28, Milan Rathnayake 26; Dilshan Madushanka 3/30."
