    "chunk_text": "Australia\u2019s Gold Rush, Seales\u2019 heroics, Essex history & UEFA oppose FIFA plan\n\nJuly.29 (Mirror Sports) -\u00a0From medal dominance to cricket heroics, historic milestones and football controversies, the world of sport produced another action-packed day. Australia, West Indies, Essex Cricket and UEFA all made headlines in the latest global sports roundup.\n\nAustralia continues to dominate the Glasgow 2026 Commonwealth Games, leading the medal table with 35 gold, 18 silver and 27 bronze medals as of 29 July.\n\nThe Australian team has built a strong advantage across multiple sports, securing the top position ahead of its Commonwealth rivals. With more events still to come, Australia remains on course to extend its lead and strengthen its position as the most successful nation at the Games.\n\nJayden Seales claimed five wickets as West Indies defeated Pakistan by 90 runs in the first Test at the Brian Lara Cricket Academy in Trinidad. The victory gave the hosts a 1-0 lead in the two-match series.\n\nChasing 211 for victory, Pakistan were bowled out for 120 after a late fightback from Babar Azam, who remained unbeaten on 58. Seales finished with figures of 5-20, while Justin Greaves also played a key role with his brilliant bowling performance.\n\nWest Indies captain Roston Chase dedicated the win to the late Sir Garfield Sobers, saying the team wanted to honour the legendary cricketer with a memorable performance. The second Test will begin in Port of Spain on August 2.\n\nWest Indies 311 (Hope 92; Ali 4-50) & 181 (Joseph 38; Abbas 5-22)\n\nPakistan 282 (Masood 109; Greaves 5-27) & 120 (Azam 58*; Seales 5-20)\n\nEssex Cricket have appointed Rachel Lewis as the club\u2019s first-ever female chair of the board in their 150-year history. Lewis replaces Jason Gallian, who stepped down from the role after \u201ccareful consideration\u201d last week."
