    "chunk_text": "Essex Cricket have appointed Rachel Lewis as the club\u2019s first-ever female chair of the board in their 150-year history. Lewis replaces Jason Gallian, who stepped down from the role after \u201ccareful consideration\u201d last week.\n\nLewis said she was excited to lead the club into a new era, with Essex focused on ground redevelopment and continued success for both their men\u2019s and women\u2019s teams. Gallian will remain involved as a board member.\n\nUEFA and Manchester Mayor Andy Burnham have criticised FIFA\u2019s plan to bring private investment into its competitions, including the FIFA World Cup. FIFA said the move aims to boost football development funding beyond $10 billion through a new commercial subsidiary, FIFA Forward Enterprise.\n\nThe proposal would allow third-party investors to take minority stakes in the venture, with US firm Thrive Eternal expected to lead the investor group. The plan still needs approval from FIFA\u2019s 211 member associations.\n\nUEFA said the move \u201ccrosses a line\u201d, while Burnham warned that football should not be controlled by investors. He insisted the game belongs to fans and communities rather than commercial interests.\n\nIbrahim Zadran\u2019s 95 powers Jaffna Kings to win over Colombo Kaps"
