    "chunk_size_bytes": 707,
    "chunk_text": "Anti-Corruption Unit constable dead in apparent suicide\n\nPanadura, July 29 (Daily Mirror) - A police constable has died by suspected suicide after shooting himself with his official service firearm.\n\nAccording to the police, the deceased officer was attached to the Panadura Walana Anti-Corruption Strike Unit.\n\nThe incident occurred early this morning (29) near the main gate of the police station, where the constable allegedly shot himself using his T-56 assault rifle.\n\nAfter sustaining critical injuries in the shooting, the officer was admitted to the Panadura Base Hospital, where he subsequently succumbed to his injuries.\n\nPolice said the deceased was a 28-year-old resident of the Peradeniya area."
