    "md5": "dc610b4aa2d7256f0f38e8447ab01f1d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1359,
    "chunk_text": "Operating in line with the highest global environmental standards, the Punnakudah plant demonstrates that large-scale industrial growth can coexist with resource conservation, by implementing the following measures.\n\nLow-impact processing: Advanced machinery minimizes chemical and energy usage across dyeing and finishing operations.\n\nLong before commercial operations commenced, Jay Jay Textile Lanka established active community engagement programmes across the Eastern Province. They include:\n\nCoastal conservation: Regular beach cleanup initiatives along the Eastern coastline.\n\nSocial cohesion: Hosting community Vesak Dansal programs to foster cultural unity.\n\nDisaster relief: Providing direct aid, emergency meals, and logistical support during extreme weather events.\n\nCommunity upliftment: Conducting capacity building programmes for local school students.\n\nJay Jay Textile Lanka is supported by its parent company, Jay Jay Mills Lanka (established in Sri Lanka in 2004), and its ultimate parent company, Jay Jay Mills India, which brings over four decades of world-class textile manufacturing expertise. With an established operational network across Avissawella, Matara, Monaragala, Trincomalee, and Mannar, this new Eastern expansion reinforces the group\u2019s long-term commitment to position Sri Lanka as a sustainable apparel manufacturing hub."
  },
  {
