    "md5": "cc7dad2a83f0647a0defc914da2615ba",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1727,
    "chunk_text": "CA Sri Lanka and APFASL launch second intake of MPFM Degree Programme\n\nThe Institute of Chartered Accountants of Sri Lanka (CA Sri Lanka), together with its public sector wing, the Association of Public Finance Accountants of Sri Lanka (APFASL) inaugurated the second batch of the Master of Public Financial Management (MPFM) Degree Programme on 24 July 2026 at the CA Sri Lanka Auditorium, welcoming 65 public sector professionals from across the country.\n\nThe ceremony was graced by Professor Indika Karunathilake, Vice Chancellor of the University of Colombo, as Chief Guest. Also in attendance were CA Sri Lanka President Tishan Subasinghe, APFASL President K. V. C. Dilrukshi, Chief Executive Officer of CA Sri Lanka Lakmali Priyangika; members of the Board of Study; distinguished academics; and senior practitioners from the Ministry of Finance, the Inland Revenue Department and the National Audit Office.\n\nAddressing the gathering, Professor Indika Karunathilake commended CA Sri Lanka and APFASL for introducing a nationally recognised Master\u2019s degree dedicated to public financial management. He noted that the programme would strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s public financial management system by developing a new generation of competent public finance professionals capable of leading governance, fiscal and digital reforms.\n\nTishan Subasinghe hailed the MPFM Degree as a significant and forward-looking initiative that aligns with Sri Lanka\u2019s ongoing public sector reform efforts. He noted that the programme equips finance professionals with the specialised knowledge and competencies required to address evolving challenges in public financial management, governance, budgeting, auditing and digital transformation."
  },
