    "chunk_size_bytes": 1865,
    "chunk_text": "Janashakthi Life among SL\u2019s 50 Best Workplaces for 2026\n\nJanashakthi Life has been recognised among Sri Lanka\u2019s 50 Best Workplaces for 2026 by Great Place To Work Sri Lanka.\n\nThe 50 recognised workplaces comprise 17 Large, 13 Medium, 10 Small, and 10 Micro workplaces, with Janashakthi Life recognised in the Medium category, comprising organisations with 251\u2013500 employees.\n\nThe recognition is based on the Great Place To Work\u00ae Trust Index Employee Experience Survey, which evaluates employees\u2019 experiences of trust, pride, and workplace relationships, alongside a Culture Audit that assesses the organisation\u2019s people practices. The Trust Index contributes 75 percent of the overall score, while the Culture Audit accounts for the remaining 25 percent. Janashakthi Life\u2019s inclusion follows its Great Place To Work Certified status and an 88 percent Employee Trust Index\u2122 score achieved in 2025, reinforcing the consistency of its employee experience and workplace practices.\n\n\u201cBeing recognised among Sri Lanka\u2019s 50 Best Workplaces, together with the strong sense of inclusivity and camaraderie experienced by our employees, reflects the strength of our culture and the leadership philosophy that shapes our workplace. The endorsement of our employees is a great encouragement to further strengthen our workplace and reinforce the values we all live by. Our values of respect, collaboration, and integrity are strongly reflected in the Great Place To Work workplace health indicators, while being performance-driven and embracing innovation remain firmly embedded in our culture. It is particularly encouraging to note that our team members feel they are given equal opportunities, empowered to contribute, and supported with the guidance needed to reach their fullest potential,\u201d said Ravi Liyanage, Director/CEO of Janashakthi Insurance PLC."
