    "chunk_text": "Intex-InMac Sri Lanka 2026 to showcase future of textile sourcing and manufacturing\n\nSouth Asia\u2019s leading textile sourcing platform, Intex, together with InMac, the dedicated textile and garment technology exhibition, will return to the Bandaranaike Memorial International Conference Hall (BMICH) from August 5 to 7, 2026, bringing together the global textile and apparel industry under one roof.\n\nThe landmark exhibition reinforces Sri Lanka\u2019s position as a leading destination for textile sourcing, apparel manufacturing and industrial innovation.\n\nIntex-InMac Sri Lanka 2026 is endorsed by several leading industry institutions and trade bodies, including the Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB), Industrial Development Board, Embassy of Indonesia in Sri Lanka, Joint Apparel Association Forum and its member associations and Sri Lanka-China Business Cooperation Council, among others.\n\nThis year\u2019s exhibition will feature more than 250 exhibitors representing over 15 countries and regions, showcasing the latest innovations across the textile and apparel value chain.\n\nIntex will present fashion fabrics, fibres, yarns, denim, trims, accessories, sustainable and functional textiles, chemicals, dyes and textile processing solutions.\n\nMeanwhile, InMac will introduce next-generation garment machinery, artificial intelligence-enabled sewing systems, automated cutting and spreading technologies, digital printing solutions, factory automation and smart manufacturing technologies designed to improve productivity while reducing the manufacturing costs.\n\nThe event is expected to attract buyer delegations and trade visitors from more than 12 countries, creating valuable opportunities for international sourcing, technology partnerships, investment and business expansion."
