    "chunk_text": "The event is expected to attract buyer delegations and trade visitors from more than 12 countries, creating valuable opportunities for international sourcing, technology partnerships, investment and business expansion.\n\nA key highlight of the exhibition will be the three-day Interactive Business Forum Seminar Series, organised with the support of GTEX-ITC and the Moratuwa University Textile Association.\n\nThe forum will bring together internationally recognised industry experts and thought leaders to discuss the emerging trends, technological advancements and the future direction of Sri Lanka\u2019s textile and apparel industry.\n\nSpeaking about the technology showcase, Worldex India Executive Director Arti Bhagat said, \u201cThe future of Sri Lanka\u2019s apparel industry will be shaped by smarter factories, advanced technologies and continuous innovation. Through InMac, we are bringing world-class manufacturing solutions closer to Sri Lankan manufacturers, helping them enhance productivity, optimise costs and build globally competitive, future-ready factories.\u201d\n\nFor more than a decade, Intex has successfully connected global suppliers with Sri Lanka\u2019s apparel industry, strengthening supply chains, promoting international collaboration and supporting the country\u2019s ambition of achieving US $ 8 billion in apparel and textile exports.\n\nIndustry professionals, manufacturers, exporters, buyers, investors and stakeholders are invited to experience the latest innovations, build strategic partnerships and explore new business opportunities at Intex-InMac Sri Lanka 2026."
