    "md5": "f1b1342820bda9916895d6ac9fc6e1f6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1963,
    "chunk_text": "Tea industry overview: January to June - 2026\n\nDuring the period January to June 2026, Sri Lanka\u2019s tea industry recorded declines in Production and Export volumes compared to the same period in 2025, while the National Tea Sale Average Price showed a marginal increase. Total tea production dropped by 3.89 Mn/Kgs, falling from 135.77 Mn/Kgs in 2025 to 131.89 Mn/Kgs in 2026. Total exports also declined by 3.71 Mn/Kgs, decreasing from 126.81 Mn/Kgs to 123.10 Mn/Kgs. Meanwhile, the National Tea Sale Average recorded a marginal increase of Rs. 3.55 per kilogram, increasing from Rs.1,158.54 in 2025 to Rs. 1,162.09 in 2026.\n\nIn terms of export destinations, Turkey emerged as the largest importer of Ceylon Tea during the first half of 2026. Turkey demonstrated a significant increase in demand, with imports nearly tripling compared to the previous year, rising from 7.91 Mn/Kgs in 2025 to 19.71 Mn/Kgs in 2026. Iraq, which had been the largest importer during Q1 2026, experienced a notable decline of 5.29 Mn/Kgs but remained the second-largest destination. Russia maintained stable demand with a marginal increase of 0.40 Mn/Kgs to 11.61 Mn/Kgs. Azerbaijan demonstrated strong growth of 2.76 Mn/Kgs to reach 6.56 Mn/Kgs. However, markets such as China, Libya, and Saudi Arabia registered noticeable declines, with China dropping by 0.23 Mn/Kgs, Libya declining by 6.90 Mn/Kgs, and Saudi Arabia falling by 0.04 Mn/Kgs.\n\nFOB prices, when measured in Sri Lankan Rupees, showed year-on-year improvement across the cumulative period, rising from Rs. 1,745.10 in 2025 to Rs. 1,810.28 in 2026, largely reflecting the currency depreciation. FOB values in USD terms remained under slight pressure throughout the period, declining from USD 5.86 in 2025 to USD 5.70 in 2026. Consequently, equivalent US Dollar export earnings for the cumulative period declined by approximately USD 41.87 Mn (5.63 percent), falling from USD 743.12 Mn in 2025 to USD 701.25 Mn in 2026."
  },
