    "chunk_text": "The comparison of CTC Tea Production for the January\u2013June 2026 period against the corresponding period in 2025 reflects a strong overall improvement across all elevations, with total production increasing by 1.45 Mn/Kgs, from 11.95 Mn/Kgs in 2025 to 13.41 Mn/Kgs in 2026.\n\nLow Grown CTC production also recorded an increase of 0.11 Mn/Kgs, rising from 4.95 Mn/Kgs in 2025 to 5.06 Mn/Kgs in 2026, further supporting the overall upward trend.\n\nOverall, CTC tea production increased from 11.95 Mn/Kgs in January\u2013June 2025 to 13.41 Mn/Kgs in the corresponding period of 2026, reflecting an improvement across all elevations. Medium Grown teas were the principal driver of this growth, followed by High Grown and Low Grown teas, contributing to the overall expansion in CTC tea production during the first half of 2026.\n\nThe comparison of Sri Lanka Tea Sale Averages for the period January to June 2026 against the corresponding period in 2025 indicates a marginal improvement in the overall average price in Sri Lanka Rupee terms, while the US Dollar values declined across all elevation categories.\n\nIn the High Grown category, the average price increased in Sri Lanka Rupee terms from Rs. 1,078.13 in 2025 to Rs. 1,127.48 in 2026, reflecting a gain of approximately Rs. 49.35. However, in US Dollar terms, the average declined by USD 0.07 from USD 3.62 to USD 3.55. The Medium Grown category recorded a decline in both Rupee and US Dollar values. The average price decreased by approximately Rs. 39.49, falling from Rs.1,029.89 in 2025 to Rs. 990.40 in 2026. Similarly, the US Dollar value declined by USD 0.34 from USD 3.46 to USD 3.12.\n\nIn the Low Grown category, which continues to command the highest average price among the elevation categories, the Rupee value remained largely stable, declining marginally by Rs.3.79, from Rs. 1,228.85 in 2025 to Rs.1,225.06 in 2026. However, the US Dollar average declined by 0.28 from USD 4.13 to USD 3.85, reflecting a decrease in export value."
