    "chunk_text": "Deputy Health Minister invites investors to build pharmaceutical export hub in  Sri Lanka\n\nHealth and Mass Media Deputy Minister Dr. Hansaka Wijemuni has extended an open invitation to both local and international investors to utilise Sri Lanka as a strategic hub for pharmaceutical manufacturing, eyeing expansion into regional\u00a0and global markets.\n\nSpeaking at the Annual General Meeting of the Sri Lanka Pharmaceutical Manufacturers\u2019 Association, Dr. Wijemuni emphasised that establishing a robust local manufacturing footprint presents lucrative opportunities well beyond merely fulfilling the domestic healthcare needs.\n\n\u201cI would like to invite more local and international investors to consider Sri Lanka as a destination for pharmaceutical manufacturing,\u201d he stated.\n\nHe pointed out that the country\u2019s strategic positioning offers a strong launchpad, noting that \u201cthere are opportunities not only to meet the domestic demand but also to expand into regional and\n\nAcknowledging the substantial capital, advanced technology and stringent international compliance required to set up such sophisticated facilities, the government pledged to maintain a supportive and\n\nDr. Wijemuni stressed that the government authorities are focused on striking a critical balance between protecting the public funds and fostering private industry growth.\n\n\u201cOur objective is clear: we must safeguard public investment while also creating a fair, predictable environment for genuine investors,\u201d he affirmed.\n\nHe further highlighted that a sustainable local manufacturing sector must ultimately thrive on market competitiveness rather than relying entirely on protectionist measures."
