    "chunk_text": "Group profit before tax rose 31 percent to Rs.4.08 billion, despite the currency loss. Excluding the net exchange losses, pre-tax profit climbed to Rs.5.97 billion, from Rs.3.49 billion a year earlier, offering a clearer view of the improvement in the underlying earnings. The profit attributable to the shareholders, excluding the exchange losses, reached Rs.1.95 billion, reversing the adjusted loss of Rs.418 million recorded in the previous year.\n\nThe Colombo West International Terminal handled 460,840 twenty-foot equivalent units during the quarter and effectively reached full utilisation of its first-phase capacity based on its recent volume run rate. Completion and operationalisation of the full terminal remain scheduled for December.\n\nRetail continued to generate the largest divisional EBITDA at Rs.6.16 billion; however, this was 16 percent below the previous year, as the lower profitability from the vehicle business outweighed growth at the Keells supermarkets."
