    "chunk_text": "But that doesn\u2019t mean that people should be aware of all languages in a country. India has 22 official languages, 121 major languages and over 19,000 mother tongues and dialects. In Sri Lanka, the Sinhalese dialect differs in different regions of the country and this is the same when it comes to Tamil as well. The Tamil dialect spoken by the Malaiyaha community is different to that spoken in Jaffna. The Tamil dialect in the Eastern province is even more different. This is the beauty of this culturally diverse nation.\n\nThe Colombo Literary Festival has initiated the first step in introducing an event that\u2019s affordable for people. Perhaps the next step should be its expansion to different locations of the country. It may be a challenge to empower people to read books in this era of social media and AI. But these initiatives would at least allow people to appreciate and take pride in the country\u2019s long lost literary heritage.\n\n\u2018Your Thought\u2019 is a space, a right of the readers to support or contradict and discuss the issues highlighted in the editorial and other articles in the editorial and op-ed pages. Designed as the reader\u2019s editorial; our readers can send in their writings, with a word count not exceeding 200, to \u2018Your Thought\u2019, Daily Mirror Political Features Desk, No 8, Hunupitiya Cross Road, Colombo 2 or email to [email\u00a0protected]"
