    "chunk_text": "Also, Bills or provisions of Bills that are certified by the Cabinet or determined by the Supreme Court as requiring the approval of the people, and those matters which, in the opinion of the President, are of national importance have to be put to the people through a referendum. The president too,\u00a0 can get a Bill that is already rejected by Parliament passed through a referendum.\n\nOpposition parties are not really concerned about the independence of the judiciary, given their track record. The United National Party (UNP) government led by leaders like J.R. Jayewardene, Ranasinghe Premadasa and Ranil Wickremesinghe once in the 1980s justified\u00a0 attacks by thugs on houses of Apex Court Judges who gave a judgement against their government. President Mahinda Rajapaksa ignored a Supreme Court ruling on oil prices and appointed superior court judges without the approval of the Constitutional Council in 2006. He used his party\u2019s majority in Parliament to impeach Chief Justice Shirani Bandaranayake in 2013 for not giving judgements favourable to him.\n\nGotabaya Rajapaksa facilitated his brother Basil to contest elections while being a US citizen through the 20th Amendment. President Ranil Wickremesinghe ignored the Supreme Court order to hold local government elections in 2023. His government attempted to summon the judges who gave this ruling before the Privilege Committee of the Parliament. He called a ruling by the Supreme Court \u201cjudicial cannibalism.\u201d\n\nMinister Jayatissa says that a Parliamentary subcommittee consisting of members of all parties in the House, including the current opposition parties,\u00a0 had recommended the extension of judges\u2019 retirement age in 2016.\n\nHence, the Opposition parties are not genuinely committed to the independence of the judiciary. They are only attempting to build a public opinion against the government using the extension of the judges\u2019 retirement age."
