    "chunk_text": "Subsequently, I entered the national phase by filing patent applications in the United States (19/581,052), Australia (P03937AU1), the United Kingdom (GB2612074.1), India (202617054614), and China (202480068343.3).\n\nBefore commencing this research, I obtained ethical approval from the Ethics Review Committee of the Faculty of Medicine, University of Kelaniya, Ragama.\n\nQWhat achievements have you received so far with this invention?\n\nThe first came in January 2024, when I was invited to present this novel concept as an invited speaker at the Annual Scientific Congress of the College of Anaesthesiologists and Intensivists of Sri Lanka, held in Colombo.\n\nLater, in September 2024, this research was selected for an oral presentation at the European Airway Management Society (EAMS) Annual Congress in Istanbul, T\u00fcrkiye. It was a great honour to present my research before some of the world\u2019s leading airway management experts and to receive their positive feedback. In particular, I would like to acknowledge the encouraging comments I received from Professor Tim Cook, a consultant anaesthetist from the United Kingdom.\n\nIn 2025, I was also allowed to present this invention at the World Airway Management Meeting (WAMM) in Florence, Italy. During the meeting, I received encouraging feedback from Professor Patrick Olomu, a consultant anaesthetist from the United States. One of the most memorable milestones of my professional career was meeting Professor Archie Brain, the British anaesthetist who invented the Laryngeal Mask Airway (LMA)\u2014one of the most revolutionary invention in modern anaesthesia\u2014and having the opportunity to discuss my invention with him in person."
