    "chunk_size_bytes": 1951,
    "chunk_text": "COYLE and Indian Chamber of Commerce sign MoU to strengthen business relations\n\nCOYLE Chairman Suren Chandraratna (right) and ICC-TN Chairman Shivkumar Eashwaran (left)\u00a0 with Indian High Commissioner Santosh Jha following the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding\n\nCOYLE members and ICC-TN representatives after the sighing of the MoU\n\nThe Chamber of Lankan Entrepreneurs (COYLE) and the Indian Chamber of Commerce (ICC) formalised a strategic partnership with the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) in Colombo, reinforcing their shared commitment to expanding bilateral trade, investment, and business collaboration.\n\nThe agreement was signed by COYLE Chairman Suren Chandraratna and\u00a0 Indian Chamber of Commerce \u2013 Tamil Nadu Chairman Shivkumar Eashwaran in the presence of business leaders from both countries as part of the India\u2013Sri Lanka Bilateral Trade Delegation.\n\nThe MoU establishes a practical framework for closer cooperation between the two chambers, creating new opportunities for entrepreneurs and businesses through trade promotion, investment facilitation, business networking, and knowledge exchange. It reflects the shared vision of both organisations to strengthen economic ties and support sustainable private sector growth.\n\nCOYLE Chairman Suren Chandraratna said the partnership marks another important milestone in strengthening regional business cooperation. \u201cThis MoU is about turning relationships into results. It brings together India\u2019s manufacturing strength and market scale with Sri Lanka\u2019s strategic location, agility and innovation. Together, COYLE and the Indian Chamber of Commerce will create practical opportunities for our members through business matchmaking, trade missions, investment partnerships and the exchange of expertise. We believe sustainable growth is built on collaboration, and this partnership is designed to create lasting value for entrepreneurs in both countries.\u201d"
