    "chunk_text": "Fleet of 104 Metro buses arrives\n\nColombo, July 30 (Daily Mirror) - Another fleet of 104 new buses for Metro Transit, a subsidiary of the Sri Lanka Transport Board (SLTB), has arrived in the country.\n\nAccording to officials, the new fleet is expected to enhance the efficiency and quality of public transport services across Sri Lanka.\n\nThey had announced earlier that the buses will be equipped with card-based electronic fare payment systems and are expected to be deployed for passenger services by September 20.\n\nGovt. to introduce Metro Bus Unit with 100 comfortable, low-entry buses\n\nMetro bus service to become new vibe in public transport: Deputy Minister"
