    "md5": "7bc8eccff4ca3225bcd5b0bb8cec75c9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 820,
    "chunk_text": "Two killed after cab crashes against tree in Vavuniya\n\nColombo, July 30 (Daily Mirror) - Two persons were killed after a cab transporting vegetables crashed against a tree in the Kanagarayankulam area along the Jaffna\u2013Kandy main road in Vavuniya early today, police said.\n\nPolice said the accident occurred when the cab, which was travelling from Dambulla to Jaffna carrying a load of vegetables, veered off the road and collided against a roadside tree.\n\nPreliminary investigations suggest that the driver may have fallen asleep at the wheel, causing the vehicle to lose control.\n\nThe injured victims were admitted to the Mankulam Hospital, where they later succumbed to their injuries.\n\nThe bodies have been transferred to the Vavuniya Hospital mortuary, where post-mortem examinations are scheduled to be conducted."
