    "chunk_text": "Wendy\u2019s joins Sri Lanka\u2019s fast-food race through JKH\n\nColombo, July 30 (Daily Mirror) - John Keells Holdings PLC (JKH) will bring the global fast-food chain Wendy\u2019s to Sri Lanka, marking the diversified conglomerate\u2019s entry into the quick-service restaurant segment.\n\nThe first Wendy\u2019s outlet is expected to open by December 2026, with the franchise agreements and other preliminary work already completed.\n\n\u201cJKH will diversify its consumer foods portfolio into Sri Lanka\u2019s quick service restaurant segment through the rollout of the internationally recognised Wendy\u2019s brand,\u201d JKH Chairperson Krishan Balendra said in the group\u2019s latest quarterly release.\n\nJKH is yet to disclose the location of the first outlet, the investment involved or the number of restaurants planned under the rollout.\n\nThe group\u2019s consumer foods segment reported earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortisation of Rs.1.52 billion for the quarter ended June 2026, up 21 percent, from Rs.1.26 billion a year earlier.\n\nThe segment\u2019s performance was supported by a strong volume growth, with the beverage volumes rising 27 percent and confectionery volumes increasing 13 percent during the quarter."
