    "chunk_size_bytes": 1950,
    "chunk_text": "Death toll from Japan\u2019s earthquake rises to 30\n\neuro news - Residents of Japan\u2019s southwestern prefecture of Kumamoto were struggling to get their lives back to normal on Thursday, two days after a powerful 7.1 magnitude earthquake set off an explosion at a mall, toppled a factory chimney and flattened homes, killing at least 30 people in the process, as search and rescue efforts continue.\n\nTime was running out to find survivors, as rescuers continued to work in Kumamoto on Japan \u2019s southern main island of Kyushu, where the powerful tremor hit on Tuesday.\n\nThe number of those missing was unclear. The quake left at least 63 people injured, five of them seriously, according to representatives of Kumamoto\u2019s prefectural government.\n\nSurvivors spoke about coming home and desperately pulling family members out of the wreckage. Some had suffered injuries and were rushed to the hospital.\n\nThousands of people spent another night at evacuation centres set up throughout the area in gymnasiums and other big spaces. Some homes were still without water or electricity, while others were simply afraid to go back.\n\nAlthough Japan boasts strict building codes because of the frequency of quakes, many of them exceeding 7 magnitude, some homes in the area are in the older style of Japanese housing, making them relatively fragile to tremors.\n\nThe most serious damage was at the Aeon Mall shopping centre in the town of Kashima, which was bustling with thousands of people when the quake struck in the late afternoon on Tuesday local time.\n\nThe company said some 3,000 customers were evacuated to a parking lot before the explosion happened in another part of the mall, where some people were still working. The mall\u2019s second floor collapsed, trapping people underneath the rubble.\n\nAs of early Thursday, six people were confirmed to have died at the mall site among the 11 people pulled out of the debris, according to officials in Kumamoto."
