    "chunk_text": "The company said some 3,000 customers were evacuated to a parking lot before the explosion happened in another part of the mall, where some people were still working. The mall\u2019s second floor collapsed, trapping people underneath the rubble.\n\nAs of early Thursday, six people were confirmed to have died at the mall site among the 11 people pulled out of the debris, according to officials in Kumamoto.\n\nIn the Yatsushiro area, where a chimney collapsed at a Nippon Paper Industries factory, 10 people were rescued, but eight others died, and one remained unaccounted for.\n\nNearly 23,000 homes were still without electricity and more than 10,000 people were staying in the roughly 400 shelters set up by the government, where power sources were being added to provide air conditioning as a dire heatwave grips parts of the country."
