    "chunk_text": "CSE begins week on positive note as buying interest supports market gains\n\nThe Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE) commenced the week on a positive note on 28th July 2026, with both benchmark indices closing higher as improved investor sentiment and selective buying in fundamentally strong counters supported the market. Favorable global and domestic developments helped sustain buying interest throughout the session, enabling the market to maintain its upward momentum despite moderate overall trading activity.\n\nThe All Share Price Index (ASPI) gained 41.92 points (+0.20%) to close at 21,229.14, while the S&P SL20 Index advanced 12.66 points (+0.21%) to 5,961.40. Total market turnover amounted to LKR 2.02 Bn, with 87.47 Mn shares changing hands during the session. Market breadth remained positive, recording 116 gainers against 78 decliners, reflecting healthy buying interest across the broader market.\n\nThe Capital Goods sector emerged as the largest contributor to market turnover, recording LKR 1.04 Bn with 43.11 Mn shares traded. RIL.N dominated sector activity, generating LKR 1.03 Bn in turnover with 42.91 Mn shares traded. Meanwhile, crossings accounted for LKR 1.19 Bn, representing 58.82% of total market turnover. The largest crossing was recorded in RIL.N, totaling LKR 1.02 Bn involving 42.50 Mn shares traded.\n\nOn the positive side, DOCK.N contributed the most to the ASPI, adding 7.45 points, followed by JKH.N, COMB.N, ACL.N, and NDB.N. On the downside, SAMP.N was the largest negative contributor, weighing on the index by 5.89 points, while GRAN.N, TKYO.N, WIND.N, and NTB.N also recorded declines."
