    "chunk_size_bytes": 1940,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s energy future takes centre stage at Solar + Storage Forum 2026\n\nGoodWe ranked as Sri Lanka\u2019s No. 1 rooftop solar storage brand\n\nGoodWe, a world-leading PV inverter manufacturer and smart energy solutions provider, in collaboration with the Sri Lanka Sustainable Energy Authority (SLSEA), successfully hosted Solar + Storage Forum 2026, at Marino Beach, Colombo.\n\nThe event drew over 400 attendees from across Sri Lanka\u2019s renewable energy sector, reflecting strong interest in GoodWe\u2019s storage solutions and the country\u2019s growing push towards solar and battery energy adoption.\n\nThe attendees included Energy Minister Anura Karunathilaka, Energy Ministry Secretary G.M.R.D. Aponsu and SLSEA Chairman Prof. Wijendra J. Bandara, alongside the senior government officials and industry leaders.\n\nSpeaking at the event, Karunathilaka said, \u201cSri Lanka\u2019s clean energy future depends on a strong collaboration between the government, industry and technology leaders. Forums such as this play a vital role in fostering innovation, attracting investment and accelerating the deployment of renewable energy solutions.\u201d\n\nAponsu added, \u201cAs Sri Lanka continues to increase the share of renewable energy in its generation mix, energy storage technologies and grid modernisation will become critical enablers.\u201d\n\nGoodWe Sales Head APAC James Hou said, \u201cAs the No. 1 rooftop solar storage supplier in the residential and C&I markets, GoodWe is committed to supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s clean energy transition and the role of solar and storage in achieving the country\u2019s renewable energy goals.\u201d\n\nGoodWe has been trusted in Sri Lanka for 13 years, delivering reliable products, localised service and continuous innovation. To better serve the customers in Sri Lanka, GoodWe has established a nationwide localised service network and an extensive dealer network; it helps ensure timely and efficient support for the customers."
  },
