    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "1db292125a81fa508ee7e60431ba3328",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1900,
    "chunk_text": "ASUS brings on-device AI to  Sri Lanka\u2019s corporate laptop market\n\nFrom left: Dinesh, Rex and Medanka Mapalagama - Pix by Kithsiri de Mel\n\nASUS yesterday expanded its business laptop portfolio in Sri Lanka, launching its premium ExpertBook Ultra alongside new B and P series models as companies increasingly look to equip employees with artificial intelligence-enabled devices.\n\nThe line-up includes the ExpertBook Ultra and the ExpertBook P5, B5, P3 and B3 models. ASUS is positioning the devices for organisations ranging from growing businesses to large enterprises, with a focus on portability, on-device AI processing, security and after-sales support.\n\nAt the top of the range, the 14-inch ExpertBook Ultra is powered by up to an Intel Core Ultra X9 Series 3 processor and features a neural processing unit capable of delivering up to 50 trillion operations per second, or TOPS. This allows certain AI workloads to be processed directly on the device, reducing reliance on cloud-based computing.\n\nStarting at 0.99 kilograms and measuring 10.9 millimetres in thickness, the laptop is aimed primarily at senior executives and professionals who travel frequently. Its chassis is made from a magnesium-aluminium alloy used in aerospace and motor-racing applications, while ASUS says the device meets military-grade durability standards.\n\nThe ExpertBook Ultra also features a 14-inch, 3K touch screen OLED display with a 120Hz refresh rate and brightness of up to 1,400 nits. A six-speaker Dolby Atmos system is designed to support virtual meetings, presentations and multimedia use.\n\nIts AI-supported features include background-noise cancellation, camera enhancements and ASUS ExpertMeet, which is intended to improve online collaboration. Security features include biometric authentication, Microsoft Pluton integration and hardware-level protection for the laptop\u2019s basic input-output system."
  },
