    "chunk_text": "Its AI-supported features include background-noise cancellation, camera enhancements and ASUS ExpertMeet, which is intended to improve online collaboration. Security features include biometric authentication, Microsoft Pluton integration and hardware-level protection for the laptop\u2019s basic input-output system.\n\nAlongside the flagship model, the expanded B and P series will be offered in 14-inch and 16-inch configurations. Depending on the model, buyers can select Intel Core Ultra Series 3 processors, up to 64GB of DDR5 memory and dual solid-state drive storage.\n\nThe broader range allows companies to deploy different specifications across their workforce while maintaining a common set of security, connectivity and device-management features. This could appeal to businesses seeking to introduce AI-capable computers without purchasing flagship devices for every employee.\n\n\u201cAs Sri Lanka accelerates into an AI-first era, we are proud to deliver a complete \u2018Power of Choice\u2019 across our new lineup powered by Intel Core Ultra Series 3 processors,\u201d ASUS Asia-Pacific Head of Commercial PCs Rex Lee said.\n\nHe said the company aimed to provide Sri Lankan organisations with devices capable of supporting secure, on-device AI collaboration while combining performance with enterprise security and local support.\n\nASUS is also attempting to differentiate the range through its commercial service package. Business customers receive a dedicated helpline operating from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m. from Monday to Saturday, onsite support and a standard three-year international warranty covering 90 countries."
