    "chunk_size_bytes": 1922,
    "chunk_text": "Bank of Ceylon once again recognised  as Sri Lanka\u2019s Most Valuable Brand 2026\n\nBank of Ceylon Chairman Kavinda de Zoysa,\u00a0General Manager/CEO Y. A. Jayathilaka\n\nBank of Ceylon (BOC) has once again been recognised as Sri Lanka\u2019s Most Valuable Brand 2026 by Brand Finance Lanka, reaffirming its position as the country\u2019s most valuable brand. With a brand value of Rs. 65.5 billion, reflecting a 14.1% year-on-year growth, this prestigious recognition highlights the enduring confidence, trust and loyalty that generations of Sri Lankans continue to place in Bank of Ceylon.\n\nFurther strengthening this achievement, Bank of Ceylon\u2019s Brand Strength Rating has been upgraded to AAA, reflecting the Bank\u2019s strong brand equity, customer relationships, market leadership and consistent ability to deliver value through innovation, responsible banking and meaningful engagement with society.\n\nBrand Finance Lanka, a subsidiary of Brand Finance UK, the world\u2019s leading independent brand valuation and strategy consultancy, evaluates leading brands annually through a comprehensive methodology built on three core pillars: Brand Investment, Brand Equity and Brand Performance. The rankings are supported by detailed financial analysis and independent consumer research, providing a transparent and evidence-based assessment of brand value, strength and reputation.\n\nBeing recognised as Sri Lanka\u2019s Most Valuable Brand is a result of far more than financial performance alone. Bank of Ceylon\u2019s success is driven by its strategic focus on customer engagement, impactful brand communication, exceptional service delivery, digital transformation, corporate social responsibility, sustainability initiatives and its ability to continuously strengthen public confidence. Through these efforts, BOC has created a powerful connection with Sri Lankans across generations while continuing to contribute to national development."
