    "chunk_text": "Net fee and commission income rose 20.9 percent to Rs.4.65 billion, while trading gains increased nearly sixfold to Rs.1.12 billion. Total operating income grew 13.3 percent to Rs.25.54 billion.\n\nOperating expenses rose slightly faster at 14.2 percent to Rs.12.28 billion, pushing the cost-to-income ratio to 48.09 percent from 44.52 percent.\n\nAsset quality improved on a gross basis, with the Stage 3 impaired-loan ratio declining to 6.97 percent from 7.54 percent. The net Stage 3 ratio remained at 1.03 percent, while provision coverage eased to 85.26 percent from 86.33 percent.\n\nDespite higher earnings, return on equity declined to 14.74 percent from 15.89 percent and pre-tax return on assets fell to 1.98 percent from 2.31 percent.\n\nCapital buffers also narrowed. The common equity Tier I ratio declined to 10.91 percent from 12.39 percent, while the total capital ratio fell to 15.56 percent from 17.89 percent. Both remained above regulatory minimums. The bank redeemed Rs.6 billion in Tier II debentures in April.\n\nFair-value losses on debt investments reduced total comprehensive income by 29.4 percent to Rs.5.09 billion, even as reported profit increased.\n\nShareholders\u2019 equity rose 3.1 percent from December to Rs.84.46 billion, while net asset value per share increased to Rs.132.87 from Rs.128.87."
