    "md5": "78c2d73211ae9c9819fa3449ccbe349f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1014,
    "chunk_text": "Odel resumes Colombo 7 mall construction\n\nOdel PLC has resumed construction of the first phase of its long-delayed mall project in Colombo 7, with completion expected within the next one-and-a-half to two years.\n\nIn a disclosure to the Colombo Stock Exchange, the Softlogic Holdings subsidiary said the mixed-use development had originally comprised two zones, but the project plan had since been revised to prioritise the completion of Zone 1.\n\n\u201cConstruction work of Zone 1 has recommenced and is progressing as at date,\u201d the company said.\n\nOdel did not disclose the current level of construction completed, the revised investment value or an expected opening date for the development.\n\nZone 2, comprising a 100-perch block of land, will remain available for future development. The company provided no timeline or further details for that phase.\n\nOdel said the disclosure was made to clarify the current status of the project and address speculative or inaccurate representations surrounding the development."
