    "chunk_size_bytes": 2020,
    "chunk_text": "A three\u2011day pause in the fighting raised hopes for peace this week. But it was not to be. Iran launched what the US now calls a \u201csurprise attack\u201d on American military targets in Jordan. An angry Trump vowed a fitting response, saying: \u201cWe are going to beat the f**king sh*t out of them. We\u2019ll be hitting them hard. They\u2019re going to get a beating.\u201d\n\nOn Wednesday night, several Iranian islands and towns in the south were hit hard. The attacks were described as the retaliation for Iran\u2019s surprise strike on US bases in Jordan. They coincided with Trump\u2019s meeting with Benjamin Netanyahu, the Israeli prime minister and architect of the Iran war. Few details of what the two leaders discussed are known. But it is no secret that Israel is pleased with the way the US is pummeling Iran while turning a blind eye to the Zionist state\u2019s atrocities in Lebanon and Gaza, despite US\u2011brokered ceasefires in both theatres.\n\nOutside the war zone, the battered poor ask when this war of attrition will end. America\u2019s playboy octogenarian president, Donald Trump\u2014a billionaire to boot\u2014is not known to have experienced hunger. He slashes funding for poverty\u2011alleviation programmes yet calls on Congress to approve US$1.5 trillion, money enough to eradicate global hunger five times over.\n\nTo the dismay of the world\u2019s poor, Iran is also matching US unwillingness to compromise in kind. It unleashes its limited military resources against US targets and ships that defy its orders, drawing more American attacks, in a strategy seen as an attempt to exhaust US missile and drone stocks. Recent US media reports indicated that US ammunition reserves were fast depleting. Such reports have given Iranians reason to be cautious about any lull in attacks and to doubt US intentions. They theorise that Washington\u2019s peace offers are merely a ruse to replenish its stocks and strike even harder at Iranian targets.\n\nNo wonder both the US and Iran say this war is not an eye for an eye but a head for an eye."
