    "chunk_size_bytes": 1817,
    "chunk_text": "To the dismay of the world\u2019s poor, Iran is also matching US unwillingness to compromise in kind. It unleashes its limited military resources against US targets and ships that defy its orders, drawing more American attacks, in a strategy seen as an attempt to exhaust US missile and drone stocks. Recent US media reports indicated that US ammunition reserves were fast depleting. Such reports have given Iranians reason to be cautious about any lull in attacks and to doubt US intentions. They theorise that Washington\u2019s peace offers are merely a ruse to replenish its stocks and strike even harder at Iranian targets.\n\nNo wonder both the US and Iran say this war is not an eye for an eye but a head for an eye.\n\nWhat is required now is diplomacy at a global level, since those affected by Washington\u2019s illegal war are not only Iran and the Gulf states but also the wider world\u2014particularly developing nations that depend on oil imports, tourism, and markets for their meagre exports. Britain\u2019s recent proposal for an international conference to discuss safeguarding ships in the Strait of Hormuz attracted only a few takers.\n\nChina, however, could assume leadership in convening an international peace conference aimed at finding a diplomatic solution to the conflict, even though it had earlier indicated that it did not wish to be a guarantor of peace in any ceasefire deal. After all, didn\u2019t China spring a diplomatic surprise by mediating an end to hostilities between Saudi Arabia and Iran in 2023?\n\nSuch a China-led international diplomatic effort would be in consonance with President Xi Jinping\u2019s Global Governance Initiative (GGI), built on new pancha seela or five core concepts: sovereign equality, the international rule of law, multilateralism, a people\u2011centred approach, and real action."
