    "md5": "87de2d28f24fa1efacece33d3fb462fd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1972,
    "chunk_text": "Similarly, those who tried to interfere with the judiciary have not survived politically. It is the same story with Mr. Mahinda Rajapaksa. Every time a person in government attempts to interfere with the judiciary, they have not survived politically.\n\nNo, I do not know because, so far, they have not asked me for any explanation or taken any action against me. There has been no official party decision.\n\nThey cannot find fault with me because they have not taken a formal decision. If they take a decision and say that I have violated party discipline by not following it, then they can find fault with me.\n\nI also have to consider whether I can remain in the party if the party takes such a decision. But that has not happened so far.\n\nQ You mentioned that a member of the NPP Politburo or the JVP contacted you. Is it possible for you to name him?\n\nIt is K.D. Lal Kantha (Minister of Agriculture). I sent him a letter. He is based in the Kandy area and is almost in charge of that area.\n\nHe is from the JVP, not from the NPP. He is the person who spoke to me and asked me to keep quiet.\n\nThey did it politely because they have treated me very well personally. They respect me so much that sometimes it is embarrassing. I have no personal problem with them at all.\n\nThis is a matter of principle. What I strongly believe is that, to live in a civilised society, there must be the rule of law. The rule of law can prevail only if there is an independent judiciary.\n\nI want to live in a civilised society. I feel that we are too old, but the future generation should also have the right to live in a civilised society as responsible citizens. We have enjoyed that privilege for so long.\n\nWe do not want, at this stage of our lives, to become a party responsible for destroying that. Therefore, I have to do whatever is possible on my part to protect it.\n\nQ So now, do you actually think the government will back down because a lot of pressure is being brought against it?"
