    "chunk_size_bytes": 1784,
    "chunk_text": "City of Dreams adds Scope Cinemas as flagship entertainment anchor\n\nScope Cinemas will open a five-screen multiplex at The Shoppes at City of Dreams Sri Lanka before the end of this year, becoming a flagship attraction in the integrated development\u2019s next phase of retail and entertainment expansion.\n\nThe multiplex, scheduled to open on Level 10, will feature next-generation cinema technology alongside two VIP cinema halls, each with a private lobby and a dedicated gourmet dining offering.\n\nThe addition is expected to strengthen the entertainment component of The Shoppes, which is approaching its first anniversary after opening in August 2025.\n\nLevels 7 and 8 of the retail complex are currently operational. The waterfront ground floor and Levels 9 and 10 are due to open under the development\u2019s phased rollout, adding new retail, dining and entertainment offerings.\n\nThe upcoming floors will also house a food court, expanded entertainment facilities and a nightlife destination, as City of Dreams seeks to position the complex as a broader leisure destination rather than a conventional shopping centre.\n\n\u201cThe Shoppes was always envisioned as more than a retail destination. It was designed to bring together shopping, dining and entertainment in a way that encourages people to stay longer, return more often and discover something new with every visit,\u201d Cinnamon Life at City of Dreams Sri Lanka Senior Vice President for Colombo Hotels and General Manager Kamal Munasinghe said.\n\nHe described the partnership with Scope Cinemas as a significant step in the development\u2019s efforts to expand its lifestyle and entertainment offering.\n\nThe cinema operator said the multiplex would combine new screening technology with premium hospitality and curated entertainment."
