    "md5": "6429b32915091e0b3aee897391bb98c3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1850,
    "chunk_text": "SLCBCC partners Intex-InMac Sri Lanka 2026\n\nInitiative aims to strengthen Sri Lanka\u2013China textile trade and industry collaboration\n\nThe Sri Lanka-China Business Cooperation Council (SLCBCC) has partnered with Intex-InMac Sri Lanka 2026, South Asia\u2019s premier international textile sourcing and garment technology platform, to further strengthen bilateral trade, sourcing partnerships, investment opportunities and business collaboration between Sri Lanka, China and the global textile and apparel industry.\n\nScheduled to take place from 5 to 7 August 2026 at the BMICH, Colombo, Intex-InMac Sri Lanka 2026 will welcome over 250 domestic and international exhibitors from 15+ countries and regions, bringing together textile manufacturers, innovators, textile and garment machinery companies, buyers, industry stakeholders under one roof.\n\nThis year\u2019s edition will feature over 130 Chinese textile companies\u2014the largest-ever participation in Intex-InMac editions to date\u2014reinforcing China\u2019s pivotal role in South Asia\u2019s textile supply chain, providing Sri Lankan manufacturers direct access to China\u2019s advanced functional, recycled, and eco-friendly raw materials to meet evolving western compliance standards.\n\nThrough this strategic collaboration, SLCBCC will provide its industry members with direct access to international suppliers, emerging technologies, sourcing solutions, and high-value business networks. The Intex-InMac Shows serve as a gateway for Sri Lankan businesses to engage with Chinese enterprises showcasing their latest innovations while exploring new markets and long-term commercial partnerships.\n\nBeyond the exhibition, the partnership will facilitate curated B2B meetings, technical workshops, and high-level networking with Chinese and international enterprises seeking to expand their footprint in South Asia."
