    "md5": "9a646daf1d8d37a4c479888236960f8c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 727,
    "chunk_text": "Customs seizes Rs. 4.5 b worth of narcotics in nine months\n\nSri Lanka Customs has seized more than 396 kg of narcotics with an estimated street value of Rs. 4.5 billion in 55 raids carried out between 30 October 2025 and July 2026, as authorities intensified efforts to curb illicit drug trafficking.\n\nCustoms Spokesman Chandana Punchihewa said the seizures comprised Kush, cannabis, cocaine and methamphetamine, commonly known as Ice.\n\nHe said Customs conducted five drug detections during July alone, leading to the seizure of 25.4 kg of narcotics.\n\n\u201cDuring July 2026, we seized 25.4 kilograms of various narcotics through five detections. The drugs included Kush, cannabis, cocaine and methamphetamine,\u201d Punchihewa said."
