    "chunk_text": "Leopards roam Peradeniya Uni; Students urged to stay alert\n\nColombo, July 31 (Daily Mirror) - Students and the staff of Peradeniya University are facing the danger of leopards that roam into the campus at night from the Hanthana hill range.\n\nA calf in the livestock farm run by the Veterinary Faculty had been killed and a part of the carcass eaten by leopards in the early hours of last morning.\n\nCCTV recordings have shown how the leopard preyed on the calf.\n\nA senior official of the university said the students have been warned to be cautious when moving about in the campus after dusk."
