    "chunk_text": "Video showed crowds of people, mainly Moroccans, walking around the breakwaters at Tarajal beach onto local roads in the Spanish North African enclave, along with pictures of migrants celebrating their safe arrival.\n\nWhile the majority appeared to be young men, there were also families with women and children. \"Viva Espana!\", some shouted, according to a freelance photographer working for The Associated Press.\n\nIt did not give any details on the circumstances of the deaths, but bodies could be seen floating in the water. Dozens have died this year attempting to reach Ceuta, according to local authorities.\n\nAround 1,500 migrants reached the city by swimming across from Morocco \u200bover the past week, according to the head of Ceuta's regional government, Juan Jesus Vivas.\n\nThe scenes of people pushing across the frontier are reminiscent of the border crisis of May 2021 when more than 8,000 migrants streamed into Ceuta in just two days.\n\nThe recent influx had overwhelmed the city's \u2060reception system and left hundreds of migrants sleeping outside, Mr Vivas told local radio stations Cadena SER and Onda Cero.\n\n\"We are facing a situation \u200bof absolute humanitarian and social emergency,\" he said, warning that facilities for \u200bunaccompanied minors were operating at 2,400% capacity.\n\nMr Vivas called for the national government to declare a national emergency on grounds of national security, asking for more police and for the army to be deployed \"to guarantee the inviolability of the frontier and citizen safety\".\n\nSpain's interior ministry said the Moroccan government was \"closely cooperating\" with Spain to handle the situation, saying Moroccan police were stopping \"numerous people\" who were trying to cross the border."
