    "md5": "600f0084c08c9465fa3a9bd3e2376378",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1932,
    "chunk_text": "Sajith to host \u2019Sri Lankan Leopard Day\u2019 tomorrow\n\nColombo, July 31 (Daily Mirror) - Leader of the Opposition, Sajith Premadasa, will host the 'Sri Lankan Leopard Day 2026' tomorrow (1 Aigist) from 2.00 p.m. to 5.00 p.m. at the Opposition Leader's office in Colombo 7, bringing together leading experts, policymakers, conservationists, researchers, government institutions, civil society organisations, the private sector and young people to strengthen national efforts to conserve the Sri Lankan leopard.\n\nThe Sri Lankan leopard (Panthera pardus kotiya) is one of the country's most treasured wildlife species and an apex predator that plays a vital role in maintaining the ecological balance of Sri Lanka's forests and natural ecosystems. As an endemic subspecies found nowhere else on Earth, its conservation is a matter of national and global importance.\n\nDespite its significance, the Sri Lankan leopard continues to face growing threats from habitat fragmentation, snaring, poisoning, road fatalities, human-induced mortality and other forms of wildlife crime. Addressing these challenges requires stronger collaboration among all sectors of society, supported by sound science, effective policy, public awareness and community participation.\n\nThe Sri Lankan Leopard Day 2026 has been organised to provide a national platform for dialogue and action on leopard conservation. The programme will highlight the latest scientific knowledge, discuss practical conservation solutions and encourage stronger partnerships among all stakeholders committed to protecting Sri Lanka's unique natural heritage.\n\nA key feature of the event will be the active participation of students and young conservation leaders. By engaging directly with scientists and wildlife experts, the programme seeks to inspire a new generation of environmental stewards who will champion wildlife conservation and biodiversity protection in the years ahead."
