    "chunk_text": "French Bar Council backs BASL\u2019s concerns over proposed judicial retirement age increase\n\nColombo, July 31 (Daily Mirror) - The French National Bar Council (Conseil National des Barreaux \u2013 CNB) has adopted a resolution expressing support for the Bar Association of Sri Lanka (BASL) over concerns regarding the Government\u2019s proposal to increase the retirement age of judges.\n\nThe resolution was adopted at the CNB\u2019s Annual General Meeting held in Paris on July 3, 2026, following discussions between the CNB\u2019s Committee on European and International Affairs and a delegation from the BASL.\n\nIn its resolution, the CNB noted the BASL\u2019s concerns that extending the retirement age of serving judges could be viewed by the public as an attempt to undermine judicial independence.\n\nThe French legal body also referred to a statement issued by the Commonwealth Lawyers\u2019 Association supporting the BASL\u2019s position, while reaffirming that an independent and impartial judiciary is fundamental to protecting the rule of law.\n\nThe CNB expressed its full support for the BASL\u2019s concerns and urged Sri Lankan authorities not to proceed with proposed constitutional amendments aimed at increasing the retirement age of judges."
