    "chunk_size_bytes": 1773,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka reviews roadmap to achieve US$5 bn digital exports by 2030\n\nColombo, July 31 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka on Friday (31) reviewed a strategic roadmap aimed at increasing the country\u2019s digital export earnings to US$5 billion by 2030, during a national workshop attended by key industry stakeholders.\n\nThe workshop, titled \u201cThe Road to US$5 Billion,\u201d was held at Cinnamon Life, Colombo, to review the proposed strategy for accelerating the growth of Sri Lanka\u2019s digital industry and to build consensus on its implementation.\n\nOrganised by the Ministry of Digital Economy and GovTech Sri Lanka with technical assistance from the World Bank Group, the event brought together representatives from the public and private sectors to discuss the future direction of the country\u2019s digital economy.\n\nDeputy Minister of Digital Economy Eranga Weeraratne, Senior Presidential Adviser on Digital Economy and Chairman of GovTech Sri Lanka Dr. Hans Wijayasuriya, and International Finance Corporation (IFC) Lead Industry Specialist Victor Antonypillai delivered the opening remarks.\n\nDuring the workshop, stakeholders reviewed an assessment report on Sri Lanka\u2019s information technology industry and a proposed strategic roadmap prepared by local and international consultants from KPMG with technical support from the World Bank Group. The roadmap was further developed with inputs from the Ministry of Digital Economy, GovTech Sri Lanka and the Industry Development Committee.\n\nParticipants also took part in thematic discussions focusing on developing future-ready digital skills, strengthening innovation and support for independent professionals, expanding global market access, and improving policies, investments and infrastructure needed for sustainable growth."
