    "chunk_size_bytes": 1552,
    "chunk_text": "As Sri Lanka increasingly embraces Artificial Intelligence, the importance of inclusive and trustworthy data becomes even greater. AI systems are only as reliable as the data used to develop them. Responsible AI requires accurate, representative and unbiased data, supported by strong governance frameworks that promote fairness, transparency and accountability. When implemented responsibly, AI has the potential to improve healthcare, education, agriculture, disaster management and many other public services.\n\nDigital transformation is ultimately about people rather than technology. The true measure of success is not the number of online services or AI applications introduced, but whether they improve the lives of all citizens. Building an inclusive digital society requires collaboration between government, academia, industry and international partners to develop policies that place citizens at the centre of digital innovation.\n\nSri Lanka has an opportunity to transform today\u2019s digital challenges into tomorrow\u2019s national strengths. By investing in digital inclusion, strengthening data governance, promoting responsible AI and ensuring that no citizen is left behind, the country can build a digital future that is inclusive, resilient and trusted. As digital technologies continue to evolve, embracing inclusion will not only enhance public services but also empower every Sri Lankan to participate fully in the nation\u2019s digital journey.\n\nDr. Surani Tissera is a Senior Lecturer at the Department of Computer Science, University of"
