    "chunk_size_bytes": 1926,
    "chunk_text": "Colombo Dockyard marks 52 years with return to quarterly profitability\n\nColombo Dockyard PLC (CSE: DOCK) has recorded a significant financial turnaround for the three months ended 30 June 2026, returning to quarterly profitability following an extended period of losses.The achievement comes as Colombo Dockyard prepares to mark its 52nd anniversary on 1 August 2026, providing a significant milestone in the company\u2019s ongoing transformation and renewed strategic direction following its collaboration with parent company Mazagon Dock Shipbuilders Limited.\n\nThe Group recorded a profit after tax of Rs. 80.2 million for the quarter, reversing the Rs. 813.4 million loss reported during the corresponding period of 2025. Profit attributable to the owners of the company amounted to Rs. 86.3 million, while earnings per share improved to Rs. 0.22 from a restated loss per share of Rs. 3.51 during the corresponding period of the previous year.\n\nDespite Group revenue declining by 6.8% to Rs. 5.84 billion during the quarter, improved cost efficiencies supported a substantial increase in profitability. Cost of sales declined by 21.8% to Rs. 4.63 billion, enabling gross profit to increase by 250.7% to Rs. 1.21 billion. The Group\u2019s gross profit margin consequently improved to approximately 20.7%, compared with 5.5% during the corresponding period of the previous year.\n\nNet finance expenses also declined by 63.8% to Rs. 188.2 million, compared with Rs. 520 million in the corresponding quarter, reflecting the benefits of the company\u2019s strengthened financial position and reduced financing burden.\n\nShip repairing emerged as the principal contributor to the improved performance. Revenue from the segment increased by 48.4% to Rs. 3.95 billion, from Rs. 2.66 billion in the corresponding quarter. The segment result at gross profit level more than doubled to Rs. 1.46 billion, compared with Rs. 727 million previously."
  },
