    "md5": "52566fb25c21c6088e7a718e85b37ad3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1890,
    "chunk_text": "Ship repairing emerged as the principal contributor to the improved performance. Revenue from the segment increased by 48.4% to Rs. 3.95 billion, from Rs. 2.66 billion in the corresponding quarter. The segment result at gross profit level more than doubled to Rs. 1.46 billion, compared with Rs. 727 million previously.\n\nCommenting on the performance, Thimira S. Godakumbura, Managing Director/CEO of Colombo Dockyard PLC, said, \u201cReturning to quarterly profitability as we mark 52 years of operations represents an important milestone for Colombo Dockyard. The result reflects the commitment of our employees, the strengthening of our ship repair operations, disciplined cost management and the reduction of our financing burden. It also demonstrates the early progress being made through our strategic collaboration with Mazagon Dock Shipbuilders Limited.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhile we recognise that further work remains, particularly in strengthening our shipbuilding portfolio and improving working capital efficiency, this performance provides greater confidence in the direction of the company. Our focus will remain on building a more resilient, competitive and financially sustainable Colombo Dockyard.\u201d\n\nThe company also strengthened its balance sheet during the period. Total Group equity stood at Rs. 15.59 billion as at 30 June 2026, compared with Rs. 4.07 billion as at 30th June 2025, while stated capital increased to Rs. 13.65 billion. Total assets amounted to Rs. 42.58 billion, with cash and cash equivalents reaching Rs. 8.48 billion.\n\nMazagon Dock Shipbuilders Limited presently holds a 51% shareholding in Colombo Dockyard. The company has also aligned its financial year with its parent company, with the current reporting year commencing on 1 April 2026. Accordingly, the results for the three months ended 30 June represent the first quarter under the revised reporting cycle."
