    "md5": "043d273e78b2ac019f09c65942277e61",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1718,
    "chunk_text": "Smart Quest enters Maldives as part of regional expansion\n\nFrom left \u2013 Smart Quest Director Anil Bandara, The Mechanism Maldives Director Tremayne Pereira, Smart Quest Founder Andrea Jayatilleka and Smart Quest Chief Operating Officer Oshana Dias\n\nSri Lankan leadership development and coaching company Smart Quest has expanded into the Maldives, marking its first overseas venture as the company celebrates 20 years in operation.\n\nThe newly established Smart Quest Coaching and Consulting (Pvt) Ltd Maldives will offer leadership training, professional coaching certification, executive and team coaching, and human resources consultancy services to organisations and professionals in the Maldivian market.\n\nThe Maldives operation will introduce Smart Quest\u2019s established leadership and coaching programmes, including Leading with Impact, an International Coaching Federation Level 1-accredited leadership programme designed to help managers adopt practical coaching skills in the workplace. Participants will receive 16 hours of professional coach training towards the Certified Trained Coaching Leader credential. The programme is intended for business leaders, managers and professionals seeking to strengthen communication, employee engagement and team performance.\n\nSmart Quest Maldives will also provide access to the professional coaching certification programmes offered through Coach Masters Academy. These online programmes provide pathwayto International Coach federation (ICF) credentialing from Associate certified coach (ACC) to Professional certified coach (PCC) to master certified coach (MCC), Certified Coach credential and a Graduate Diploma in Professional Coaching and Leadership Development."
  },
