    "md5": "eb5db7f349dcbfaadc085714d9c14dc7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1835,
    "chunk_text": "People\u2019s Bank unveils \u2018A Gallery in the Bank\u2019 documentary\n\nPresentation of tokens of appreciation to Ismeth Raheem and Nadine David.\n\nPresentation of tokens of appreciation to Senaka Senanayake and\u00a0 B.Wimalaratne.\n\nPeople\u2019s Bank recently held the special screening of \u2018A Gallery in the Bank\u2019 \u2013 Priceless Treasures of People\u2019s Bank, a documentary that showcases the unique and culturally significant artworks displayed at the lobbies of the Bank\u2019s Old and New Head Office Buildings in Colombo 02. The screening was held at People\u2019s Tower, the Bank\u2019s new Head Office in Colombo 02.\n\nThe documentary explores 12 rare and remarkable works of art from the People\u2019s Bank collection, uncovering the stories behind each masterpiece, their historical significance, artistic value, and the enduring legacy they represent. Through this production, the Bank has taken a significant step towards documenting and preserving a valuable part of Sri Lanka\u2019s artistic heritage.\n\nCreated by some of Sri Lanka\u2019s most celebrated artists, including George Keyt, Pushpananda Weerasinghe, Senaka Senanayake, Wimal de Silva, Jayantha Premachandra, Nadine David, Yasantha Boange, B. Wimalaratne, Richard Gabriel, Upasiri and Ismeth Raheem, these extraordinary artworks reflect the richness and diversity of Sri Lanka\u2019s cultural identity.\n\nThese masterpieces form an irreplaceable part of the nation\u2019s artistic legacy, standing as silent witnesses to an important era in Sri Lanka\u2019s history. The documentary aims to preserve these invaluable creations for future generations while introducing this hidden treasure within People\u2019s Bank to a wider audience. It celebrates the vision and creativity of the artists while highlighting People\u2019s Bank\u2019s commitment to safeguarding and promoting the country\u2019s cultural heritage."
  },
