    "md5": "4865332591bf515cfb82804f333f2b1e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1241,
    "chunk_text": "These masterpieces form an irreplaceable part of the nation\u2019s artistic legacy, standing as silent witnesses to an important era in Sri Lanka\u2019s history. The documentary aims to preserve these invaluable creations for future generations while introducing this hidden treasure within People\u2019s Bank to a wider audience. It celebrates the vision and creativity of the artists while highlighting People\u2019s Bank\u2019s commitment to safeguarding and promoting the country\u2019s cultural heritage.\n\nA special highlight of the event was the presentation of tokens of appreciation to four living artists featured in the documentary \u2014 Ismeth Raheem, Nadine David, Senaka Senanayake and B. Wimalaratne \u2014 in recognition of their outstanding contribution to Sri Lankan art and culture.\n\nAmong these distinguished artists, B. Wimalaratne holds a special place in the People\u2019s Bank collection, as he is the only artist featured in the documentary who also served as an employee of People\u2019s Bank.\n\nThe event was attended by People\u2019s Bank Chairman Prof. Narada Fernando, Chief Executive Officer/General Manager Clive Fonseka, members of the Board of Directors, Corporate and Executive Management, distinguished guests, artists and art enthusiasts."
