    "chunk_size_bytes": 1747,
    "chunk_text": "Organisers said Sri Lanka\u2019s tourism industry is now at a critical juncture as it seeks to respond to digital disruption, rapidly changing traveller expectations and increasingly stringent global sustainability requirements.\n\nThe deliberations will culminate in the publication of a Vision 2030 Whitepaper, outlining key recommendations and priorities for the industry\u2019s long-term development.\n\nThe conference agenda will focus on six strategic themes: future-ready leadership and governance; commercial strategy and business performance; innovation and digital transformation; sustainability and responsible tourism; talent development and workforce readiness; and destination competitiveness and global positioning.\n\nAttendance is open through paid registration at Rs. 25,000 per delegate. Organisers are also inviting corporate partners to participate through sponsorship packages that will provide brand visibility, direct engagement with senior decision-makers and recognition in the Vision 2030 Whitepaper.\n\nThe Institute of Hospitality, headquartered in the United Kingdom, is an internationally recognised professional body serving the hospitality, tourism and leisure sectors.\n\nIts Sri Lanka Chapter promotes professional standards, education, leadership development and industry collaboration while connecting local professionals with a global network committed to advancing excellence in hospitality.\n\nColombo Dockyard marks 52 years with return to quarterly profitability\n\nINSEE secures top honours at Sri Lankan Sustainability Awards 2026\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
