    "md5": "149e55c553a5ea54a513f5fca156b530",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1627,
    "chunk_text": "Sampath Bank enhances care at Lady Ridgeway Hospital with essential hospital upgrades\n\nSampath Bank Employees\u2019 Association Treasurer Nalin Nishantha Liyanage, Secretary Chandana Weragama and President Kalpa Jayasinghe, Chief Operating Officer Deepal De Silva, Hospital Director Consultant Dr. Pradeep Rathnasekara, Hospital Deputy Director Dr. Prabath Amarasinghe, Hospital Committee Chairman Kusal De Silva and Hospital Committee Secretary Anura Thilakasiri\n\nRecognising the importance of maintaining quality healthcare facilities for children, the Sampath Bank Employees\u2019 Union, together with the bank\u2019s Sustainability Unit, marked the union\u2019s 35th anniversary by supporting a series of essential upgrades at the Lady Ridgeway Hospital for Children, Colombo.\n\nAs Sri Lanka\u2019s national referral centre and largest free paediatric hospital, Lady Ridgeway Hospital provides specialised care to children from across the country, making continuous investment in its facilities vital to delivering timely and effective treatment.\n\nThe initiative included the refurbishment of a blood filtration machine required for patient care, the installation of air-conditioning for the Physiotherapy Unit, the erection of directional signboards across the hospital premises and the addition of child-friendly decorations to create a more welcoming environment for young patients and their families.\n\nThe event was attended by Sampath Bank Chief Operating Officer Deepal de Silva, the Sampath Bank Employees\u2019 Union President Kalpa Jayasinghe, members of the bank\u2019s staff and the hospital director together with the hospital staff."
