    "md5": "c6b0f331801f2ba854189d85a45b0c06",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1768,
    "chunk_text": "Am\u00e3na Bank marks 15 years of non-interest-based, development-focused, people-friendly banking\n\nAmana Bank, Sri Lanka\u2019s first and only licensed commercial bank operating entirely under the non-interest-based banking model, marks 15 years of operations today.\n\nSince opening its doors in 2011, the bank has made remarkable progress while successfully navigating some of the most challenging periods in the nation\u2019s recent history, driven by the growing trust, acceptance and support of its customers.\n\nToday, the bank serves over 500,000 customers through a growing network of more than 80 customer locations comprising branches and Self Banking Centres across the country. This remarkable growth reflects the bank\u2019s commitment towards enabling growth and enriching the lives of its customers through the bank\u2019s development-focused, people-friendly approach to banking.\n\nBuilding on this strong foundation, Am\u00e3na Bank has continued to deliver a robust financial performance and sustainable growth, reinforcing its position as a key player in Sri Lanka\u2019s banking sector.\n\nThe bank recently surpassed Rs.200 billion in total assets, becoming one of the fastest banks in the country to achieve this milestone. It has also consistently outpaced industry growth in both deposits and financing, while maintaining the strongest CASA ratio and being one of the lowest non-performing advances ratios in the sector.\n\nThese achievements reflect the bank\u2019s ability to pursue sustainable growth without compromising portfolio quality, supported by a robust risk management framework, sound governance and a customer-centric culture.\n\nThe bank has also maintained a consistent track record of profitability while declaring successive dividends over the last eight years."
  },
