    "md5": "787c5b6e4ab5a5fae986a0efe99c2dbe",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1917,
    "chunk_text": "FCCISL congratulates EDB on Sri Lanka\u2019s exports surpassing $ 9 b in first half of 2026\n\nThe Federation of Chambers of Commerce and Industry of Sri Lanka (FCCISL), under the leadership of its President, Dr. Rohitha Silva, together with the Board of Directors and FCCISL State Affairs Committee Chairman Ruwan De Silva in a statement extended its warmest congratulations to Sri Lanka Export Development Board Chairman and Chief Executive Officer Mangala Wijesinghe, and the entire EDB team on the significant achievement of Sri Lanka\u2019s total exports surpassing $ 9 billion during the first half of 2026.\n\nThis important national milestone reflects the dedication, commitment and visionary leadership of Mangala Wijesinghe, together with the professionalism and sustained efforts of the EDB team and the resilience, innovation and determination of Sri Lanka\u2019s export community.\n\nWijesinghe\u2019s leadership in facilitating export growth, encouraging innovation, addressing longstanding institutional challenges and guiding the sector through increasingly complex and evolving global market conditions is highly commendable. His commitment to strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s export competitiveness and creating new opportunities for local enterprises represents an important contribution to the country\u2019s economic recovery and future development.\n\nFCCISL also acknowledges with appreciation the active guidance, close cooperation and dedicated leadership extended by Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Minister Sunil Handunnetti, and Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Deputy Minister Chathuranga Abeysinghe. The Federation further recognises the valuable support, commitment and coordination provided by the Secretary to the Ministry and the entire ministry team in creating an enabling institutional and policy environment to advance Sri Lanka\u2019s export sector and broader national economic objectives."
  },
