    "chunk_text": "FCCISL also acknowledges with appreciation the active guidance, close cooperation and dedicated leadership extended by Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Minister Sunil Handunnetti, and Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Deputy Minister Chathuranga Abeysinghe. The Federation further recognises the valuable support, commitment and coordination provided by the Secretary to the Ministry and the entire ministry team in creating an enabling institutional and policy environment to advance Sri Lanka\u2019s export sector and broader national economic objectives.\n\nThe achievement of an estimated $ 9,012.24 million in combined merchandise and services exports between January and June 2026, representing an 8% year-on-year increase, provides renewed confidence in the resilience, competitiveness and future potential of Sri Lanka\u2019s export sector.\n\nDespite high energy and utility costs, significant tax burdens, and complex statutory and regulatory compliance challenges, this achievement clearly demonstrates the resilience of Sri Lanka\u2019s exporters and the considerable potential of the export sector to expand further and contribute more strongly to national economic recovery and sustainable growth.\n\nThe newly formed FCCISL State Affairs Committee, chaired by Ruwan De Silva and functioning under the guidance and leadership of FCCISL President Dr. Rohitha Silva and the Board of Directors, provides an ideal institutional platform for building closer collaboration, constructive engagement and effective cooperation between FCCISL and the Government.\n\nThrough FCCISL\u2019s extensive nationwide network of district chambers, sectoral chambers, trade associations, business associations and affiliated institutions, the State Affairs Committee seeks to facilitate structured engagement with the Export Development Board, the Ministry and other relevant public institutions."
