    "chunk_text": "Legacy of Podi Hamuduruwo continues\n\nThe late Most Venerable Galboda Siri Gnanissara Thero, whom everyone knew with love and\u00a0 respect as \u2018Podi Hamuduruwo\u2019, spent his life serving the Buddha Sasana and helping people.\n\nFor many years, he gave leadership to the Hunupitiya Gangaramaya Temple in Colombo. He made the temple a place that was close to people from every part of society. It was not only a place of worship, but also a place where people could come for help, advice and\u00a0 encouragement.\n\nPodi Hamuduruwo always paid special attention to children, young people and families facing difficulties. He supported Buddhist education, social welfare, youth development and\u00a0 many programs that helped communities throughout Sri Lanka.\n\nHe believed that the teachings of the Buddha should be practised by helping others. He brought together members of the Maha Sangha, devotees, professionals, government\u00a0 institutions, donors and volunteers to carry out this service.\n\nEducation was always very important to him. He knew that many talented children in rural\u00a0 areas had to face financial difficulties. Some children who did well in their studies could not continue their education because their families did not have enough money.\n\nPodi Hamuduruwo believed that helping these children to study was one of the best services that could be offered to the country. He wanted them to receive a proper education, build good lives and become responsible citizens.\n\nAlthough he is no longer with us, the programs he began and the people he inspired\u00a0 continue his work. The second-year commemoration of the late Most Venerable Galboda Siri Gnanissara Thero\u00a0 will be held on Sunday, 2 August 2026.\n\nThe program is being organised by the Hunupitiya Gangaramaya Temple under the guidance of Ven. (Dr.) Kirinde Assaji Thero, Chief Incumbent of the Hunupitiya Gangaramaya Temple, Colombo, and Sanghanayaka of the Colombo Nawa Koralaya under the Malwatta Chapter."
