    "chunk_text": "The mechanism itself is not mysterious. A unified Thomian Digital Campus, one platform, one shared identity, would let a lesson taught in Mount Lavinia reach a classroom in Ampara the same evening, curating the best teaching available anywhere rather than only what STC itself can produce. A free annual national aptitude program, open to every child regardless of school or district, would identify promise on reasoning rather than curriculum access, with paper-based sittings where connectivity has not reached. Every element must serve girls and boys in genuinely equal measure, a reminder Sri Lanka\u2019s own record makes plain, since girls already outperform boys in progression to higher education nationally. Selected students, Satellite Scholars, would not need to leave home; each would be paired with a Thomian Companion, an alumnus who walks alongside them not as a tutor marking work but as a companion for the journey itself, there as the child reaches for the stars, with enrichment, mentoring, and a short residential camp each year brought to the Scholar rather than the other way round, while partner schools across the island could join as regional hubs extending the network wherever the college itself cannot physically reach."
