    "chunk_text": "During more than three decades in diplomacy, I have observed governments and societies across diverse political systems and cultures. One enduring lesson stands out: the strength of a nation is measured not only by the size of its economy or the power of its institutions, but also by the confidence its citizens place in those institutions.\n\nHistory shows that every generation finds its own language of protest. The real test of leadership is not whether dissent can be prevented, but whether it can be transformed into dialogue, reform and renewed public confidence. Governments do not diminish their authority by listening to their young people; they strengthen their legitimacy by doing so.\n\n(The author is a former Sri Lankan Ambassador to the European Union, Belgium, T\u00fcrkiye, Ukraine and Saudi Arabia. He also served as Additional Secretary of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs)"
