    "chunk_text": "Minor flood warning issued for low-lying areas of Kelani River valley\n\nColombo, August 1 (Daily Mirror) - The Irrigation Department has issued a warning for minor flood situation within the next 48 hours in the low-lying areas of\u00a0the Kelani River valley.\n\nThe Department said a minor flood situation could develop in the low-lying areas of the Kelani River along the Dehiowita, Ruwanwella and Seethawaka Divisional Secretariat Divisions.\n\nIt said a significant and high-intensity rainfall has currently been recorded in the upper and middle catchment areas\n\nResidents of these areas, river users and motorists travelling through the region have been strongly urged to act with extreme caution because current forecasts indicate that future high-intensity rainfall could occur, potentially causing a sudden rise in river water levels."
