    "md5": "d72dbb01e3cd40493b748d20e21b2d0f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 828,
    "chunk_text": "Cannabis worth Rs. 106m seized in air cargo\n\nColombo, August 1 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka Customs has detected more than 10.6 kilograms of suspected cannabis-based narcotics concealed inside an air cargo consignment that arrived from Bangkok, Thailand.\n\nAccording to Customs, the consignment arrived as a gift shipment on SriLankan Airlines flight UL405 on July 24, 2026.\n\nThe shipment was examined at the TRICO UPB Warehouse on July 31 in the presence of an authorised representative, during which officers discovered polythene packets suspected to contain narcotic substances hidden inside metal containers.\n\nA final inventory revealed 10.608 kilograms (including wrapping) of cannabis-related narcotics, including marijuana, hashish and hashish oil.\n\nThe seized narcotics have an estimated street value of Rs. 106.08 million."
  },
