    "chunk_size_bytes": 775,
    "chunk_text": "Adding an academic perspective, Mr. Dilanka Karunarathne, a Master of Public Administration graduate from Tsinghua University, shared his experiences studying in China and offered insights into governance, public policy, and leadership in a rapidly changing global environment.\n\nSpeaking on the significance of the initiative, CPID stated that the workshop marked the beginning of a broader effort to empower young leaders with knowledge, international perspectives, and practical insights to contribute meaningfully to Sri Lanka's future.\n\nThe organisation said that it plans to conduct a series of similar workshops across the country in the coming months, creating more opportunities for youth engagement, leadership development, and dialogue on international cooperation."
