    "chunk_size_bytes": 846,
    "chunk_text": "President AKD congratulates Rumesh on Commonwealth Games gold\n\nColombo, August 1 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake has congratulated Sri Lankan athlete Rumesh Tharanga on winning the men\u2019s javelin gold medal at the 2026 Commonwealth Games, describing the achievement as the fulfilment of the nation\u2019s \u201cgolden dream.\u201d\n\nIn a congratulatory message, the President said, \u201cYour gold medal at the Commonwealth Games brings our nation\u2019s golden dream into reality. Congratulations, Rumesh Tharanga!\u201d\n\nTharanga ended Sri Lanka\u2019s 20-year wait for a Commonwealth Games gold medal with a championship-winning throw of 89.75 metres.\n\nHis winning effort came in a highly competitive field that included India\u2019s Olympic champion, Neeraj Chopra, marking one of the biggest achievements in Sri Lankan athletics in recent years."
