    "chunk_size_bytes": 1845,
    "chunk_text": "Angelo Mathews leads Kandy Royals at launch of new cancer drug facility project\n\nKandy Royals cricket team captain Angelo Mathews and members of the Lanka Premier League (LPL) franchise participated in a series of events organised by their primary sponsors, Kelun Lifescience and Celogen, including the foundation stone-laying ceremony for a new manufacturing complex for cancer treatment drugs.\n\nThe Kandy Royals team, one of the prominent franchises in the LPL, visited the pharmaceutical manufacturing facility located at the Pallekele Export Processing Zone on July 30, where they were welcomed by employees led by Kelun Lifescience and Celogen Chairman V. Nadarajah, Vice President Gyan Prakash Ujailan, Director I. Sathya Murthi and Managing Director Rishi Kumar Nadaraja.\n\nThe new manufacturing complex is expected to strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s pharmaceutical production capacity, particularly in the field of cancer treatment medicines.\n\nSpeaking at the event, Mathews said support from institutions such as Kelun Lifescience and Celogen provided a major boost to the development of cricket in Sri Lanka.\n\nHe stressed the importance of identifying talented players from the grassroots level, particularly through schools, and nurturing them to reach national and international standards.\n\nMathews expressed appreciation for the contribution made by private sector organisations in supporting cricket and helping create opportunities for emerging players.\n\nThe Kandy Royals are backed by Kelun Lifescience and Celogen as their primary sponsors for the ongoing LPL tournament.\n\nColombo Dockyard marks 52 years with return to quarterly profitability\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
