    "chunk_size_bytes": 2043,
    "chunk_text": "Three days later, after school, my father and I sat on our chairs behind the house. It was a beautiful evening; the sun was setting, and a fresh breeze brought us some comfort. My mother made aggala, sweet fried rice balls with leftover rice and jaggery.\n\n\u201cI want to look after my mother and also you of course.\u201d He chuckled. \u201cI do not think you need to worry about us. We are still young, and I will get a pension when we are old. That will be enough for your mother and me.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhat else? \u201cI think I will marry one day a pretty girl who is kind to you and my mother.\u201d He called out, \u201cCatherine, your son has plans to marry a pretty girl. Have you already arranged one for him?\u201d My mother laughed, and I felt bullied.\n\n\u201cDo you have a girl in your mind? I saw you smiling with that Burgher girl the other day. I will break your legs if you get entangled with her\u201d. He threatened and then smiled.\n\n\u201cI do not have a particular girl in my mind. But I would like to marry a girl who looks like Princess Anne,\u201d I confessed. \u201cWhy?\u201d he asked. I tried to explain, \u201cShe is on the cover page of my exercise books. I don\u2019t know; probably I like her hair and smile.\u201d\n\n\u201cKeep quiet. You are going too far with bad thoughts. When you are 30 we will find a suitable girl for you. Do not worry now. I think your mother is spoiling you. Think about a PhD in political science or law, becoming a scholar, and living a happy life\u201d, he advised.\n\nI told him that I wanted to live a happy life and understand how a PhD would help me to gain happiness. He laughed, patted my head, and told me, \u201cYou are too young to discuss life and the future. I should have waited for a while before broaching the topic. For now, concentrate on your studies.\u201d\n\nMy father said that he heard about Nihal\u2019s promise to Brother Cassian to become a priest. He wanted to know my view on becoming a priest. I told him I would consider the possibility if there is a guarantee that I could become a bishop. He liked that answer and told my mother,"
