    "chunk_text": "OPA Facilitates Brainstorming Session on Harnessing Digital Transformation for Inclusive Development\n\nThe Organisation of Professional Associations of Sri Lanka (OPA), under the patronage of Mr. Jayantha Gallehewa, President of OPA, through its National Issues Committee (NIC), convened a high-level brainstorming session on \u201cDigitalization for Societal Upliftment\u201d as part of its continued commitment to advancing national dialogue on digital transformation. The initiative was spearheaded by Mr. Bhanu Wijayaratne, Vice President of OPA and Chairman of the National Issues Committee.\n\nThe session served as a multidisciplinary platform bringing together government officials, academics, technology specialists, and professionals to deliberate on the strategic role of digital transformation in advancing Sri Lanka\u2019s socio-economic development agenda.\n\nRecognizing that digitalization has evolved beyond the realm of technology into a key enabler of national progress, the discussion explored how digital solutions can strengthen governance systems, enhance public service delivery, foster innovation, promote social inclusion, and create sustainable opportunities for citizens.\n\nIn his address, the President of OPA emphasized that Sri Lanka\u2019s digital transformation journey requires a collective and forward-looking approach driven by professional expertise, collaborative partnerships, and citizen-focused solutions. He highlighted OPA\u2019s continued commitment to facilitating constructive dialogue on national priorities by bringing together professionals from diverse disciplines to contribute knowledge, insights, and practical recommendations."
  },
