    "chunk_size_bytes": 1664,
    "chunk_text": "In his address, the President of OPA emphasized that Sri Lanka\u2019s digital transformation journey requires a collective and forward-looking approach driven by professional expertise, collaborative partnerships, and citizen-focused solutions. He highlighted OPA\u2019s continued commitment to facilitating constructive dialogue on national priorities by bringing together professionals from diverse disciplines to contribute knowledge, insights, and practical recommendations.\n\nThe session featured an eminent panel of experts representing the Government, academia, industry, and the technology sector, including Mr. Waruna Sri Dhanapala, Secretary, Ministry of Digital Economy; Mr. Sumudu Rathnayaka, Adviser, Ministry of Digital Economy; Dr. Shanta Rajapaksha Yapa, Director and Senior Academic Fellow, SLIIT Business School; Mr. Dulip Somiratna, Senior Assistant Secretary to the President; Mr. Thilak Pathirage, Chairman, Sri Lanka Computer Emergency Readiness Team (SLCERT); Mr. Sanjaya Karunasena, Executive Director and Acting CEO, GovTech Sri Lanka; Mr. Indika De Zoysa, Strategic Adviser and Vice President, Huawei Technologies Lanka (Pvt) Ltd and Dr. Aparrajitha Ariyadasa.\n\nExperts at the session highlighted the urgent need for Sri Lanka to accelerate digital adoption and strengthen citizen-focused digital services to achieve the vision of Society 5.0. They emphasized that while Sri Lanka has made considerable progress in developing digital infrastructure, introducing technology solutions, and encouraging innovation, the utilization and adoption of these digital facilities remain comparatively low when compared with several countries in the region."
