    "chunk_text": "Experts at the session highlighted the urgent need for Sri Lanka to accelerate digital adoption and strengthen citizen-focused digital services to achieve the vision of Society 5.0. They emphasized that while Sri Lanka has made considerable progress in developing digital infrastructure, introducing technology solutions, and encouraging innovation, the utilization and adoption of these digital facilities remain comparatively low when compared with several countries in the region.\n\nHighlighting the importance of citizen-centered digital platforms, the experts pointed out that Sri Lanka has the opportunity to expand digital services across key areas, including government services and public administration; healthcare and medical services; education and skills development; public transportation; financial services; and citizen complaint and support mechanisms.\n\nThey observed that many countries have successfully used integrated digital platforms to provide faster, more transparent, and accessible services to citizens. However, Sri Lanka still faces challenges in ensuring widespread public adoption and effective utilization of available digital facilities.\n\nThe session was moderated by Mr. Heshan Karunaratne, President of the Computer Society of Sri Lanka (CSSL) and Mr. Udesh I W Seneviratna, Secretary, Computer Society of Sri Lanka (CSSL) and Member of the National Issues Committee (NIC) of OPA who guided the deliberations towards identifying opportunities, challenges, and strategic pathways for advancing digital transformation in Sri Lanka. The proceedings were compered by Mr. B.A.H.S. Preena, NIC Committee Member."
