    "md5": "e2e577eff18ebfbcfef2ecf52d4d1878",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1946,
    "chunk_text": "He clearly saw a need for a practical outcome in his inaugural speech on 28 November 1987. In his own words. . . \u2018. . . the crisis that rages in Sri Lanka at the present time could never have reached the gigantic proportions of today but for the regressive nature of the Constitution of 1972 and the far more authoritarian and illiberal nature of the Constitution of 1978. . . . so, we must recognize that if individual and political freedom, racial harmony, justice and peace are our objectives, they are unattainable without the enactment of a Constitution that is compatible with the attainment of such objectives.\u2019\n\nThe change of government resulting from the victory of the United National Party in the election of 1977 provided continuing evidence that Chanaka Amaratunga\u2019s statement that an \u2018 . . .adverse feature of our Constitutional processes has been a belief that power should be concentrated \u2026\u2019 was fully justified. It is well known that the Constitution of 1978 set up a President who was not answerable to the legislature. The denial of civic rights to opposition politicians including former Prime Minister Sirima Bandaranaike, while it gained temporary political advantage, eventually weakened trust in government.\n\nThe extension of the life of the legislature elected in 1977 for five years, all the way up to 1989 through a referendum, was also clearly the use of the political process for partisan advantage. While the single university was replaced by separate universities with some degree of autonomy, those of us who were in the academic world wore disheartened when an amendment to the Universities Act in 1985 abolished the University Courts and returned the control of the appointment of Vice Chancellors to the President of the country. There were a number of important specific recommendations that emanated out of the presentations and discussions of the seven seminars that Chanaka Amaratunga organized."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-08-01-islandlk-98572c39",
    "num": "islandlk-98572c39",
    "date_str": "2026-08-01",
    "description": "Contributions of Chanaka Amaratunga towards Constitutional Reform",
    "url_metadata": "http://island.lk/contributions-of-chanaka-amaratunga-towards-constitutional-reform/",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "islandlk",
