    "language": "en",
    "md5": "9dab4c13b1b22c8eb5aeba02bdf6afbe",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2001,
    "chunk_text": "AAT Sri Lanka felicitates 2,179 passed finalists\n\nThe Association of Accounting Technicians of Sri Lanka (AAT Sri Lanka), the pioneer in accounting education and professional skills development in the country, recently held its Passed Finalists\u2019 Diploma Awarding Ceremony, at the BMICH, Colombo, honouring the students who successfully completed the final level of the January 2026 AAT examinations.\n\nA total of 2,179 passed finalists, representing every district of the island, were invited to receive their Diploma in Accounting and Business, each accompanied by a guest to witness this significant milestone in their academic journey.\n\nOwing to the large number of recipients, the ceremony was conducted across three sessions, welcoming an audience of approximately 4,000 throughout the day, making it one of the largest Passed Finalists\u2019 Diploma Awarding Ceremonies organised by AAT Sri Lanka.\n\nThe morning session was graced by Fintrex Finance General Manager and CEO Jayathilake Bandara as the chief guest, with CA Sri Lanka President Tishan Subhasinghe as the guest of honour.\n\nThe afternoon session featured Colombo Re Insurance Brokers (Pvt.) Ltd CEO Roshini Silva as the chief guest, joined by CA Sri Lanka Council Member Saman Siri Lal as the guest of honour, while the evening session was graced by Capital Maharaja Group Finance Director Lalith Fernando as the chief guest, with CA Sri Lanka Council Member Thivanka Jayasinghe as the guest of honour.\n\nThe occasion was further distinguished by the presence of AAT Sri Lanka President Dr. Chamara Bandara, who led the proceedings alongside the vice president, secretary, members of the Governing Council and CEO of AAT Sri Lanka.\n\nHaving successfully completed the final level of the AAT qualification and secured the NVQ Level 5 equivalent Diploma in Accounting and Business, the passed finalists are now equipped with the knowledge, practical skills and competencies required to embark on careers in accounting, finance and business."
  },
