    "md5": "c3b3079504b1d3c4654174d13d0c2f1e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2009,
    "chunk_text": "Vision Beyond Sight: A Day of Fellowship at the School for  the Blind, Ratmalana\n\nVisually impaired students are keen and capable players of cricket.\n\nEducation is often thought of as something found within the four walls of a classroom. Yet some of the most valuable lessons cannot be found in a textbook.\n\nOn\u00a0 June 9, 2026, the Sub-Prefects\u2019 Guild of Wesley College visited the School for the Blind, Ratmalana, for a day of fellowship and learning. While the visit included music, games, conversation, and shared laughter, it also offered something far more meaningful: the opportunity to better understand a way of life unfamiliar to many of us.\n\nThe programme began with a warm welcome and an introduction by the Principal of the Blind School, followed by an introduction to the Prefects\u2019 Guild of Wesley College delivered by one of our own Sub-Prefects. From there, the formalities quickly gave way to something much more natural. Music became the first common language.\n\nStudents from both schools took turns performing, sharing songs with one another before the atmosphere gradually shifted from one of introductions to one of friendship. Conversations became easier, laughter became louder, and before long, there was little sense that these were students meeting for the first time.\n\nOne of the most eye-opening moments of the day came during a brief introduction to Braille education. For many Wesleyites, Braille had always been something they had heard about but never truly understood. We learned that the students follow the very same national curriculum as any other school in Sri Lanka. The subjects, lessons, and examinations are no different.\n\nThe only difference is the medium through which they learn. Instead of printed pages, they read and write using Braille. It was a simple yet powerful reminder that blindness does not lower the standard of education, it simply changes the way that education is accessed.\n\nThe afternoon brought one of the day\u2019s highlights: a game of cricket."
  },
