    "chunk_size_bytes": 964,
    "chunk_text": "Senior Prefect of Wesley College, Master Joel De Silva, also reflected on the experience: \u201cIt is difficult to leave a place like the Blind School without learning something about yourself. What stood out to me wasn\u2019t what the students couldn\u2019t do, it was everything they could. They welcomed us so warmly that it never felt like we were visitors. We spent the day playing, laughing, and talking just as any group of students would. It was an experience that reminded us that some of the strongest people you\u2019ll ever meet simply see the world differently.\u201d\n\nThe visit did not teach us to feel sorry for visually impaired students. It taught us to let go of the idea that they ever needed our pity in\u00a0the first place.\n\nOn that day, two schools came together. By the time we left, we were no longer thinking about who could see and who could not.\n\nWe were simply students who had shared a day\u2014and walked away with a few more friends than when we arrived."
