    "chunk_text": "We need new or reformed institutions to develop our country at the crossroads, even as we draw on the lessons from the past. The Central Bank will have to play a developmental role. A twenty first century development bank is a must. Industrial and trade policies amidst a global economy coming apart are necessary. State institutions including SOEs have to be reformed and updated for our contemporary needs, and certainly not privatised and left to the whims of extractive financiers. Agricultural transformation is necessary to ensure a secure food system. Mobilisation of society with a new generation of co-operatives can be a way forward.\n\nA robust housing scheme creating a multiplier of livelihoods for masons and wage workers, and backward linkages for industries and employment related to carpentry, roof tile making, metal works etc. could be considered for growth. Such an approach to the economy where the government takes the lead with investment, and in the process bringing in domestic private investment, is the need of the hour in world where we can expect little from external actors.\n\nThe NPP has an overwhelming mandate\u2014like no other government in the history of the country. On a trying global pitch, the government has played a very cautious first innings over the last two years. The second innings cannot be the same, and it needs to muster the political will to mobilise state and society far beyond the boundaries set by the collapsing neoliberal order."
