    "md5": "3e43940b751dc6b6308ff11dc6f95145",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1613,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka makes history at World Schools Debating Championships\n\nThe Sri Lankan national debating team at the opening ceremony of the World Schools Debating Championships in Nairobi, Kenya (from left): Rudhesh Ram, Savith Wijesundara, Apoorva Jinadasa, Adam Dhilshan, and T. Tharaniharan\n\nSri Lankan national team member Adam Dhilshan delivers his speech during a debate round at the World Schools Debating Championships\n\nNational team ranks first out of over 80 countries after preliminary rounds \u2014 the best result in Sri Lankan debating history\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s national schools debating team has delivered the finest performance in the country\u2019s history at the World Schools Debating Championships (WSDC), the largest and most prestigious debating competition for secondary school students in the world.\n\nAt WSDC 2026, held in Nairobi, Kenya from 14 to 24 July with more than 700 students, coaches, and judges from over 80 countries, the Sri Lankan team won seven of its eight preliminary debates and ranked first overall after the preliminary rounds \u2014 the highest ranking a Sri Lankan team has ever achieved at the tournament, and the first time a Sri Lankan team has topped the preliminary standings altogether. The team progressed until Double-Octofinals afterwards.\n\nThis result surpasses the country\u2019s previous record in the preliminary rounds of the WSDC, which was fourth place in 2023, a particularly impressive feat given the rapidly expanding level of international competition. The achievement reinforces Sri Lanka\u2019s standing on the global stage and sets a strong benchmark for future teams."
  },
