    "chunk_size_bytes": 1743,
    "chunk_text": "That determination runs through every page of Made in Nepal. Unlike many business memoirs that celebrate wealth, this one celebrates perseverance. It traces the transformation of a modest family trading business into CG Corp Global, a diversified enterprise of more than 200 companies operating across Asia, Europe and Africa.\n\nAt its heart are the values inherited from his father: discipline, prudence, humility and long-term thinking. These principles became the foundation of sustainable growth.\n\nOne memorable episode illustrates the unpredictability of operating in fragile environments. During a period of unrest, armed men approached him and asked, \u201cAre you Binod Chaudhary?\u201d Having previously encountered Maoist insurgents and militant groups, he feared the worst. Moments later, he realised they were members of his own security team. The story captures the psychological demands of leadership and the courage required simply to keep moving forward.\n\nYet, \u2018Made in Nepal\u2019 is about more than entrepreneurial success. It is equally about institution-building. Dr. Chaudhary repeatedly argues that businesses cannot depend forever on charismatic founders. Sustainable organisations require professional management, strong governance, succession planning and systems that outlive individuals. His philosophy closely mirrors Jim Collins\u2019 Built to Last: enduring companies are built on disciplined leadership rather than individual heroics.\n\nFor Sri Lankan business leaders, these lessons are particularly relevant. We too operate from a small market and have endured political uncertainty and economic crises. Yet Sri Lanka possesses considerable strengths: its strategic location, educated workforce and entrepreneurial talent."
