    "chunk_text": "For Sri Lankan business leaders, these lessons are particularly relevant. We too operate from a small market and have endured political uncertainty and economic crises. Yet Sri Lanka possesses considerable strengths: its strategic location, educated workforce and entrepreneurial talent.\n\nHe concluded his keynote by identifying five qualities every future-ready director should possess: think globally, embrace innovation and artificial intelligence, take calculated risks, build trusted brands rather than simply manufacture products, and remain proud of one\u2019s national identity. The strongest global companies, he reminded the audience, never forget where they came from.\n\nThat message lies at the heart of Made in Nepal. World-class companies can emerge from Kathmandu, Colombo or any city where people possess vision, discipline and determination. Small countries should never think small.\n\nstory is not wealth. It is about building belief: that adversity can become opportunity, that resilience is a lasting competitive advantage, and that leaders who combine ambition with integrity can build not only successful companies but stronger nations. His journey is a powerful reminder that the size of your country should never define the size of your dreams.\n\n(The author teaches Accounting and Finance at the University of Buckingham UK)"
