    "chunk_size_bytes": 1909,
    "chunk_text": "Crucially, scientific dating methods proved that the Ibbankatuwa megalithic tombs significantly predated the written, chronicle-based history of Sri Lanka. They proved beyond all doubt that a highly advanced, technologically capable, and socially stratified society lived, traded, and buried its dead on the island centuries before the traditional historical timeline even began.\n\nRaja lived an exceptionally long, fruitful life characterised by unyielding personal and professional integrity. He was a rare scholar who believed that an archaeologist\u2019s sole duty is to be an honest scientist who seeks the objective truth, not a comforting storyteller who tries to satisfy the emotional or political biases of the public. He stood as a grand bulwark against the politicisation of history, protecting the past from being weaponised by modern agendas.\n\nThrough the special collection of articles brought together by Uvindu Kurukulasuriya, the citizens of Sri Lanka are reminded of what made Raja an irreplaceable icon. He was a strict yet loving father who taught his children that greatness is achieved only through tireless, nightly toil. He was a joyful brother and an unmatched storyteller who filled rooms with laughter. Professionally, he was the visionary chemist who saved our finest art from destruction, the bold historian who recognised the deep maternal comfort of Tara Devi in our ancient landscape, and the pioneer who unravelled our deep prehistoric roots.\n\nBy challenging orthodox history, rejecting biased traditions, and setting an uncompromising scientific standard for generations to follow, he single-handedly protected the true, multifaceted soul of Sri Lankan heritage. He will forever be missed, but his monumental work ensures that he will always be remembered as the legendary scholar who looked at the past through the clear, clean lens of science and proudly dared to be different."
