    "chunk_text": "Less nodding and more prodding essential to making Boards more effective\n\nIn an era of hyper-velocity change, the Boardroom has transformed from a predictable theater of governance into a high-stakes crucible where corporate solidity, success, and survival are forged and enabled. Corporate Boards no longer enjoy the luxury of quarterly contemplation. Today, directors are thrust into an unforgiving arena where technological shifts, geopolitical dynamics, intense competition, and close public scrutiny converge and interplay in ways that are difficult to anticipate and decipher. The fundamental challenge facing modern Boards is not merely oversight. It is survival in an environment where the shelf life of a strategy is very short, and the degree of alertness to win and survive is ultra-high. Board membership is no longer a walk in the park or a retirement perk!"
