    "chunk_size_bytes": 1318,
    "chunk_text": "Contemporary Boards operate in a business environment defined by permanent volatility. The convergence of exponential AI, systemic digital disruptions, and fragmented geopolitical realities has compressed decision-making timelines and inflated the cost of strategic missteps. AI is not just another line item on the technology roadmap. It is a fundamental shift in the architecture of business. In this backdrop, Boards must be AI-savvy and must establish a robust, dynamic AI governance framework that balances aggressive value creation with strict risk mitigation. Boards face an unprecedented cognitive burden governing the complexities of AI. To remain competitive, Boards must balance their ethical duty to mitigate existential risks posed by technology with intense commercial pressures to accelerate innovation.\n\nThe \u201cexpert in the room\u201d is one of the most dangerous features in today\u2019s Board dynamics. When a Board defers to a single specialist, it replaces collective oversight with blind trust. In a slower era, outsourcing intellect to a subject matter expert was a convenient shortcut. Today, in an era of hyper-volatility, it is a liability. True oversight is not a relay race of passing the baton to the nearest specialist. It is a contact sport that requires every director to step into the arena."
