    "chunk_size_bytes": 1055,
    "chunk_text": "The \u201cexpert in the room\u201d is one of the most dangerous features in today\u2019s Board dynamics. When a Board defers to a single specialist, it replaces collective oversight with blind trust. In a slower era, outsourcing intellect to a subject matter expert was a convenient shortcut. Today, in an era of hyper-volatility, it is a liability. True oversight is not a relay race of passing the baton to the nearest specialist. It is a contact sport that requires every director to step into the arena.\n\nWhen directors rely on \u201cexpert deference,\u201d they do not just silence dissent, they abdicate their fiduciary duty. A Board\u2019s strength lies in intellectual friction, not harmony. By demanding that every director brings strategy, risk awareness, and pragmatism to every single agenda item, a Board transforms from a rubber-stamping committee into a resilient, forward-looking brain trust. True oversight demands a climate where directors feel empowered and obligated to challenge assumptions, stress-test vulnerabilities, and voice uncomfortable truths."
