    "chunk_text": "With a long-standing history of trust and sustainable business practices, COOPFED remains committed to improving the economic well-being of both its members and consumers. By promoting local industries and reducing market monopolies, the Federation continues to demonstrate the vital role of the cooperative movement in building a stronger and more equitable economy.\n\nThe Deputy Minister further noted that the Ministry of Finance and the Ministry of Trade are working together to strengthen the cooperative banking system, which will provide small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) with a stronger platform to bring their products to the market.\n\nThe event was attended by COOPFED Chairman and Trade, Commerce, Food Security and Cooperative Development Adviser Dr. Shantha Jayaratne, COOPFED CEO Roshani Pradeepa, BCC Lanka Chairman Prasanga Indrajith, Lanka Sugar Company Chairman Wasantha Athula Kumara, and Director/CEO Dharmavardhana Udaya Kumar."
