    "chunk_size_bytes": 998,
    "chunk_text": "The NIPO is fully aware of this implementation process, as the DG of NIPO is a member of the EU GI project steering committee. This sequencing formed part of the agreed implementation strategy and followed the same approach adopted for the registration of Ceylon Cinnamon.\n\nThe domestic legal framework for GI implementation has been developed with the active participation of the Sri Lanka Tea Board, the National Intellectual Property Office, and other relevant stakeholders.\n\nIn accordance with the agreed implementation strategy, and based on the advice of the CIRAD, the domestic GI application was intended to be submitted after the completion of the EU registration process.\n\nThe Sri Lanka Tea Board values the close cooperation and support extended by the National Intellectual Property Office throughout this important initiative. We remain committed to continuing this collaboration in successfully completing both the international and domestic GI registration processes for Ceylon Tea.\""
