    "md5": "4e5f98291dcbc2e876985726db58b836",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1772,
    "chunk_text": "Import Section of Ceylon Chamber of Commerce holds 91st AGM\n\nCommittee members of the Import Section of The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce\n\nThe 91st Annual General Meeting (AGM) of the Import Section of The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce was held recently at Shangri-La Colombo, bringing together members of the import and trade community to review the Section\u2019s achievements and outline its priorities for the year ahead.\n\nSri Lanka Ports Authority (SLPA) Chairman Dr. Parakarama Dissanayake attended as the Chief Guest and the keynote speaker, while Maersk Sri Lanka and Maldives Managing Director Biju Ravi delivered the address as Guest Speaker.\n\nBrandix Apparel\u2019s Ushan de Silva was reappointed as Chairman for a second consecutive term. Sankha Gammanpila of Hemas Pharmaceuticals Ltd., was appointed Vice Chairman, while Rajasooriyar Canagasooriyar of Hayleys PLC was appointed Deputy Vice Chairman.\n\nUshan de Silva reaffirmed the Import Section\u2019s commitment to strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s trade competitiveness through trade facilitation, digital transformation, and responsible trade practices. While noting that the country\u2019s economic recovery is progressing, he said businesses continue to face rising logistics costs, supply chain disruptions, and geopolitical uncertainty, highlighting the need for a more resilient and efficient trading environment.\n\nHe said the Import Section will continue to work closely with policymakers and industry stakeholders to advance practical trade reforms, streamline border processes, and support the implementation of paperless trade initiatives and the National Single Window. He also highlighted the Section\u2019s advocacy over the past year in addressing key trade policy issues and operational challenges faced by importers."
  },
