    "chunk_text": "Several inmates reportedly attempted to escape by breaking through a temporary wall under construction, while another group set fire to a prison building. Prison officers positioned near the main entrance opened fire to contain the escalating situation. During the unrest, some inmates also allegedly assaulted fellow prisoners who refused to join the violence.\n\nMeanwhile, tension also mounted outside the prison on Saturday as worried relatives gathered after hearing sounds resembling gunfire from inside the facility. Police said some members of the crowd attempted to breach security barriers and threw stones towards the prison before being dispersed by police and STF personnel. The Sri Lanka Air Force also deployed drones and a Bell 412 helicopter to conduct aerial surveillance of the prison complex.\n\nTo maintain public order, police imposed an overnight curfew in three Grama Niladhari divisions surrounding the Mahara Prison within the Ragama Police Division\u2014Kendaliyaddapaluwa West (246), Kendaliyaddapaluwa North (246/C), and Dambuwe (181/G). The curfew was lifted earlier yesterday after authorities confirmed that the situation had been brought fully under control.\n\nThe violent disturbance caused extensive damage to several prison facilities, including the rehabilitation division, visitors' area, prison hospital, kitchen, industrial section, and a number of prison buildings, according to the Department of Prisons.\n\nThe Department said a number of inmates from Mahara Prison are being transferred to other prisons following the unrest.\n\nMahara Prison unrest brought under control; Curfew remains in force"
