    "chunk_text": "Harsha says no to govt. crossover but says govt searching for people like him\n\nColombo, Aug. 3 (Daily Mirror) - Samagi Jana Balawegaya (SJB) MP Harsha de Silva yesterday scoffed rumors that were being circulated in the media about a crossover to the government.\n\n\" There is rumour that I am to cross over to the government. This is far from being the truth . However I am happy that the government has wanted people such as myself \" Dr. De Silva said in a special statement.\n\n\" The politics I follow is different. I don't hesitate to praise good things and to oppose bad ones. As the Chairman of Committee on Public Finance (COPF) I always try to maintain it's dignity. I am aware that there are some who do not like the way I work\" he added.\n\nDr. De Silva was seen with Minister of Health Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa at a ceremony held to mark the 10th anniversary of \"Suwa Seriya\" Ambulance service."
