    "chunk_size_bytes": 1514,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka's national schools debating team has delivered the finest performance in the country's history at the World Schools Debating Championship (WSDC), the largest and most prestigious debating competition for secondary school students in the world.At WSDC 2026, held in Nairobi, Kenya from 14 to 24 July with the participation of more than 700 students, coaches and judges from over 80 countries,.\n\nThe team's success was matched by outstanding individual results:Individually, Savith Wijesundara (Elizabeth Moir School) finished 4th Best Speaker in the world and 1st in the ESL (English as a Second Language) category \u2014 another national first \u2014 while Rudhesh Ram (Colombo International School) placed 7th Best Speaker in the world, and Adam Dhilshan (Royal College) was ranked 6th Best ESL Speaker.\n\nA rigorous, year-long selection processRepresenting Sri Lanka at WSDC is the product of a demanding, year-long process overseen by the Debaters' Council of Sri Lanka, the organization that administers the national schools debating circuit. Debaters take part in more than 15 Debaters\u2019 Council-endorsed tournaments annually, before applications for the National Pool are opened. From that pool, candidates go through training and trial rounds before the final team of five is selected.This year's team \u2014 Savith Wijesundara, Rudhesh Ram, Adam Dhilshan, T. Tharaniharan (Royal College) and Apoorva Jinadasa (Hillwood College) \u2014 was coached by Shalem Sumanthiran, Sachin Tissera and Kavindra Senaratna."
