    "chunk_text": "Suicide bomber targets rally in Pakistan, killing at least 14\n\nsky news - At least 14 people have been killed in a suicide bombing that targeted protesters at an anti-militant rally in northwestern Pakistan, officials say.\n\nThe attack happened in the Swat Valley town of Kabal, in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province, where demonstrators had gathered near a police station, chanting anti-militant slogans and demanding peace.\n\nThe victims included five police officers and eight civilians, according to a police official who said the 14th person to die was believed to be the suicide bomber.\n\nAt least 18 other people were injured in the attack as police launched an operation to arrest anyone who may have helped the bomber.\n\nShortly before the atrocity, speakers at the rally accused authorities of failing to act decisively against militants, according to witnesses.\n\nMilitancy in the country's border areas has increased \u2060sharply in recent months, targeting mainly the military and police.\n\nIn response, residents have repeatedly organised anti-Taliban rallies to protest against the militants' presence.\n\nThe Swat Valley was once a stronghold of Islamic militants who imposed a strict interpretation of Sharia, or Islamic law.\n\nThen in 2007, Pakistan's military carried out a major operation that drove them out and restored government control.\n\nHowever, militants have resurfaced in the valley, fuelling fears the Pakistani Taliban are seeking to regain a foothold in the region."
