    "chunk_size_bytes": 1699,
    "chunk_text": "Jay Shah\u2019s Tanzania milestone, US ban, Sri Lanka gold & FIFA leadership crisis\n\nAUG.03 (Mirror Sports) - Global sports headlines featured a new cricket milestone in Tanzania, a major anti-corruption ban, Sri Lanka\u2019s Commonwealth Games gold and fresh FIFA leadership controversy.\n\nInternational Cricket Council (ICC) Chairman Jay Shah officially inaugurated the Tanzania Cricket Association's (TCA) new arena on Sunday, 2 August 2026, marking a major milestone for cricket in the East African nation. The ceremony comes just days before Tanzania hosts the ICC Men's Cricket World Cup Challenge League B 2026 from 8 to 18 August, with the new venue set to serve as the tournament's principal ground.\n\nThe state-of-the-art facility is expected to play a key role in the growth of cricket in Tanzania, providing a permanent base for international matches, player development, coaching, umpire education and grassroots programmes. Construction of the arena began in May 2025 and was completed in July 2026, following the project's launch in late 2024.\n\nSpeaking at the inauguration, Shah described the arena as \"a significant milestone for cricket in Tanzania\" and praised the Tanzania Cricket Association for its vision and commitment to expanding the sport. He said the ICC would continue supporting its Members in developing infrastructure and strengthening cricket across the region.\n\nTanzania Cricket Association Chairman Dr B.S. Sreekumar called the opening of the TCA Arena a defining moment for cricket in the country, saying the facility would create new opportunities to host international events, develop future generations of players and inspire more young Tanzanians to take up the game."
