    "chunk_text": "The naming reflects the diplomatic relationship that developed during Trump\u2019s first administration. In December 2020, Washington recognized Moroccan sovereignty over Western Sahara alongside a US-brokered agreement under which Morocco agreed to normalize relations with Israel.\n\nWestern Sahara has been disputed since Spain withdrew from the territory in 1975. Morocco controls most of the region, while the Algeria-backed Polisario Front seeks the establishment of an independent Sahrawi state.\n\nIsrael formally recognized Moroccan sovereignty over Western Sahara in 2023 and reaffirmed that position the following year.\n\nThe UN Security Council adopted a resolution in October 2025 that supported negotiations based on Morocco\u2019s autonomy proposal, under which Western Sahara would receive limited self-government while remaining under Moroccan sovereignty.\n\nIn his letter to Trump, Mohammed VI presented the expressway as both an infrastructure project and a symbol of the two countries\u2019 strategic partnership, saying it would strengthen Morocco\u2019s position as a commercial link between Europe and Africa."
