    "chunk_size_bytes": 1999,
    "chunk_text": "At the heart of the model are Pods: small, accountable teams of four to five professionals who work together to deliver outsourced and fractional back-office services, such as finance, administration, and operational support, to client businesses. Each pod is guided by a pod lead, who manages the client relationship and ensures consistent, professional delivery. This structure allows individuals to re-enter the workforce on flexible terms, without sacrificing the accountability and quality that businesses need.\n\nCrucially, the ReturnShip Alliance talent model imposes no barriers based on age, gender, or geographic location and is designed to include differently abled professionals as well. Professionals from anywhere in Sri Lanka can join a pod, opening opportunities for talented individuals regardless of where they live or what stage of life they are in.\n\n\u201cReturnShip Alliance was born from a simple observation, that Sri Lanka is full of skilled professionals who\u2019ve had to step back from their careers, not because they lack ability, but because the system never offered them a flexible way back in,\u201d said Shivalatha Sivasundaram, founder/CEO of The Training Lab Pvt. Ltd. \u201cThe Pod model gives people a real, structured path to restart their professional journeys \u2013 on their terms \u2013 and I\u2019m grateful to be building it alongside a team that believes in that same vision,\u201d said Shivalatha Sivasundaram, founder/CEO of The Training Lab Pvt Ltd.\n\n\u201cFrom a technology and operations standpoint, our focus has been on building a stack that lets Pods function seamlessly so professionals can concentrate on delivering great work for clients rather than wrestling with tools,\u201d said Shiraz Safaideen, an independent consultant who leads the technology stack and broader operational support behind ReturnShip Alliance. \u201cWe\u2019ve designed the backend to scale with the model, from the first cohort in Sri Lanka right through to the franchise-style expansion planned ahead.\u201d"
  },
