    "md5": "d110e6e5e033123b6fe72ad162619d38",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1720,
    "chunk_text": "Ceylon Chamber\u2019s Import Section holds 91st AGM\n\nThe 91st Annual General Meeting (AGM) of the Import Section of The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce was held recently at Shangri-La Colombo, bringing together the members of the import and trade community to review the section\u2019s achievements and outline its priorities for the year ahead.\n\nSri Lanka Ports Authority Chairman Dr. Parakarama Dissanayake attended as the chief guest and keynote speaker, while Maersk Sri Lanka and Maldives Managing Director Biju Ravi delivered the address as the guest speaker.\n\nUshan de Silva of Brandix Apparel (Pvt.) Ltd was reappointed as Chairman for a second consecutive term. Sankha Gammanpila of Hemas Pharmaceuticals (Pvt.) Ltd was appointed as Vice Chairman, while Rajasooriya of Hayleys PLC was appointed as Deputy Vice Chairman.\n\nAddressing the members, de Silva reaffirmed the Import Section\u2019s commitment to strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s trade competitiveness through trade facilitation, digital transformation and responsible trade practices. While noting that the country\u2019s economic recovery is progressing, he said businesses continue to face the rising logistics costs, supply chain disruptions and geopolitical uncertainty, highlighting the need for a more resilient and efficient trading environment.\n\nHe said the Import Section will continue to work closely with the policymakers and industry stakeholders to advance practical trade reforms, streamline border processes and support the implementation of paperless trade initiatives and the National Single Window.\n\nHe also highlighted the section\u2019s advocacy over the past year in addressing the key trade policy issues and operational challenges faced by the importers."
