    "md5": "495cb47f96db36989e530fca9680c88b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1858,
    "chunk_text": "IPS celebrates 6 researchers awarded prestigious graduate scholarships\n\nThe Institute of Policy Studies of Sri Lanka (IPS) celebrates the outstanding achievement of its latest batch of researchers in winning prestigious scholarships for postgraduate studies at top-rated universities.\n\nSuresh Ranasinghe joined the IPS on graduating with a BA in Economics with First Class Honours from the University of Colombo and an LLB from the Open University of Sri Lanka and secured a Commonwealth Shared Scholarship in 2022/23 to follow an MSc in Development Economics from the University of Nottingham, UK.\n\nOn his return, Ranasinghe pursued his research interests in health, education and labour policy and was awarded a fully-funded studentship to commence a PhD in Economics at Nottingham Trent University, UK, from October 2025.\n\nUsha Perera joined the IPS with a BA in Economics with First Class Honours from the University of Colombo and won a Commonwealth Shared Scholarship 2023/24 to pursue an MSc in Economics at the University of Leeds.\n\nOn her return to the IPS, she continued to pursue her research interests in health, labour and education policy and successfully secured funding from the Economic and Social Research Council, UK, to commence a PhD in Economics at Lancaster University, UK in October 2026.\n\nChandula Idirisinghe joined the IPS with a BSc (Hons) in Agricultural Technology and Management with an Upper Second Class from the University of Peradeniya and successfully completed a Master of Agricultural Economics from the Postgraduate Institute of Agriculture at the University of Peradeniya.\n\nWith his research pursuits in the areas of agriculture and agribusiness development policy, Idirisinghe has gained admission to the University of Guelph, Canada, on a fully-funded scholarship to commence his PhD in Management in September 2026."
  },
