    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s longer-term export strategy is built around the National Export Development Plan 2026-2030, launched in June. It aims to increase the total export earnings to US $ 36 billion by 2030, almost double the amount targeted for this year. The statement listed the 2030 targets as US $ 27 billion from the merchandise exports and US $ 8 billion from services. These figures add up to US $ 35 billion, leaving a US $ 1 billion discrepancy that requires clarification.The plan also seeks to widen Sri Lanka\u2019s export basket beyond the traditional industries. Eight new sectors have been selected for promotion, with the EDB identifying electronics, food and beverages, information technology and logistics as the areas already recording growth.\n\nSri Lanka Expo will return from January 14 to 17, 2027, after a 15-year break, as part of the efforts to connect the local exporters with international markets. The EDB expects more than 1,500 foreign buyers to participate.\n\nIt will select 650 exporters from more than 1,100 applicants, while over 200 stalls will be reserved for the SMEs. An investor forum will also be held on January 15, in collaboration with the Board of Investment, Tourism Ministry and Colombo Port City."
