    "chunk_size_bytes": 1400,
    "chunk_text": "DFCC scales up retail banking with StanChart portfolio buyout\n\nDFCC Bank PLC has completed the acquisition of Standard Chartered Bank Sri Lanka\u2019s wealth and retail banking business, bringing approximately 50,000 customers and employees attached to the operation into the bank.\n\nThe transaction covers customer relationships across priority banking, credit cards, retail lending, deposits, wealth management and small and medium enterprise (SME) portfolios, along with selected operating assets.\n\nThe acquisition expands the scale of DFCC\u2019s retail operations and strengthens its wealth management and SME businesses, forming part of the bank\u2019s longer-term strategy to broaden its customer base across Sri Lanka.\n\nDFCC said the migration was structured to minimise disruption, following several months of preparation and collaboration between the two banks.\n\nThe customers can continue using their existing Standard Chartered account numbers alongside their newly issued DFCC account numbers. The existing credit and debit cards, card PINs, standing instructions, direct debits, recurring payments and instalment arrangements will also remain operational.\n\nThe saved payees and beneficiaries have been transferred to DFCC\u2019s digital banking platforms, DFCC ONE and DFCC iConnect. The customers can also continue using their existing branches and dealing with their current relationship managers."
  },
