    "md5": "d1c39811f09474ed87b51a2482d0c6ad",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1688,
    "chunk_text": "The saved payees and beneficiaries have been transferred to DFCC\u2019s digital banking platforms, DFCC ONE and DFCC iConnect. The customers can also continue using their existing branches and dealing with their current relationship managers.\n\n\u201cSuccess meant ensuring that the customers experienced as little of that complexity as possible. Their existing Standard Chartered account numbers remain usable alongside their new DFCC Bank account numbers. They can continue using the same credit and debit cards and the same card PINs, while their standing instructions, direct debits, recurring payments, instalment arrangements and other everyday banking arrangements continue as before,\u201d he added.\n\nPerera said transferring the customers\u2019 saved payees and beneficiaries to DFCC\u2019s digital platforms would remove one of the most common inconveniences associated with changing banks.\n\n\u201cI extend my sincere appreciation to my colleagues at DFCC Bank and our colleagues at Standard Chartered Bank, the Central Bank of Sri Lanka, our technology and implementation partners and everyone whose expertise and commitment made this possible. It is an honour to welcome our new customers and colleagues to DFCC Bank. We look forward to earning their trust and supporting them through every stage of their financial lives,\u201d he said.\n\nThe customers requiring assistance can contact DFCC Bank\u2019s 24-hour Customer Care Centre on +94 11 235 0000 or continue using the existing Standard Chartered customer hotline on +94 11 248 0480. Calls to this number are now routed to DFCC Bank.\n\nThe customers may also visit any DFCC Bank branch or access information and support through www.dfcc.lk/welcome."
  },
