    "md5": "9cfcc96125f1dbd692b7795f9815a9d9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1959,
    "chunk_text": "Standard Chartered sharpens  Sri Lanka strategy around corporate and investment banking\n\nStandard Chartered is sharpening its focus in Sri Lanka around corporate and investment banking, following the divestment of its wealth and retail banking business, as the lender aligns its local operations with its broader global strategy.\n\nThe bank said the shift would allow it to concentrate resources on areas where it has sufficient scale and can offer a more distinctive proposition, particularly to corporates, multinationals and financial institutions.\n\n\u201cStandard Chartered\u2019s focus on corporate and investment banking reflects a clear strategic direction: to concentrate on areas where we can deliver our strongest and most distinctive value to clients, institutions and the wider economy. The divestment of our wealth and retail banking business reflects a strategic decision, in line with our global strategy, to focus resources where we have the necessary scale and most distinctive proposition,\u201d said Standard Chartered Sri Lanka CEO Bingumal Thewarathanthri.\n\nThrough its corporate and investment banking business, Standard Chartered provides transaction banking, financing, risk management, advisory and market solutions to corporate and institutional clients.\n\nIts financial institutions business in Sri Lanka also operates as a banker to the local banks, providing cash and trade solutions that support cross-border payments, liquidity management and trade flows.\n\nDrawing on its network across Asia, Africa and the Middle East, Standard Chartered connects Sri Lankan businesses and financial institutions with international trade corridors, capital flows and investment opportunities.\n\nThe bank said this role becomes particularly important when access to international markets and banking appetite are constrained. It supports the local banks with cross-border trade requirements, including letters of credit, guarantees and financing solutions."
  },
