    "chunk_size_bytes": 1463,
    "chunk_text": "The bank said this role becomes particularly important when access to international markets and banking appetite are constrained. It supports the local banks with cross-border trade requirements, including letters of credit, guarantees and financing solutions.\n\nFor Sri Lankan corporates pursuing cross-border expansion, the bank provides access to international markets, counterparties and financing expertise. Its support covers trade, cash management, foreign exchange, risk management and capital solutions, helping clients structure transactions, manage liquidity and navigate complex global conditions.\n\nStandard Chartered has operated in Sri Lanka for more than 130 years, supporting trade, connecting businesses with overseas markets and bringing international banking expertise to the local clients.\n\nThe bank said its long-standing presence provides continuity, while the sharper focus on corporate and investment banking would position it to serve clients whose requirements are becoming more sophisticated, international and closely linked to Sri Lanka\u2019s economic recovery.\n\nAs Sri Lanka moves through economic recovery and reform, Standard Chartered said it would continue serving businesses, financial institutions and investors while connecting the country with international markets. The bank added that its purpose of driving commerce and prosperity and its \u201cHere for good\u201d brand promise would continue to guide its operations in Sri Lanka."
