    "md5": "bcedacf89dd8b88ba78523c78a3b6b1e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1437,
    "chunk_text": "Our intention is to increase the tenure of most of the Professions   -Chathuranga Abeysinghe, Deputy Minister of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development\n\n\u201cIn our manifesto itself we have mentioned that we will not re-invent the wheel, but we will start from where we have left\u201d-Chathuranga Abeysinghe, Deputy Minister of Industry and Entrepreneurship\n\nWe have already started an employee up skilling programme especially for our Development Officers\n\nThe only way for government organizations to be efficient is by making their task simpler and bringing in technology\n\nThe Deputy Minister of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Chathuranga Abeysinghe in an interview with Daily Mirror said that the Government is weak in communicating its long-term objectives to the public and he believes that the coordination between Ministries should improve. He further said that the Government will be introducing Strategic Investment Act, SOE Management Act and Private Public Partnership Act. The Minister added that they will abide by their Manifesto and will take steps to abolish the Executive Presidency. Excerpts of the interview:\n\nQIrrespective of the opposition\u2019s claims that the government has failed to attract new investors, you stated a few weeks ago that the government plans to enact key reforms within the next three months to attract investment and boost exports. How do you intend to move forward with these reforms?"
