    "chunk_text": "The strategy itself is having a technological platform. Because of that you could train people while on the job. What we feel is that the only way for government organizations to be efficient is by making their task simpler and bringing in technology. If other countries have done it we should also be able to do it too.\n\nI think the government has been a little weak in communicating its long-term objectives and reforms to the public. That is a weakness that needs to be corrected. At the same time we could have done better in inter-ministerial coordination and getting a cohesive strategy or a game plan which again we could have done better. Also, we could have done better in terms of industrial land and readiness for industries for infrastructure, which we are struggling but we could have done better. There needs to be more coordination and speed in industrial, land preparation and infrastructure readiness. This is from my Ministry\u2019s perspective.\n\nGovernment is trying to improve communication in each Ministry. Staff members are being trained and there is a cohesive communication plan that\u2019s been implemented and various methods of reaching to public both physically and digitally. We would see improvement by the completion of the second year. We are planning to communicate the substantial changes the government has brought into every sector, so that people can be clear.\n\nQThere is an ongoing debate that increasing the retirement age of judges is an attempt by the government to influence the composition of the judiciary. How do you respond to these concerns?"
