    "chunk_text": "Government is trying to improve communication in each Ministry. Staff members are being trained and there is a cohesive communication plan that\u2019s been implemented and various methods of reaching to public both physically and digitally. We would see improvement by the completion of the second year. We are planning to communicate the substantial changes the government has brought into every sector, so that people can be clear.\n\nQThere is an ongoing debate that increasing the retirement age of judges is an attempt by the government to influence the composition of the judiciary. How do you respond to these concerns?\n\nThe other fact is that I will not agree with the argument that they bring saying that this is an ad hoc thing. I say this because we can to do this change at any point that we wish; whether now or next year even afterwards. The same logic would be presented by the opposition.\n\nWe are also in discussion with the Digital Ministry on of a particular platform that can do end to end servicing which will be part of the entity that is going to be called EITA- Entrepreneurship and Industry Transformation Agency. That will be digital first organization. With that we are confident\n\nAnyway, the existing judges\u2019 retirement will increase at any point. We don\u2019t see a rationale behind why such a resistance is coming. If there is a proper case, we would like to listen to it.\n\nQThere are allegations that politically sensitive investigations progress more slowly than investigations involving ordinary members of the public. Do you agree with this? If not, why?"
