    "chunk_size_bytes": 1539,
    "chunk_text": "Anyway, the existing judges\u2019 retirement will increase at any point. We don\u2019t see a rationale behind why such a resistance is coming. If there is a proper case, we would like to listen to it.\n\nQThere are allegations that politically sensitive investigations progress more slowly than investigations involving ordinary members of the public. Do you agree with this? If not, why?\n\nThere is no reason for us to pick and choose among cases. Just because of complexity and time lapses of some of these cases, some may observe that the recent ones (Cases) are being brought faster than the older cases.\n\nQThe NPP\u2019s election manifesto included a pledge to abolish the executive presidency. It has now been two years since the party assumed power, yet no concrete action has been taken on this issue. Does the NPP intend to contest the 2029 Presidential Election with the executive presidency still in place, or will it be abolished before that?\n\nOur current understanding still is that we will abide by the manifesto. This has been clearly articulated by the Prime Minister in Parliament. The intention is to adhere to the majority of the demands made regarding the manifesto. And we also know that the Constitution and the changes to be made are complex and take time. In our manifesto itself we have mentioned that we will not re-invent the wheel, but we will start from where we have left. Therefore, we still believe that there are three more years to start this debate and bring reforms that are in line with our promises to the people."
