    "md5": "06c49aa95af571f3aa9167c6d207593f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1726,
    "chunk_text": "KPMG webinar on understanding Sri Lanka\u2019s recent tax reforms: Navigating complexity with confidence\n\nPrincipal \u2013 Head of Tax and Regulatory Suresh R. I. Perera /\u00a0Director \u2013 Tax and Regulatory\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s evolving tax framework has introduced a range of legislative changes that require careful interpretation by businesses and tax professionals alike. While several amendments are relatively straightforward, others contain complex provisions and unresolved ambiguities that could significantly influence tax compliance and financial decision-making. Understanding these developments is becoming increasingly important for organisations seeking to remain compliant while making informed strategic decisions.\n\nTo help professionals gain greater clarity, KPMG Sri Lanka Academy will host a webinar that examines selected complicated tax issues arising from the recent reforms. The session will provide practical guidance on determining the appropriate basis of tax computation, interpreting complex provisions within the legislation, and understanding the implications of the revised income tax computation methodology.\n\nThe webinar will be conducted by Principal \u2013 Head of Tax and Regulatory Suresh R. I. Perera, Director \u2013 Tax and Regulatory Hasna Hassan, and Principal \u2013 Tax and Regulatory Rifka Ziyard. Their combined expertise will provide participants with valuable insights into current legislative challenges and practical considerations for businesses operating in today\u2019s changing tax environment.\n\nThose interested in participating or obtaining further information may contact Seneli Jayatunge on 077 444 6649 or via [email\u00a0protected], or Nirosha De Silva on 071 723 6842 or via [email\u00a0protected]."
