    "chunk_text": "SLEIS 2026 to spotlight investment opportunities and economic reform\n\nThe Ceylon Chamber of Commerce Chairperson\u00a0Krishan Balendra /\u00a0EDB Chairman Mangala Wijesinghe /\u00a0Director General of Commerce (Actg.) Somasena Mahadiulwewa /\u00a0BOI Board Member Vish Govindasamy\n\nThe Sri Lanka Economic and Investment Summit 2026 (SLEIS 2026), organised by The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce, will open with a high-level investment-focused panel discussion, bringing together leaders from the public and private sectors to examine Sri Lanka\u2019s investment landscape and the opportunities emerging as the country advances its economic reform agenda.\n\nThe session, which will be held on the opening day of the summit, will explore opportunities across priority sectors, the policy, regulatory and institutional support available to investors, and the reforms needed to strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s competitiveness as an investment destination.\n\nIt will also examine how stronger collaboration between government and the private sector can accelerate investment, drive economic growth and create long-term value for the country.\n\nThe panel will feature The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce Chairperson Krishan Balendra, Export Development Board Chairman Mangala Wijesinghe, Director General of Commerce (Actg.) Somasena Mahadiulwewa, and Board of Investment Board Member Vish Govindasamy."
