    "md5": "64f2996fc62e90c3f5a8cb01c8afaca6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1985,
    "chunk_text": "CIC Holdings reports strong 20% profit growth in 1Q, group assets exceed Rs. 100 b\n\nDiversified conglomerate CIC Holdings PLC recorded continued revenue growth during the first quarter ended 30 June 2026 (1QFY27), delivering improved profitability despite a challenging operating environment.\n\nThe group posted consolidated revenue of Rs. 22.03 billion, reflecting 2.74% year-on-year growth, driven by resilient performance across its diversified portfolio.\n\nGroup gross profit rose to Rs. 6.01 billion, an increase of 10.26% YoY, with gross margins improving to approximately 27.3%. Group operating profit increased by 12.70% to Rs. 3.20 billion, reflecting disciplined execution, improved operational efficiencies, and stronger contributions from key business sectors. Profit after tax increased by a commendable 19.69% to Rs. 1.81 billion, while profit attributable to equity holders of the Company increased by a significant 23.24% to Rs. 1.51 billion.\n\nCIC\u2019s Agri Solutions segment remained the Group\u2019s largest contributor, accounting for approximately 45% of total segmental revenue. Livestock Solutions and Health & Personal Care contributed approximately 22% each, while Industrial Solutions accounted for approximately 12% of total revenue.\n\nThe quarter was characterised by a strong recovery in Livestock Solutions and Industrial Solutions, with both revenue and profitability recording significant growth. Livestock Solutions continued to benefit from higher feed volumes, poultry demand, and growth in veterinary care, while Industrial Solutions recorded robust growth supported by improved market demand and execution.\n\nAlthough Agri Solutions experienced a decline compared to the corresponding period owing to seasonal factors, it remained the Group\u2019s largest business segment and continued to underpin overall performance. Health & Personal Care maintained stable growth, supported by the continued performance of pharmaceuticals and consumer healthcare products."
  },
