    "chunk_size_bytes": 1689,
    "chunk_text": "Although Agri Solutions experienced a decline compared to the corresponding period owing to seasonal factors, it remained the Group\u2019s largest business segment and continued to underpin overall performance. Health & Personal Care maintained stable growth, supported by the continued performance of pharmaceuticals and consumer healthcare products.\n\nDuring the period under review, key Group businesses under the four operating sectors, namely Agri Solutions, Livestock Solutions, Industrial Solutions, and Health and Personal Care, demonstrated resilience. Livestock Solutions revenue increased from Rs. 4.45 billion to Rs. 4.90 billion, while Industrial Solutions recorded the strongest top-line growth, increasing from Rs. 1.87 billion to Rs. 2.63 billion. Health & Personal Care revenue increased from Rs. 4.73 billion to Rs. 4.80 billion, while Agri Solutions recorded revenue of Rs. 9.97 billion.\n\nIn terms of profitability, Livestock Solutions recorded the strongest segmental profit growth, increasing by 111.37% to Rs. 660.25 million, while Industrial Solutions grew by 62.22% to Rs. 533.90 million. Agri Solutions remained the largest profit contributor at Rs. 1.08 billion, while Health and Personal Care contributed Rs. 662.51 million. Overall, net segmental results increased by 11.84% to Rs. 2.94 billion, reflecting broad-based operational resilience across the Group.\n\nThe Group\u2019s earnings per share increased from Rs. 0.65 to Rs. 0.80, reflecting a 23.08% year-on-year improvement. Total assets surpassed the Rs. 100 billion milestone to reach Rs. 100.14 billion, while total equity increased to Rs. 55.69 billion, further strengthening the Group\u2019s financial position."
