    "chunk_size_bytes": 1982,
    "chunk_text": "n Introducing age-appropriate and ethically grounded learning in artificial intelligence, coding and digital literacy.\n\nn Strengthening English-language proficiency while preserving excellence in Sinhala and Tamil.\n\nn Reforming assessment systems to measure understanding and competence rather than memorisation.\n\nn Creating pathways for lifelong learning, reskilling and continuous professional development.\n\nn Strengthening civic education, ethics, constitutional understanding and responsible citizenship.\n\nn Education reform must become a national mission rather than a collection of disconnected policy initiatives.\n\nDiscussions about education reform frequently begin with universities, technology and graduate employment. However, national transformation must begin much earlier.\n\nA child who does not acquire strong literacy, numeracy, communication and reasoning skills during the primary years will find it increasingly difficult to benefit from advanced science, technology or vocational education later.\n\nArtificial intelligence and digital education cannot compensate for weak foundations. Technology becomes transformative only when learners possess the basic knowledge, discipline and reasoning skills required to use it wisely.\n\nA national education system cannot be considered successful when opportunity depends upon a student\u2019s district, income, language, disability, school category or access to private tuition.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s reform agenda must therefore address the circumstances of rural, estate-sector and low-income students; children with disabilities; students in underserved provinces; and those without reliable access to teachers, laboratories, libraries, devices and internet connectivity.\n\nA National Education Equity Guarantee should establish minimum standards for every school. These should include access to qualified teachers, safe classrooms, sanitation, libraries, science facilities, digital connectivity, counselling and learning support."
  },
