    "chunk_size_bytes": 1667,
    "chunk_text": "The Committee for the Protection of Prisoners' Rights has attributed the incident to severe overcrowding at the facility. Chairman of the Committee, Attorney-at-Law Senaka Perera, alleged that conditions inside prisons have deteriorated due to the excessive number of inmates being held beyond the facilities' capacity.\n\nEarlier, Cabinet Spokesman and Minister Nalinda Jayatissa said the country's prison population had increased from around 28,000 to more than 40,000 since the government assumed office in 2024. He attributed much of the increase to intensified anti-narcotics operations carried out under the \"Ratama Ekata\" programme.\n\nThe rapid growth in the inmate population has placed considerable pressure on the prison system, prompting the government to accelerate measures to expand capacity and improve prison conditions.\n\nAs part of these efforts, the government has begun recruiting additional prison officers and implementing several development projects. Construction work has been completed at the Pallekele Prison, while new buildings at the Pallansena Prison have also been commissioned. The Mahara Prison storage complex was completed in 2025, and temporary accommodation facilities are being completed at Welikada, Magazine, and Colombo prisons to reduce congestion.\n\nThe Minister also said that a high-security prison facility has been established at the Welisara Navy Camp to accommodate inmates requiring enhanced security arrangements.\n\nFurther prison development projects are planned between 2026 and 2029 at Pallekele, Wataraka, Kalutara, Kuruvita, and Matara.\n\nPrison population surges to over 42,000 following \u2019Ratama Ekata\u2019 operation"
