    "chunk_size_bytes": 1808,
    "chunk_text": "Two remanded over alleged multi-million rupee Customs fraud involving luxury vehicles\n\nColombo, August 4 (Daily Mirror) - Two suspects, including the son of the owner of a well-known gate manufacturing and motor vehicle importing company, were ordered to be remanded till August 5 by Colombo Additional Magistrate Oshadha Migara Maharachchi over allegations of evading taxes amounting to millions of rupees through the import of luxury vehicles and raw materials for the construction sector.\n\nThe suspects, Achini Tharaka Mihirani Dias, an employee of the company and Athila Ravinaka Weeraratne, were remanded.\n\nThe order was made after the Magistrate considered submissions made by officials of the Sri Lanka Customs Department, who appeared before court on behalf of the investigation.\n\nCustoms officials informed court that an investigation was being conducted into allegations that goods had been imported by declaring lower values, causing a loss of revenue to the government.\n\nThe officials told court that investigations had revealed that a Mercedes-Benz vehicle had been imported by declaring an undervalued price, resulting in a loss of Rs. 4.1 million in government taxes.\n\nThey further stated that an examination of invoices belonging to the company had revealed information relating to the import of goods valued at USD 49,815.75 through an invoice, the issuing of letters of credit amounting to USD 19,926.30 and the import of goods valued at USD 29,889.45.\n\nThe Customs officials also requested the court to impose overseas travel bans on three directors of the company in connection with the investigation.\n\nAppearing for the suspect, President\u2019s Counsel Nalinda Indatissa informed court that the investigating officers had failed to submit a proper summary of evidence against the suspects."
  },
