    "chunk_text": "The Customs officials also requested the court to impose overseas travel bans on three directors of the company in connection with the investigation.\n\nAppearing for the suspect, President\u2019s Counsel Nalinda Indatissa informed court that the investigating officers had failed to submit a proper summary of evidence against the suspects.\n\nThe President\u2019s Counsel further submitted that according to previous Supreme Court decisions, proper evidence must be presented before court, and that no such summary of evidence had been submitted to court in relation to the ongoing investigation.\n\nMeanwhile, the investigating officers informed court that further suspects were expected to be arrested in connection with the incident.\n\nThey opposed bail, stating that if the suspects were released, there was a possibility of evidence being destroyed or interfered with.\n\nAfter considering submissions from both parties, the Magistrate ordered that the suspects be remanded till August 5 and directed the investigators to submit a progress report on the investigation on that date."
