    "chunk_size_bytes": 714,
    "chunk_text": "Eight dead, nearly 12,000 affected by adverse weather\n\nColombo, August 4 (Daily Mirror) - Eight people have lost their lives due to the adverse weather conditions that have affected several parts of the country over the past few days, the Disaster Management Centre (DMC) said.\n\nAccording to the DMC\u2019s latest situation report issued this evening (4), the severe weather has impacted 56 Divisional Secretariat divisions across nine districts.\n\nThe report said a total of 11,832 people from 3,014 families have been affected by the prevailing weather conditions, while three others sustained injuries.\n\nThe DMC also reported damage to property, with one house completely destroyed and 290 houses partially damaged."
