    "md5": "cca9b45c2c35c772fecdd1b4511395ac",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1898,
    "chunk_text": "\u2019It was a rebirth for all of us\u2019: Passengers recall chaos after Air India flight hits turbulence\n\nTimes of India - An Air India flight from Phuket to Delhi encountered severe turbulence on Tuesday morning, briefly losing around 300 feet in altitude and leaving at least 17 people injured, including four cabin crew members.\n\nFlight AI2379, operated by an Airbus A320 aircraft, landed safely at Indira Gandhi International Airport around 11.30am.\n\nThe aircraft had 134 passengers and eight crew members on board, news agency PTI reported.\n\nThe Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA) has launched a probe into the incident.\n\nA passenger onboard the flight described the turbulence as an extremely frightening experience, saying his father was thrown into the air and hit the aircraft\u2019s roof, while his mother, wife and two-year-old daughter also suffered injuries.\n\n\u201cMy father was sitting on the aisle seat and was having coffee. He was not wearing a seat belt as there was no mandatory light for it. Suddenly, a big jolt happened, and he flew and hit the roof and fell on the floor,\u201d the passenger said.\n\nHe said his mother suffered swelling after hitting her head against the overhead cabin, while a part of the overhead compartment also struck her near the left eye, news agency ANI reported.\n\nHis wife and two-year-old daughter were also thrown into the aisle during the turbulence.\n\nThe child suffered a head injury and swelling and was treated at the airport.\n\nThe family was later discharged after doctors assessed their injuries as minor and travelled to Chandigarh by road.\n\n\u201cI would say that it was a rebirth for all of us. There were screams and my elder daughter, who is five years old, was so scared, as were we all,\u201d he said.\n\nThe passenger also praised the pilot and cabin crew for helping passengers remain calm and called for a thorough inquiry into the incident."
  },
