    "md5": "1aac47e3a0b7632bb611f80387a3c6ee",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2008,
    "chunk_text": "Welcoming Anchor Sports, Anil Mohan, Chairman and CEO of Innovative Production Group, the tournament rights holder, said: \u201cWe welcome Anchor Sports on board and to the LPL family as they take over the iconic Jaffna franchise. Jaffna has been a legendary team in the six-year history of the league, winning four championship titles and setting the benchmark for excellence. We are confident that Anchors Sports will build on this remarkable legacy, bring fresh vision and energy to the franchise and continue to elevate the standard of the Lanka Premier League. We look forward to an exciting new chapter for Jaffna and wish the new ownership every success.\u201d\n\nSamantha Dodanwela, Tournament Director, Lanka Premier League, said: \"Having an owner of Zaheer Khan's calibre involved with the Jaffna Anchor is a real boost for the league. The mentorship and direction he can offer our young Sri Lankan players will be enormous, and we're excited to see that experience passed on both on and off the field.\" - source:cricbuzz\n\nFIFA President Gianni Infantino has called an emergency executive meeting in Rabat, Morocco, as criticism continues to mount over his controversial proposal to sell parts of FIFA's commercial and event operations.\n\nSenior FIFA figures, including Ars\u00e8ne Wenger, Secretary General Mattias Grafstr\u00f6m and Prince Ali bin Al Hussein, have publicly opposed the plan. Wenger said the proposal had to be withdrawn, stressing the need for \"transparency and integrity\" within FIFA.\n\nThe controversy has already claimed one resignation, with senior adviser Carlos Cordeiro stepping down after calling the proposal \"a bad deal for football.\"\n\nIndia Test squad arrives in Sri Lanka for World Test Championship Series\n\nThe Indian Test cricket team arrived in Sri Lanka today (4) ahead of a two-match series against the hosts in the 2025\u20132027 ICC World Test Championship.\n\nThe team landed at Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA) at 3:50 p.m. on SriLankan Airlines flight UL 1144 from Mumbai."
