    "chunk_text": "The Indian Test cricket team arrived in Sri Lanka today (4) ahead of a two-match series against the hosts in the 2025\u20132027 ICC World Test Championship.\n\nThe team landed at Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA) at 3:50 p.m. on SriLankan Airlines flight UL 1144 from Mumbai.\n\nIndia will face Sri Lanka in the upcoming two-Test series as both teams continue their campaign in the ICC World Test Championship cycle.\n\nArs\u00e8ne Wenger has backed FIFA\u2019s decision to scrap its controversial private investment plan, saying the move was \u201cabsolutely necessary\u201d to protect the independence of world football\u2019s governing body.\n\nFIFA President Gianni Infantino had proposed creating a commercial subsidiary to manage major tournaments, including the FIFA World Cup, allowing private investors to buy stakes in the venture.\n\nThe plan was withdrawn following strong opposition from UEFA and several FIFA member associations.\n\nIn a statement, Wenger said he was not involved in developing the proposal and only learned about it through media reports. He stressed that FIFA must operate with transparency, integrity and independence.\n\nThe proposal also led to the resignation of senior FIFA adviser Carlos Cordeiro, who described the plan as \u201ca bad deal for football\u201d that could have affected the sport\u2019s future."
