    "chunk_text": "WISTA Sri Lanka reappoints Chamila Bandara as President\n\nThe Women in Shipping and Trading Association (WISTA) Sri Lanka successfully held its 11th Annual General Meeting recently at The Kingsbury Hotel.\n\nSri Lanka Ports Authority Chairman Dr. Parakrama Dissanayake graced the event as the chief guest.\n\nThe highlight of the evening was the presentation of the prestigious WISTA Sri Lanka Personality of the Year Award to Worldlink Shipping Colombo (Pvt.) Ltd Director Marketing Swabha Wickremesinghe, in recognition of her outstanding contributions made to the maritime and logistics sectors.\n\nChamila Bandara was unanimously reappointed as President of WISTA Sri Lanka for another term, reflecting on the confidence and trust placed in her leadership by the membership.\n\nShe serves as a Member of the Group Management Committee of Hayleys Advantis Limited and Director of Advantis Express licensee of FedEx and IML Delivery Systems.\n\nMeridian Maritime Services Director Operations Maleena Awn was re-elected as Vice President, Centrum Marine Consultancy Director Patali Karunarathne was re-elected as Secretary, Hayleys Advantis General Manager Assurance and Insurance Shiyamalee Karunanayake was re-elected as Treasurer, GAC Marine Services Manager Operations Felicita Alwis was elected as Assistant Secretary and McLarens Lubricants Director Finance Hannelore Baldsing was re-elected as Assistant Treasurer."
