    "chunk_text": "Under existing Indian EPF regulations, members are eligible to withdraw their benefits after reaching the age of 58. However, many Sri Lankan workers have faced difficulties in accessing their funds due to practical issues, including challenges in maintaining or operating Indian bank accounts.\n\nThe Indian delegation at the talks was led by P. S. Gangadhar, while the Sri Lankan delegation was headed by Commissioner General of Labour Nadeeka Wataliyadda. Senior officials from the Ministry of Labour, Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism participated in the discussions."
