    "chunk_text": "The financial burden of this administrative bottleneck has been substantial. The audit report details that while Cabinet approval was granted in 2023 to appoint transaction advisors, a sum of Rs. 193 million was paid in 2024 to two foreign firms, utilising the Ministry of Finance\u2019s general deposit account 18/62P. Despite this heavy expenditure on external expertise, the Auditor General explicitly states that the objectives of establishing the restructuring unit had not been achieved by the end of 2024.\n\nBetween 2023 and the end of 2025, an additional Rs. 157.7 million was incurred merely to maintain the administrative unit. The audit report firmly concludes that despite the Rs. 350.7 million total financial outlay, the intended restructuring mandate remained unfulfilled, casting significant doubt on the execution and financial accountability of the divestiture programme."
