    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka possesses the professional expertise within its security and disaster management institutions to close these gaps. What has been lacking is a coherent, whole-of-government approach that treats reliable communication as a strategic national asset rather than a technical afterthought, and that insists on continuous skill development among those who lead. The cost of continued failure is measured not only in lives and economic damage, but in the steady erosion of public confidence in the state\u2019s ability to protect its citizens.\n\n(This analysis is offered in the interest of national security, institutional reform, and public safety)\n\nFormer Deputy Director in Charge, Counter-Terrorism Desk, State Intelligence Service (2005\u20132009) Former Director, Police Special Branch and former First Secretary (defense) Sri Lanka Embassy \u2013 Thailand)"
