    "md5": "fcc5aee440f3f6fde5729ab1eebcec99",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1918,
    "chunk_text": "Rush Metropolis secures BOI approval\n\nRush Lanka senior management receive the official BOI approval for Rush Metropolis from BOI Chairman Duminda Hulangamuwa (right)\n\nRush Lanka Group yesterday said its flagship residential development, Rush Metropolis in Dehiwala, recently received approval from the Board of Investment (BOI) of Sri Lanka.\n\nThe approval, reinforces the company\u2019s commitment to developing high-quality residential projects that meet stringent regulatory and governance standards while offering greater confidence to homebuyers and investors, the company said in a statement.\n\nThe official recognition was received at the Board of Investment, with Rush Lanka\u2019s Managing Director Sabeer Iqbal, Director Zaid Ariff, General Manager Irfan Rafeek and Finance Manager Zulfihar Ali representing the company.\n\nRush Metropolis is set to redefine urban living in Dehiwala as the area\u2019s first high-rise residential development. Comprising 125 contemporary apartments, the project combines modern architecture with lifestyle-focused amenities, including a swimming pool, children\u2019s pool, fully equipped gymnasium, dedicated children\u2019s play area and an exclusive rooftop entertainment space designed to foster community living.\n\nCommenting on the achievement, Rush Lanka Director Zaid Ariff said the company has consistently placed transparency, quality and regulatory compliance at the core of every development.\n\n\u201cAt Rush Lanka Group, transparency and regulatory compliance have always been at the heart of how we build. From CIDA LB1 grading to ISO certification and Certificates of Conformity, we believe buyers deserve to make informed decisions backed by genuine credentials\u2014not just promises. Receiving BOI approval for Rush Metropolis is another affirmation of our commitment to delivering developments that meet the highest standards of quality, governance and long-term value,\u201d he said."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
