    "md5": "b00f53c965f3004239e557a5e98d805d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1825,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cAt Rush Lanka Group, transparency and regulatory compliance have always been at the heart of how we build. From CIDA LB1 grading to ISO certification and Certificates of Conformity, we believe buyers deserve to make informed decisions backed by genuine credentials\u2014not just promises. Receiving BOI approval for Rush Metropolis is another affirmation of our commitment to delivering developments that meet the highest standards of quality, governance and long-term value,\u201d he said.\n\nFor homebuyers, this provides an added layer of assurance that the project is being developed within a recognised regulatory framework, supported by structured governance and oversight.\n\nBOI approval also strengthens the credibility of a development by demonstrating that the project has satisfied additional regulatory requirements beyond standard approvals. It reflects careful project planning, sound corporate governance and a long-term commitment by the developer to responsible business practices.\n\nThe recognition is particularly valuable for overseas Sri Lankans and international investors, as BOI-approved condominium developments are often structured to facilitate foreign investment, subject to prevailing Sri Lankan laws and regulations.\n\nAs such the BOI approval serves as an important benchmark alongside certifications such as CIDA grading, ISO standards and Certificates of Conformity. Collectively, these credentials provide buyers with greater confidence that they are investing in a professionally managed development built on strong regulatory foundations.\n\nWith Rush Metropolis now securing BOI approval, Rush Lanka Group continues to reinforce its position as a trusted developer committed to delivering quality residential communities that combine modern living with transparency, compliance and long-term value."
  },
