    "chunk_size_bytes": 1632,
    "chunk_text": "Clash between Minister and Deputy Minister reaches boiling point over SriLankan Airlines\n\nColomob, Aug. 5 (Daily Mirror) - A major administrative crisis has erupted within the Government, as the clash between Ports and Civil Aviation Minister Anura Karunathilake and Deputy Minister Janitha Kodithuwakku reaches boiling point over the controversial push to appoint an interim Chief Executive Officer at loss-making SriLankan Airlines, according several sources within Sri Lankan Airlines.\n\nAccording to them, the friction peaked on Monday when the Minister directly intervened in a formal inquiry convened by his Deputy to reinstate a suspended airline employee. They noted that the Minister effectively undermined the proceedings by delaying the inquiry from the morning until the evening before shutting down the session prematurely. Although the aviation portfolio falls under the purview of the Deputy Minister, it was emphasized that ministerial interference continues to stall efforts to resolve serious administrative disputes at the national carrier.\n\nThe escalating power struggle comes against the backdrop of a prolonged and heavily criticized leadership vacuum at the airline. During a recent parliamentary Sectoral Oversight Committee hearing, Chairman MP S. M. Marikkar directed sharp criticism at the carrier's 16-month failure to appoint a CEO. Pointing to the inability to secure a candidate despite calling two interview rounds that yielded hundreds of applications, it was highlighted as a tragic situation that the airline could not find a suitable external or internal candidate for over a year and four months."
