    "chunk_text": "The escalating power struggle comes against the backdrop of a prolonged and heavily criticized leadership vacuum at the airline. During a recent parliamentary Sectoral Oversight Committee hearing, Chairman MP S. M. Marikkar directed sharp criticism at the carrier's 16-month failure to appoint a CEO. Pointing to the inability to secure a candidate despite calling two interview rounds that yielded hundreds of applications, it was highlighted as a tragic situation that the airline could not find a suitable external or internal candidate for over a year and four months.\n\nHowever, the move to elevate the Head of IT was abruptly stalled after a widespread social media campaign surfaced, exposing severe allegations of corrupt activities within the airline's IT department.\n\nA formal grievance letter warned of a \"serious escalation of mismanagement in the IT division under the stewardship of Mr. Chamara Perera\". The document further alleged that Perera \"has become a serious threat to the future of the Airlines Business and serious damage to the professional outlook of the organisation and its culture\".\n\nWhile the public backlash prompted the Minister to temporarily hold back the official appointment for the time being, he remains determined to push ahead with the elevation as interim CEO.\n\nAdding to the tension, the JVP-affiliated union remains deeply frustrated after being entirely excluded from Monday's inquiry, with union representatives forced to wait by the door outside the proceedings.\n\nAccording to several sources. The union is now planning to take action against the alleged corrupt activities of the IT head, ahead of his potential appointment, further intensifying the operational and political friction surrounding SriLankan Airlines."
