    "chunk_size_bytes": 1188,
    "chunk_text": "The MP also requested a sector-wise breakdown of funds allocated under the 2026 Budget for El Ni\u00f1o preparedness and response, including allocations for agriculture, irrigation, disaster management, drinking water, public health, electricity generation and emergency relief, together with any allocations expected to continue into 2027.\n\nHe also asked what contingency measures had been implemented to safeguard food production, irrigation, water resources, electricity supply, healthcare services and disaster response, including maintaining adequate reserves of food, seed, medicines, drinking water and emergency relief supplies.\n\nIn addition, the MP questioned what public awareness and preparedness programmes had been implemented, which districts had been identified as being at the highest risk, whether Sri Lanka had sought technical or financial assistance from international organisations including the World Meteorological Organization (WMO), the Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO), the World Bank and the Asian Development Bank (ADB), and why the government had not obtained natural disaster insurance similar to the arrangements made during the 2016/2017 El Ni\u00f1o event."
