    "chunk_text": "Despite the market recovery, foreign investors remained significant net sellers, recording a net foreign outflow of LKR 4.87 billion. This reflected continued foreign selling pressure, particularly through the high-value crossing transactions recorded during the session.\n\nCargills was the strongest positive contributor to the ASPI, adding 15.20 points to the index. Colombo Dockyard, Ceylon Grain Elevators, RIL Property, and Melstacorp also supported the market\u2019s recovery.\n\nCeylinco Insurance was the largest negative contributor, reducing the ASPI by 7.86 points. Commercial Credit and Finance, Commercial Bank, Central Finance, and Richard Pieris also weighed on the index.\n\nOverall, the session reflected a notable improvement in domestic investor sentiment, supported by gains across a broader range of counters. However, the concentration of turnover in crossing transactions and the substantial foreign outflow suggested that underlying market sentiment remained cautious."
