    "chunk_text": "Among the key developments was the exchange of agreements for two Indian Rupee-denominated Lines of Credit worth USD 350 million, including USD 250 million for railway projects and USD 100 million for livestock and other priority sectors.\n\nBoth countries also confirmed that reconstruction of damaged houses and permanent bridges under a USD 100 million grant will begin shortly.\n\nThe rehabilitation of the Northern Railway corridor, funded through a USD 5 million Indian grant, has also been completed, allowing train services to resume.\n\nBoth sides agreed to expedite several major infrastructure and energy projects, including the electricity grid interconnection, the Sampur Solar Power Project and the development of Trincomalee as an energy hub.\n\nThey also pledged to fast-track the Sri Lanka Unique Digital Identity Project and begin discussions on a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) for the rehabilitation and modernisation of Kankesanthurai Harbour under a USD 61.5 million Indian grant.\n\nIndia further reiterated its support for expanding the 1990 Suwa Seriya Ambulance Service and noted that more than 1,000 Sri Lankan professionals have already benefited from capacity-building programmes launched last year.\n\nThe visit reaffirmed India's commitment to implementing the outcomes of the December 2024 Joint Statement issued during President Anura Kumara Disanayake's visit to India, as well as the agreements signed during Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi's visit to Sri Lanka in April 2025."
