    "md5": "b8e27c99bc6b59ecbeceaa9d8e8384dc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1904,
    "chunk_text": "BASL President says he is target of baseless personal attacks\n\nColombo, Aug. 5 (Daily Mirror) - In a Facebook post, Bar Association of Sri Lanka (BASL) President Rajeev Amarasuriya said he has faced several personal attacks over the past few weeks, describing them as \u201cfalse and malicious\u201d and part of a series of baseless personal attacks aimed at undermining him.\n\nHe said this campaign began with allegations that he had entered into a secret deal with the Leader of the Opposition.\n\nThe BASL President has strongly denied allegations of wrongdoing made against him.\n\nHe said the latest allegation was made by Nagananda Kodithuwakku, who, according to Amarasuriya, was found guilty of professional misconduct and removed from the office of Attorney-at-Law by the Supreme Court on February 29, 2024.\n\nAmarasuriya said Kodithuwakku had publicly claimed that his Vinivida Foundation had lodged a complaint against him with the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption.\n\nAccording to Amarasuriya, the complaint relates to matters in which he has appeared, and continues to appear, in his professional capacity together with several President\u2019s Counsel on behalf of the authorised dealer of a motor vehicle manufacturer in Sri Lanka in proceedings before the Court of Appeal and the Supreme Court.\n\nSetting out what he described as the \u201ctrue facts,\u201d Amarasuriya said he had appeared only as counsel duly instructed to represent his client before the courts.\n\nHe further noted that Kodithuwakku himself had appeared on behalf of a respondent and an intervenient petitioner in some of the earlier proceedings but had ceased to do so after being removed from the office of Attorney-at-Law by the Supreme Court.\n\nAmarasuriya categorically rejected the allegations against him, stating that they were \u201cfalse, malicious and, in my view, intended to serve collateral purposes.\u201d"
  },
