    "chunk_text": "He further noted that Kodithuwakku himself had appeared on behalf of a respondent and an intervenient petitioner in some of the earlier proceedings but had ceased to do so after being removed from the office of Attorney-at-Law by the Supreme Court.\n\nAmarasuriya categorically rejected the allegations against him, stating that they were \u201cfalse, malicious and, in my view, intended to serve collateral purposes.\u201d\n\nAmarasuriya also said he would not be deterred by personal attacks.\n\n\u201cWhen one takes principled positions, speaks independently and is prepared to defend institutions and the rule of law, criticism is inevitable. That is part of public life,\u201d he said.\n\nHe added that it was important to remain focused on the truth, continue to discharge professional responsibilities faithfully and allow the facts to speak for themselves.\n\nConcluding his post, the BASL President quoted an old saying: \u201cThe tallest tree catches the most wind.\u201d"
