    "md5": "ce8db0574021cbea823fa0683d025752",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1769,
    "chunk_text": "Regen Renewables and Suntech Power to drive SL\u2019s renewable energy growth\n\nRegen Renewables reinforcing its partnership with global photovoltaic (PV) technology leader Suntech Power\n\nRegen Renewables (Pvt) Ltd is reaffirming its long-standing partnership with Suntech Power, demonstrating a shared commitment to accelerating the country\u2019s transition towards clean energy.\n\nThe milestone was celebrated during Suntech Power\u2019s 25th anniversary celebrations, held alongside InterSolar Europe 2026 in Germany, where the Directors of Regen Renewables were invited as guests in recognition of their longstanding partnership and contribution to expanding Suntech\u2019s presence in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe celebration also marked a significant milestone in Suntech\u2019s growth journey with its strategic partnership with HYSOLAR, strengthening its position as a global industry leader.\u00a0 Suntech has also earned consistent recognition as one of Bloomberg NEF\u2019s Top 10 Most Bankable PV Brands, reflecting the high level of confidence that financial institutions, developers, and investors place in the company\u2019s products, performance, and long-term reliability.\n\nWith over 25 years of photovoltaic expertise, more than 55 GW of modules supplied across over 100 countries, and a portfolio of landmark projects - including Germany\u2019s largest floating solar plant, Japan\u2019s Kanzaki Utility PV Plant, South Africa\u2019s 250 MW Kimberley Droogfontein Solar Plant, San Francisco International Airport Terminal 3, IKEA MLFU Sydney and the Beijing International Stadium BIPV Project, Suntech continues to strengthen its global leadership through innovations such as its Ultra T 3.0 high-efficiency quarter-cut modules, delivering reliable and sustainable clean energy solutions worldwide."
  },
