    "chunk_text": "With over 25 years of photovoltaic expertise, more than 55 GW of modules supplied across over 100 countries, and a portfolio of landmark projects - including Germany\u2019s largest floating solar plant, Japan\u2019s Kanzaki Utility PV Plant, South Africa\u2019s 250 MW Kimberley Droogfontein Solar Plant, San Francisco International Airport Terminal 3, IKEA MLFU Sydney and the Beijing International Stadium BIPV Project, Suntech continues to strengthen its global leadership through innovations such as its Ultra T 3.0 high-efficiency quarter-cut modules, delivering reliable and sustainable clean energy solutions worldwide.\n\nCommenting on the partnership, Suntech Chairman Yang Jianliang said, \u201cOn behalf of Suntech, I would like to express our sincere gratitude for the valuable partnership we have built with Regen over the years. As we proudly celebrate Suntech\u2019s 25th anniversary, we reaffirm our commitment to delivering high-quality, reliable clean energy solutions to the Sri Lankan market. We look forward to deepening our collaboration with Regen and exploring new opportunities for mutual growth in the years ahead.\u201d\n\nSharing his thoughts, Lakmal Fernando, Managing Director of Regen Renewables (Pvt) Ltd said, \u201cOver fourteen years we have shared many successes, overcome many challenges, navigated market changes and adopted evolving technologies. What has remained constant is the professionalism, integrity and friendship of the Suntech team. We are proud to have walked alongside Suntech for fourteen of its twenty-five years, and we look forward to continuing that journey together in the years ahead.\u201d"
