    "chunk_text": "These results highlight the value of combining capacity building, tailored coaching and targeted market access through strong collaboration between the public sector and international development partners.\n\nSpeaking at the inauguration, EDB Chairman and CEO Mangala Wijesinghe said that programmes such as ExpoScaleUp are vital to help Sri Lankan SMEs move from export potential to export success.\n\nThe participants in the third cohort will receive hands-on support to develop Export Marketing Plans tailored to their products, target markets and business goals.\n\nThe eligible companies that successfully complete the programme may also access further international market exposure and business development support through ExpoConnect \u2013 the programme component that connects the SMEs with the global partners.\n\nThrough this continued collaboration, the EDB, IFC and EU aim to develop a stronger pipeline of export-ready SMEs that can compete internationally and contribute to Sri Lanka\u2019s national goal of reaching US $ 36 billion in export earnings by 2030."
