    "md5": "b7e9f47cd9aa6f9d314893739a6cc952",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1451,
    "chunk_text": "Indices close in green\n\nThe ASPI closed in green as a result of price gains in counters such as Cargills, Colombo Dockyard and Ceylon Grain Elevators with the turnover crossing Rs. 8.4 Bn. A similar behaviour was witnessed in the S&P SL20.\n\nCrossings were witnessed in Cargills, Hayleys and Lanka Realty Investments accounting for 72.8% of the turnover. Mixed interest was observed in Commercial Credit & Finance, Sierra Cables and John Keells Holdings whilst retail interest was noted in Industrial Asphalts, HNB Finance and Browns Investments. Furthermore, foreigners remained active closing as net sellers.\n\nFood & Staples Retailing sector was the top contributor to the market turnover (due to Cargills ) whilst the sector index gained 8.95%. The share price of Cargills increased by Rs 32.00 (5.12%) to close at Rs 657.00.\n\nCapital Goods sector was the second highest contributor to the market turnover (due to Hayleys, Sierra Cables and\n\nJohn Keells Holdings) whilst the sector index increased by 0.97%. The share price of Hayleys gained Rs 1.25 (0.56%) to close at Rs 224.00. The share price of Sierra Cables recorded a gain of Rs 2.00 (7.14%) to close at Rs 30.00. The share price of John Keells Holdings appreciated by Rs 0.10 (0.50%) to close at Rs 20.00.\n\nCommercial Credit & Finance was also included amongst the top turnover contributors. The share price of Commercial Credit & Finance moved down by Rs 7.25 (6.42%) to close at Rs 105.75."
