    "chunk_size_bytes": 683,
    "chunk_text": "Harischandra Mills delivers strong first-quarter earnings on revenue surge\n\nHarischandra Mills PLC reported a sharp rise in first-quarter earnings, with profit after tax surging 147 percent year-on-year to Rs.91.9 million for the three months ended June 30, 2026, supported by a double-digit revenue growth and stronger operating profitability across its core businesses. Revenue rose 31 percent to Rs.1.93 billion, from Rs.1.47 billion a year earlier, while gross profit increased 35 percent to Rs.347.5 million, lifting the gross profit margin to 18 percent, from 17 percent in the corresponding period. Other income more than tripled to Rs.22.6 million, further boosting earnings."
