    "description": "Customer-friendly hotlines a must!",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/opinion/Customer-friendly-hotlines-a-must/172-347519",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1785953236.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-05-dailymirrorlk-db8d6aca-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "37350d5a39bfa6525005d2832c11195b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1933,
    "chunk_text": "Customer-friendly hotlines a must!\n\nBefore automation, company phones were answered by human beings within 3 rings to build trust, show respect for time, and to stop callers from hanging up.\n\nHowever, the digital age has reshaped this notion entirely with designated hotlines provided by many organisations includ\u00ading banks and\u00a0 gov\u00adern\u00adment offices where the automated voice calls answered\u00a0 by lengthy recor\u00added mes\u00adsages -- \u201cthis call will be recorded to ensure quality service\u201d,\u00a0 \u201c your call will be answered by one of our customer service representatives\u00a0 or \u201cyour call is important to us, currently all our customer service representatives\u00a0 are busy ,\u00a0 the next available\u00a0 agent\u00a0 will assist you\u201d .\n\nBut this next available agent never answers and keeps the customer on line for unreasonably long time whilst the companies promote their products.\n\nIn many instances cus\u00adtom\u00aders are effect\u00adively pay\u00ading for the privilege of listen\u00ading to the company\u2019s lengthy product and services because they con\u00adtinue to incur mobile or tele\u00adphone charges while they keep on hold,\u00a0 sac\u00adri\u00adficing their valu\u00adable time.\n\nBlindly following these automated response trends typically setup without consideration can lead to inefficiency, overwhelm organisations, aban\u00addoned calls due to cus\u00adtomer frus\u00adtra\u00adtion, losing a vital business deal and unne\u00adces\u00adsary con\u00adges\u00adtion in call centres.\n\nIronically,\u00a0 if the calls are recorded to ensure quality service don\u2019t these companies analyse the waiting time exper\u00adi\u00adenced by cus\u00adtom\u00aders, how many calls have been aban\u00addoned due to the long wait\u00ading time and if the calls are important to these very com\u00adpan\u00adies. Why don\u2019t they ser\u00adi\u00adously consider intro\u00addu\u00adcing more cus\u00adtomer-friendly sys\u00adtems that place greater value on the time of the very people who keep their busi\u00adnesses alive and those who have genu\u00adine griev\u00adances to be sorted?"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
