    "md5": "088cf0d6598c59d2f82b074c6ba1a680",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1584,
    "chunk_text": "In fact, the victim community \u2013 which was mainly concerned about who the culprits behind the terrorist attacks were and what prompted them to kill nearly 300 innocent people \u2013 was sent from pillar to post by\u00a0 successive governments, giving false hopes.\n\nWhile the committee was conducting its probe, a nine- member Parliamentary Select Committee (PSC) headed by Deputy Speaker Ananda Kumarasiri was also appointed to inquire into the same matter on May 22, 2019. The final report of the Committee containing 272 pages was presented to the Parliament on October 23, 2019, but nothing important came out either from the Malalgoda Committee report or the PSC report.\n\nFrustrated by the government\u2019s actions, the Cardinal, during a service at St. Sebastian\u2019s Church in Katuwapitiya which was devastated by Easter Sunday Bombings, stated that the leadership lacked a backbone, had failed the country, and must step down to allow capable individuals to run the government. He seemed to be turning to the then Presidential hopeful, Gotabaya Rajapaksa who was highly critical of the joint administration by President Sirisena and Prime Minister Ranil Wickremesinghe.\n\nRajapaksa and his party, the Sri Lanka Podujana Peramuna (SLPP) assumed office in November 2019, and Cardinal Ranjith expressed satisfaction in the new government\u2019s actions towards revealing the mastermind of the attacks. Prominent politicians such as former Trade Minister Rishard Bathiudeen and his brother Riyad were arrested in connection with the terrorist attacks, on purported strong evidence against them."
  },
