    "chunk_text": "The heart of the proposal is speed with accountability. Every complete submission would receive a named BOI case officer and a clear preliminary decision within the least possible number of working days, and in every case within a month. The month is the outer limit, not the pace. A straightforward case could receive its answer within days, even within a single day.\n\nSuccess would be counted in one currency only, foreign exchange actually received and confirmed through the banking system. Not proposals collected, not meetings held, not investments announced. Verified earnings,\n\nThe next billion dollars Sri Lanka earns may begin as a form filled in on a phone. This proposal was designed for that. Sri Lanka's development would then no longer rest on a handful of institutions or individuals doing their best under pressure. It would be powered by countless minds, inside the country and across the world, all pulling in one direction\n\nThe engineer in Jaffna who knows how to export a testing service. The doctor whose foreign patients ask why they cannot be treated here. The young graduate running a design service for overseas clients from a bedroom in Matara. The retired Customs officer who knows exactly which procedure blocks a re-export opportunity, and exactly how to fix it safely. The Sri Lankan in Melbourne or Milan who sees demand for something this island can supply. The university researcher whose work could become a certification service the whole region would pay for.\n\nToday, a person with such an idea must know someone, or be lucky, or be extraordinarily persistent. An idea travels only as far as its owner's personal contacts, and the country cannot count how many valuable opportunities have quietly died this way, because what is never properly received is never recorded."
