    "chunk_text": "\"This proposal did not come from frustration. It came from confidence,\" Fernando said. \"Our members have watched the country stabilise after its most painful crisis. We believe this recovery has created a short and precious window in which Sri Lanka can build the earning capacity it has lacked for nearly half a century, and we decided the most useful thing we could do was to put a complete, workable mechanism on the table of the institution best placed to run it.\"\n\nThe FTZMA has also addressed the officers of the BOI directly. If the Window opens, they are the ones who will make it real. A case officer who moves a blocked proposal to activation will have done something few public servants ever get to do, put a new stream of foreign exchange into the country's account, visibly and measurably, with the results counted, published and credited. There are few forms of public service where the connection between an officer's work and the nation's benefit is that direct.\n\nThe decision now sits with the Board of Investment, and the Association has expressed its respect and confidence in the leadership now considering it. What could follow is something larger than one proposal changing hands, a Sri Lanka where no good idea dies for want of a door to knock on\n\nThe FTZMA has made clear that it did not hand over this proposal to watch from the gallery. The association has committed to supporting the BOI through implementation. Its member companies will bring forward credible founding cases so that the Window opens with a working pipeline rather than an empty portal, and its engineers, professionals, exporters and managers will share their practical knowledge of where the blocks are. The association has also stated that it will accept the same rules as everyone else, no privileged approvals, every case through the same gateways."
