    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "229151cea674980694a3a8efa4102295",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1945,
    "chunk_text": "Shanakiyan raises concerns over water and land rights and illegal settlements\n\nIlankai Tamil Arasu Kachchi (ITAK) MP Shanakiyan Rasamanickam has raised concerns over the Government\u2019s Mahaweli development plans, including the proposed Kivul Oya Project, land allocation practices and the impact on traditional livelihoods in the Eastern Province.\n\nThe MP said the issues were discussed during a meeting with President Anura Kumara Dissanayake this week, with the President assuring that steps would be taken to address longstanding concerns.\n\nHowever, Rasamanickam said statements made in Parliament by the relevant Minister indicated that the Kivul Oya Project would proceed, requiring consultation with affected communities on land rights, livelihoods and demographic concerns.\n\n\u201cDuring discussion with President Anura Kumara Dissanayake, we held extensive discussions on the long-standing Mahaweli-related issues affecting the people of the Eastern Province. The President assured us that the Government would take the necessary steps to address these longstanding concerns.\n\nHowever, during Parliamentary proceedings, the Minister stated that the Kivul Oya Project is not on hold and that the Government intends to proceed with its implementation. If the Government is to move forward with this project, it must first engage in meaningful consultation with the affected communities and address the long-standing concerns relating to land rights, livelihoods and demographic change.\u201d\n\nRasamanickam said the issue extended beyond water distribution to the manner in which land was being allocated under the Mahaweli Scheme.\n\n\u201cTo date, not a single drop of water has been supplied to the Northern and Eastern Provinces through the Mahaweli Authority. Yet, water has been provided under the Mahaweli Scheme to the districts of Polonnaruwa and Anuradhapura. This reflects a discriminatory approach towards the people of the North and East."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-08-06-dailyftlk-22f89646",
    "num": "dailyftlk-22f89646",
    "date_str": "2026-08-06",
    "description": "Shanakiyan raises concerns over water and land rights and illegal settlements",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/Shanakiyan-raises-concerns-over-water-and-land-rights-and-illegal-settlements/56-795664",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
