    "md5": "350419b6ff53a8cef658baf548cbdd74",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 854,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThe Government had previously stated that Mathavanai would be declared a designated grazing reserve through a Gazette notification. However, the Minister\u2019s response makes it clear that there has been no progress towards fulfilling that commitment. Indeed, the Minister confirmed that even the survey work for the area has yet to be completed.\u201d\n\nHe warned that continued occupation of Mahaweli Authority lands could increase tensions between communities.\n\nI therefore call upon the Government to intervene immediately to prevent further illegal settlements, protect the traditional grazing lands and livelihoods of the Mayilathamadu\u2013Mathavanai livestock farmers, and uphold their rights. I also reiterate that any settlement programme that alters the ethnic demographic composition of the North and East is unacceptable and should not proceed.\u201d"
