    "chunk_text": "Wasp attack leaves over 50 students hospitalised\n\nColombo, Aug. 6 (Daily Mirror) - More than 50 students of Divulwewa Maha Vidyalaya in Trincomalee have been hospitalised after being attacked by wasps, police said.\n\nThe students were stung after a wasp nest located in a school building was disturbed, causing the insects to attack.\n\nThe affected students were admitted to the Mahadivulwewa Hospital for treatment, while three female students who were in a serious condition were transferred to the Trincomalee General Hospital."
