    "md5": "3f02f78c085bb17993bb2c1b0038d242",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 886,
    "chunk_text": "Sajith, government MP clash in Parliament\n\nColombo, Aug. 6 (Daily Mirror) - A verbal clash erupted between Opposition Leader Sajith Premadasa and government MP Susantha Nawaratne in Parliament today.\n\nThe exchange began when MP Nawaratne accused Premadasa of leaving the House after delivering his speech.\n\n\u201cThe Opposition Leader is leaving the Chamber,\u201d he said while responding to a point raised by Premadasa.\n\nResponding to the accusation, the Opposition Leader said he was leaving the Chamber to meet the Speaker and request that MP Chaminda Wijesiri be allowed to attend Parliament.\n\n\u201cWijesiri is being denied his privilege of attending Parliament sessions while in prison. I was going to meet the Speaker about it, not because I cannot face you,\u201d Premadasa said.\n\nMP Nawaratne replied that he had never accused the Opposition Leader of being unable to face the government."
  },
