    "chunk_size_bytes": 1948,
    "chunk_text": "But as the case escalated, he issued a statement urging authorities to examine the CCTV footage \"so the accurate version of events stands clearly revealed\". He also alleged that the case against him was part of a \"political vendetta\" by the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) government in Goa.\n\nTehelka, the magazine Tejpal co-founded in 2000, had published a number of scoops, many of them based on sting operations.\n\nTejpal was arrested in 2013 and spent seven months in jail until the Supreme Court granted him bail.\n\nIn 2021, a sessions court in Goa threw out all the charges against him. But the judge's observations in the 527-page order had sparked criticism after she questioned the behaviour of the survivor..\n\nIn photographs taken shortly after the assault, the judge wrote, the young woman was \"smiling and looked happy, normal, in [a] good mood\".\n\n\"She did not look disturbed, reserved, terrified or traumatised in any way even though this was immediately after she claims to have been sexually assaulted,\" the order said. Some lawyers told the BBC that the judgment itself seemed like \"an assault on the survivorThe Goa government had appealed against this judgment in the high court.\n\nAppearing for the Goa government, Solicitor General Tushar Mehta urged the high court to impose the maximum sentence on Tejpal.\n\n\"This court must give a clear message to society that when a girl says no, it means no. A no means a no,\" Livelaw quoted him as saying.\n\n\"All I can say is I am 62. I believe I am a political victim. I am a father of two daughters. I have a wife. All we can say is we will go up and appeal. My lawyer wants me to request you to be lenient,\" legal website Bar and Bench quoted Tejpal as telling the court.\n\nThe court said it found Tejpal guilty under legal sections including 376(2)(f), which pertains to rape committed by \"a relative, guardian or teacher of, or a person in a position of trust or authority towards the woman\"."
