    "chunk_text": "Five officers assigned for child welfare work in each DS Division\n\nColombo, Aug. 6 (Daily Mirror) - Five officers have been assigned to each Divisional Secretariat Division by the Women and Child Affairs Ministry to strengthen child welfare activities, Ministry Secretary\u00a0 Tharangani Wickramasinghe said today (06).\n\nShe made these remarks while addressing a special media briefing held at the Head Office and Media Centre of the \u201cRatama Ekata\u201d National Campaign to raise awareness on the rescue and rehabilitation of children from the dangers of drugs.\n\nThe Secretary said these officers will also be deployed for programmes conducted under the \u201cRatama Ekata\u201d campaign to rescue children affected by drug abuse, adding that necessary measures will be taken to implement related activities efficiently.\n\nMeanwhile, Deputy Director (Preventive Education and Training) of the National Dangerous Drugs Control Board Pradeep Koholanegedara said the rehabilitation treatment capacity of the institution has been further expanded through the \u201cRatama Ekata\u201d programme to provide enhanced support for children affected by drug-related issues."
