    "md5": "d22b2340e90748bb205192935c0903dc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1952,
    "chunk_text": "ASPI surges for a second day as turnover hits LKR 12.24 Bn\n\nThe Colombo Stock Exchange extended its positive momentum for a second consecutive session on Thursday, 6 August 2026, as broad-based buying interest lifted both benchmark indices despite another substantial foreign outflow.\n\nThe All Share Price Index gained 102.73 points, or 0.49%, to close at 21,269.67, while the S&P Sri Lanka 20 Index advanced by 26.40 points, or 0.44%, to end the session at 5,971.50.\n\nThe ASPI rose strongly during the morning and briefly approached the 21,300 level before easing from its intraday high. The S&P SL20 also remained firmly positive throughout the session, supported by gains in several large-cap counters.\n\nTotal market turnover surged to LKR 12.24 billion, with approximately 231.09 million shares changing hands. However, the exceptionally high level of activity was largely driven by sizeable crossing transactions in Commercial Credit and Finance PLC and United Motors Lanka PLC.\n\nCrossing transactions generated approximately LKR 10.15 billion, accounting for nearly 83% of total equity turnover. Commercial Credit recorded the largest combined crossing activity, with transactions valued at LKR 9.03 billion involving approximately 89.78 million shares.\n\nThe Diversified Financials sector dominated market activity, generating LKR 10.00 billion in turnover from 157.67 million shares. Commercial Credit accounted for the majority of the sector\u2019s activity, recording LKR 9.38 billion in turnover from approximately 93.0 million shares.\n\nCommercial Credit also emerged as the highest individual turnover generator for the session. The counter gained 1.65% to close at LKR 107.50.\n\nDespite the positive market performance, foreign investors remained significant net sellers, recording a net foreign outflow of LKR 7.97 billion. The heavy foreign selling was largely associated with the high-value crossing transactions executed during the session."
  },
