    "chunk_text": "Despite the positive market performance, foreign investors remained significant net sellers, recording a net foreign outflow of LKR 7.97 billion. The heavy foreign selling was largely associated with the high-value crossing transactions executed during the session.\n\nCentral Finance was the strongest positive contributor to the ASPI, adding 13.56 points to the index. Commercial Bank, Cargills, C T Holdings and Hayleys also supported the market\u2019s advance.\n\nCeylinco Insurance was the largest negative contributor, reducing the ASPI by 7.86 points. Bukit Darah, Ceylinco Insurance non-voting, Hatton National Bank and Royal Ceramics also weighed on the index.\n\nOverall, the session reflected strengthening domestic investor sentiment and broad-based buying interest. However, the high concentration of turnover in crossing transactions and the substantial foreign outflow suggested that underlying market participation remained selective."
