    "md5": "66bf78cb1d2e18b593fe4bb97e2f1362",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1563,
    "chunk_text": "President orders urgent overhaul of Sri Lanka Police and unified drug rehab push\n\nColombo, Aug. 6 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake has instructed officials to expedite the modernisation and development of the Sri Lanka Police to ensure the delivery of more efficient and quality services to the public.\n\nEmphasising the need for active participation from all stakeholders in the Government\u2019s \u201cA Nation United\u201d (\u201cRatama Ekata\u201d) national operation launched to eradicate the drug menace, the President highlighted the importance of improving facilities at rehabilitation centres and bringing all rehabilitation institutions under a unified national programme without delay.\n\nThe President issued these directives while participating in a progress review of projects implemented by the Ministry of Public Security and Parliamentary Affairs in 2026, along with a pre-budget discussion for 2027, held today (06) at the Presidential Secretariat.\n\nThe progress of projects implemented under the 2026 Budget allocations by the Ministry of Public Security, Sri Lanka Police, Special Task Force, National Dangerous Drugs Control Board, Bureau of Rehabilitation, National Police Academy, Department of Immigration and Emigration, Department of Civil Security and the Parliamentary Affairs Division was reviewed extensively.\n\nThe meeting also reviewed the progress of programmes implemented under the Rs. 1000 million capital allocation provided for the Government\u2019s \u201cA Nation United\u201d national operation aimed at eliminating the drug menace."
  },
