    "chunk_size_bytes": 1481,
    "chunk_text": "The meeting also focused on the Sri Lanka Police digitalisation programme, modernisation of police uniforms and measures to address health-related issues arising from the demanding duties of police officers. The President\u2019s attention was drawn to proposals submitted by the National Police Academy to prevent the increasing prevalence of non-communicable diseases among police personnel.\n\nIt was further revealed that a three-month family counselling programme is being conducted for individuals who voluntarily seek rehabilitation before they enter rehabilitation programmes. The success of this initiative has contributed to an increase in the number of drug-dependent persons voluntarily seeking rehabilitation in recent months.\n\nSpecial attention was also given to the activities of the Department of Civil Security. Discussions focused on challenges faced in integrating its members, who are deployed across different parts of the country, into national programmes. The President instructed officials to prepare and submit a project proposal addressing these concerns.\n\nThe meeting also noted that discussions have commenced on establishing a formal, integrated rehabilitation process covering the entire country, instead of separate rehabilitation programmes currently operated independently by institutions such as the Department of Social Services, Sri Lanka Police, Ministry of Justice and Ministry of Health. The President instructed officials to expedite this process."
