    "chunk_id": "2026-08-06-dailymirrorlk-158fdd9d-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "26485ab4c69bd883bc9a782933741ee0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1981,
    "chunk_text": "National Business Excellence Awards 2026 Barista wins Gold for  2nd consecutive year\n\nBarista Sri Lanka has been awarded the Gold award in the Hospitality and Tourism Sector at National Business Excellence Awards 2026, organised by the National Chamber of Commerce of Sri Lanka.\n\nThis achievement marks the second consecutive year that Barista has received Gold in the Hospitality and Tourism Sector, reaffirming the company\u2019s contribution to Sri Lanka\u2019s hospitality and tourism industry.\n\nThrough its presence across 17 districts, Barista serves the local customers and international travellers across major cities, tourism destinations and key travel routes. Its network includes Galle and the southern coast, Anuradhapura, Polonnaruwa, Sigiriya, Trincomalee, Jaffna, Nuwara Eliya, Ella and Kandy, enabling the travellers to enjoy a reliable caf\u00e9 experience throughout different stages of their journey across Sri Lanka.\n\nBarista Sri Lanka Director and CEO Dilupa Pathirana stated, \u201cReceiving the Gold award in the Hospitality and Tourism Sector for the second consecutive year is a significant milestone for Barista. It reflects the strength of our strategy, the resilience of our business and the continued trust of our customers, together with the dedication of our employees, franchise partners, suppliers and stakeholders.\n\nFrom the beginning, our focus has been on ensuring that the customers across Sri Lanka can enjoy a caf\u00e9 experience that meets the highest international standards. This commitment continues to guide our expansion into new communities and tourism destinations, development of our service standards and creation of welcoming spaces for both local customers and international travellers.\n\nBy being present across key regions of the country, we have become part of the journey for many visitors exploring Sri Lanka. Our aim is to provide a consistent and memorable experience that contributes positively to their overall impression of the country."
  },
