    "md5": "e5a95214b106ac4641cafa5fecdf585e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1918,
    "chunk_text": "For businesses, the introduction of this framework creates a new pathway to resolve commercial disputes in a manner that is confidential, collaborative and focused on achieving practical outcomes. Unlike traditional dispute resolution processes that can often result in prolonged proceedings, mediation enables parties to engage directly, explore mutually acceptable solutions and preserve important commercial relationships that may otherwise be affected by conflict.\n\nBeyond strengthening domestic business confidence, Sri Lanka\u2019s evolving mediation ecosystem creates an opportunity for the country to develop as a trusted destination for commercial dispute resolution. With its strategic location at the centre of Indian Ocean trade routes, strengthened legal framework and growing institutional capability, Sri Lanka is positioned to support not only domestic businesses but also cross-border commercial engagements.\n\nThe Corporate Mediation Pledge reflects growing recognition among businesses that disputes between commercial partners must be managed efficiently to minimise disruption to operations and protect long-term relationships. Through the pledge, participating companies have committed to considering mediation as part of their corporate dispute resolution approach, recognising that effective dispute management contributes to responsible corporate governance and sustainable business outcomes.\n\nThe initiative aligns with a growing global movement towards mediation as a preferred mechanism for commercial dispute resolution. Internationally, businesses and institutions have increasingly adopted mediation due to its ability to provide flexible, confidential and relationship-focused solutions while reducing the costs and delays associated with prolonged disputes.\n\nThe Corporate Mediation Pledge Ceremony was supported by The Asia Foundation, with Colombo Port City serving as the venue partner."
