    "md5": "0c507824074c5a7490b85c7709600119",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1838,
    "chunk_text": "PickMe launches Colombo Connect first city-wide destination\n\nChief Guest Governor Hanif Yusoof purchasing the first ticket for Colombo Connect Lotus Tower on PickMe Explore as PickMe CEO Jiffry Zulfer and Colombo Lotus Tower Chairman Shirantha Peries look on\n\nFrom left: Digital Economy Ministry Secretary Waruna Sri Dhanapala, Colombo Lotus Tower Chairman Shirantha Peries, Travel writer, photojournalist and author Juliet Coombe and PickMe CEO Jiffry Zulfer\n\nLotus Tower becomes first destination connected to a city-wide digital ecosystem linking Colombo\u2019s attractions, culture, entertainment and commerce\n\nPickMe on Wednesday launched Colombo Connect, the first city-wide destination to be introduced under its newly unveiled PickMe Explore platform, a national digital ecosystem designed to connect attractions, experiences, events and communities through a single technology platform.\n\nThe initiative was launched at Colombo Lotus Tower, with Western Province Governor Hanif Yusoof attending as Chief Guest. Also in attendance were Digital Economy Ministry Secretary Waruna Sri Dhanapala, Colombo Lotus Tower Chairman Shirantha Peries, travel writer, photojournalist and author Juliet Coombe, along with several other distinguished guests and members of the management teams of PickMe and Colombo Lotus Tower.\n\nA partnership with Colombo Lotus Tower, the first destination to join the Colombo Connect ecosystem, the initiative aims to transform how residents and visitors experience the capital by digitally linking attractions, restaurants, entertainment, retail, culture and mobility into one seamless journey. The company estimates that once fully developed, the ecosystem could generate more than Rs. 30 billion annually in economic activity by encouraging visitors to discover more of Colombo and spend more time in the city."
  },
