    "language": "en",
    "md5": "833091cfc89aaf72d39e3bb4d34decd1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 810,
    "chunk_text": "Real-time analytics: Using integrated data streams to monitor trends and evaluate interventions.\n\nLearning networks: Sharing insights and lessons to improve institutional capacity.\n\nThese mechanisms embed continuous learning and agility within governance structures.\n\nBy doing so, the country can anticipate risks, align national and local policies, improve service delivery, and strengthen public trust.\n\nThe era of static policies is over. The future belongs to governments that learn, adapt, and anticipate. Adaptive policy frameworks combined with strategic foresight create resilient, responsive, and future-ready governance. For Sri Lanka, embracing this approach is not just a reform\u2014it is a strategic necessity.\n\n(The author is a Governance and Policy Specialist and a former Secretary to Ministries)"
  },
