    "chunk_text": "Unrest at New Magazine Prison leaves 11 inmates injured\n\nColombo, Aug. 7 (Daily Mirror) - Eleven inmates were injured after unrest broke out at New Magazine Prison close to midnight yesterday, prompting prison authorities to bring the situation under control with the assistance of the Sri Lanka Police and the Police Special Task Force (STF).\n\nPrisons Spokesperson A.C. Gajanayake said a group of inmates became disorderly during the incident, which was contained by prison officials with support from the police and STF.\n\nFollowing the disturbance, security at the prison was strengthened with the deployment of the Sri Lanka Police, the Police Special Task Force, and the armed forces.\n\nThe injured inmates were admitted to the prison hospital for treatment, while nine inmates were transferred to another prison facility."
