    "md5": "772b2b90595ce4e4d77d0a0ac6758d80",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1913,
    "chunk_text": "Bravo Mr. President but please address the reality of your people too\n\nIn a span of over one and a half years in office, you have lived up to your word and a kept a key election pledge that those who were embroiled in corruption in the previous governments would be taken to task and justice would be served to the people of this nation.\n\nSome key political figures are now in jail while some others are facing allegations in front of the Bribery and Corruption Commission. You did not consider their position seniority or even their power, but instead you did what you pledged.\n\nWhile the opposition is crying foul stating that this is a political witch hunt, your decision remains firm in serving justice to the 22 million people of this nation who voted you in with much hope and encouragement that you would bring in a system change.\n\nTrust me, as a journalist myself, it was quite frustrating and painful to see my country suffer and see my fellow countrymen queue up for their basic essentials such as medicines, fuel or even food. And worse, the shame we all faced when our own government declared bankruptcy was nothing short of an embarrassment. Was it our fault that led to this? Definitely not. It was years and years of mismanagement by the very people we voted in to power and who we believed in, to transform our nation into an international financial hub, with a steady economy, a strong currency, a better education system, stronger employment opportunities and a better living standard for our children.\n\nThese pledges just remained words by the previous governments. Instead some politicians who were voted into power converted politics into business with their own commissions and deals and easy access to state funds for their personal use. Finally, as a nation we suffered as we ran out of money and essentials. The world focused on us as a country who was starving while some even pitied us."
  },
