    "md5": "819becc4a20b16b1c39f2c2f4049447f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1359,
    "chunk_text": "These pledges just remained words by the previous governments. Instead some politicians who were voted into power converted politics into business with their own commissions and deals and easy access to state funds for their personal use. Finally, as a nation we suffered as we ran out of money and essentials. The world focused on us as a country who was starving while some even pitied us.\n\nThe cost of living is still soaring and people are unable to meet their basics. With the income levels of the common man still very low, what relief are these people getting? Many families in the most poorest parts of the country are surviving on barely one meal a day. In some areas even access to clean water remains a challenge.\n\nFarmers have begun island wide protests urging your government to announce a guaranteed minimum price on paddy and reductions in the prices of fertilizer. They say the present proposed price by the government is still not sufficient and some mill owners do not purchase at the quoted rate. It was of course a welcome sight to see your Agriculture Minister K.D. Lal Kantha assuring that the government would blacklist the mill owners who do not adhere to the government rate but considering the present crisis it may be advisable to sit with the farmers and thrash out the issues. As a blow to our rice will be a blow to our stomachs."
